{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba poc/ui/src/idea/composite.js | sed -n '15,55p;177,242p'; nl -ba poc/ui/src/idea/idea.js | sed -n '120,165p'; rg -n 'binary|yesno|yesNo|yes/no' poc/ui/src --glob '\"'!*.json'\"' | head -100; ls scripts | rg 'page|release|library|serve|export'\"","aggregated_output":"    15\t}\n    16\t\n    17\tfunction numericScore(thesis, position) {\n    18\t  const value = score(thesis, position);\n    19\t  if (!['+2', '+1', '0', '−1', '−2', 'Yes', 'No'].includes(value))\n    20\t    throw new TypeError('Unsupported composite input score');\n    21\t  return value === 'Yes' ? 2 : value === 'No' ? -2 : Number(value.replace('−', '-'));\n    22\t}\n    23\t\n    24\t/** Apply one fixed basket to the dated assessments, preserving missing values and coverage. */\n    25\tfunction history(drivers, dataset, asOf, weighted = false) {\n    26\t  const byId = new Map(dataset.theses.map((thesis) => [thesis.id, thesis]));\n    27\t  const start = dataset.days[0] || asOf;\n    28\t  const dates = new Set([start, asOf]);\n    29\t  for (const driver of drivers)\n    30\t    for (const judgement of byId.get(driver.thesis_id).judgements)\n    31\t      if (judgement.day >= start && judgement.day <= asOf) dates.add(judgement.day);\n    32\t  const series = [...dates].sort().map((day) => {\n    33\t    const contributions = drivers.map((driver) => {\n    34\t      const thesis = byId.get(driver.thesis_id);\n    35\t      const judgement = assessmentAt(thesis, day);\n    36\t      const raw = judgement ? numericScore(thesis, judgement.rung) : null;\n    37\t      return { ...driver, score: raw, signed: raw === null ? null : raw * driver.direction };\n    38\t    });\n    39\t    const active = contributions.filter((entry) => entry.signed !== null);\n    40\t    const sum = active.reduce(\n    41\t      (total, entry) => total + entry.signed * (weighted ? entry.weight_percent / 100 : 1),\n    42\t      0,\n    43\t    );\n    44\t    for (const entry of contributions)\n    45\t      entry.contribution =\n    46\t        entry.signed === null\n    47\t          ? null\n    48\t          : entry.signed * (weighted ? entry.weight_percent / 100 : 1 / active.length);\n    49\t    return {\n    50\t      day,\n    51\t      value: weighted\n    52\t        ? drivers.length && active.length === drivers.length\n    53\t          ? sum\n    54\t          : null\n    55\t        : active.length\n   177\t    throw new TypeError('Every connected thesis needs a composite disposition');\n   178\t  if (\n   179\t    weighted &&\n   180\t    drivers.reduce((total, driver) => total + driver.weight_percent, 0) !==\n   181\t      (drivers.length ? 100 : 0)\n   182\t  )\n   183\t    throw new TypeError('Idea impact weights must sum to 100');\n   184\t  return { ...plan, excluded, drivers, ...history(drivers, dataset, plan.as_of, weighted) };\n   185\t}\n   186\t\n   187\t/** An explicit trial basket; directions and representative selection are never inferred here. */\n   188\texport function prepareCompositeTrial(trials, card, dataset) {\n   189\t  const matching = trials.filter(\n   190\t    (trial) => trial.idea_text === card.idea.text && trial.as_of === card.idea.as_of,\n   191\t  );\n   192\t  if (!matching.length) return null;\n   193\t  if (matching.length !== 1)\n   194\t    throw new TypeError('A response needs exactly one matching composite trial');\n   195\t  const plan = matching[0];\n   196\t  shape(plan, ['version', 'idea_text', 'as_of', 'note', 'drivers'], 'composite trial');\n   197\t  if (\n   198\t    plan.version !== 'idea-composite/1' ||\n   199\t    !isCalendarDay(plan.as_of) ||\n   200\t    plan.as_of !== dataset.as_of ||\n   201\t    typeof plan.note !== 'string' ||\n   202\t    !Array.isArray(plan.drivers) ||\n   203\t    !plan.drivers.length\n   204\t  )\n   205\t    throw new TypeError('Invalid composite trial');\n   206\t  const selected = new Set((card.reading?.chosen || []).map((entry) => entry.view_id));\n   207\t  if (plan.drivers.some((driver) => !selected.has(driver.thesis_id))) return null;\n   208\t  const used = new Set();\n   209\t  const byId = new Map(dataset.theses.map((thesis) => [thesis.id, thesis]));\n   210\t  const drivers = plan.drivers.map((driver) => {\n   211\t    shape(driver, ['thesis_id', 'question', 'label', 'direction', 'reason'], 'composite driver');\n   212\t    const thesis = byId.get(driver.thesis_id);\n   213\t    if (\n   214\t      !thesis ||\n   215\t      thesis.question !== driver.question ||\n   216\t      !selected.has(thesis.id) ||\n   217\t      used.has(thesis.id)\n   218\t    )\n   219\t      throw new TypeError('A composite driver must identify one unique connected thesis');\n   220\t    if (undirected(thesis))\n   221\t      throw new CompositeUnavailable(\n   222\t        `No composite: ${thesis.id} states no direction for the company`,\n   223\t      );\n   224\t    if (\n   225\t      ![1, -1].includes(driver.direction) ||\n   226\t      ![driver.label, driver.reason].every((text) => typeof text === 'string' && text.trim())\n   227\t    )\n   228\t      throw new TypeError('A composite driver needs an explicit direction and explanation');\n   229\t    used.add(thesis.id);\n   230\t    return { ...driver };\n   231\t  });\n   232\t  return {\n   233\t    ...plan,\n   234\t    drivers,\n   235\t    ...history(drivers, dataset, plan.as_of),\n   236\t    excluded: [...selected].filter((id) => !used.has(id)),\n   237\t  };\n   238\t}\n   239\t\n   240\texport function compositeAt(trial, day) {\n   241\t  return (\n   242\t    trial.series.findLast((point) => point.day <= day) || {\n   120\t  return `$${value}`;\n   121\t}\n   122\t\n   123\t/** What the card's chip and status line say, from the service's answer alone (no DOM). `scoreOf(position)`\n   124\t * renders a ladder position the way the thesis cards do (+2 … −2) when the thesis is loaded. */\n   125\texport function statusOf(card, scoreOf = (position) => `position ${position}`) {\n   126\t  if (card.no_recorded_view)\n   127\t    return {\n   128\t      badge: 'No thesis',\n   129\t      cls: 'chip--line',\n   130\t      line: 'No recorded view on anything in this idea.',\n   131\t      summary: '',\n   132\t    };\n   133\t  const chosen = card.reading?.chosen || [];\n   134\t  const summary = esc(card.reading.summary);\n   135\t  if (!chosen.length) return { badge: 'No thesis', cls: 'chip--line', line: '', summary };\n   136\t  const e = card.evaluation;\n   137\t  if (e && e.evaluable !== false && e.verdict && VERDICT[e.verdict]) {\n   138\t    const claim = `${e.comparator} ${fmtUsd(e.value_usd)}`;\n   139\t    const at = e.claim_position ? ` at ${scoreOf(e.claim_position)}` : '';\n   140\t    return {\n   141\t      badge: VERDICT[e.verdict],\n   142\t      cls: e.verdict === 'holds' ? 'chip--ink' : 'chip--line',\n   143\t      line: `Your claim <b>${esc(claim)}</b>${esc(at)} ${SEP} Judged <b>${esc(scoreOf(e.judged_position))}</b> ${esc(e.judged_label || '')}`,\n   144\t      summary,\n   145\t    };\n   146\t  }\n   147\t  return {\n   148\t    badge: `${chosen.length} ${chosen.length === 1 ? 'thesis' : 'theses'}`,\n   149\t    cls: 'chip--line',\n   150\t    line: '',\n   151\t    summary,\n   152\t  };\n   153\t}\n   154\t\n   155\t/** The card element the canvas leads with. `state` is one of pending, answered, failed. */\n   156\texport function ideaCard({\n   157\t  text,\n   158\t  state,\n   159\t  card,\n   160\t  error,\n   161\t  scoreOf,\n   162\t  onOpen,\n   163\t  composite,\n   164\t  compositeNote = '',\n   165\t  day,\npoc/ui/src/model/thesis.js:20:/** What a state shows: a yes/no ladder or an undirected one names its own outcome or range once; a five-rung ladder shows its score and label. */\npoc/ui/src/adapters/bundle.js:62:    // a yes/no ladder may list No first: each rung shows its own outcome; other two-rung labels keep their order\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10989,11006p;11827,11846p'; nl -ba poc/ui/verify-page.mjs | head -55; nl -ba src/hivemind/vocabulary.py | sed -n '12,52p'; rg -n 'apiBase|localhost:8788|127.0.0.1:8788|apiOrigin' poc/ui/src\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '10989,11006p;11827,11846p'; nl -ba poc/ui/verify-page.mjs | head -55; nl -ba src/hivemind/vocabulary.py | sed -n '12,52p'; rg -n 'apiBase|localhost:8788|127.0.0.1:8788|apiOrigin' poc/ui/src\"","aggregated_output":" 10989\t- **Not done:** nothing built, sent or changed.\n 10990\t\n 10991\t## D726 · 2026-11-22 · Alex opens a judge version for related number questions ($0 gate first) and agrees to \"Forecast unavailable\" as the first-release interim\n 10992\t\n 10993\t- **The questions** (after D725):\n 10994\t  - \"要不要开一个新的判官版本来试修法（相关的题合在一次里算，每个数字标明出处，程序检查算术和出处）？\" Options: 开，先做 0 元那一关\n 10995\t    (recommended: the format and checks designed and through the council, then the $0 gate on five stored cases, four gold controls and\n 10996\t    three planted errors; the paid gate asks Alex for its ceiling); 先不开.\n 10997\t  - \"第一版上线前的过渡：数字题只显示问题和来源，档位和预测文字写成'预测暂缺'，等通过检查再放出来。你同意这个做法吗？\" Options: 同意\n 10998\t    (recommended); 暂不定.\n 10999\t- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-22): \"开，先做 0 元那一关 (推荐)\"; \"同意 (推荐)\".\n 11000\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 11001\t  - A new judge version is opened for the bounded test of D725: related number questions judged together, with labelled figures and\n 11002\t    code checks of identity and arithmetic. It is designed and reviewed at $0, then the $0 gate runs. The paid gate needs Alex's\n 11003\t    ceiling.\n 11004\t  - Until the number answers pass, a first release shows number questions with their sources and \"Forecast unavailable\": the band, the\n 11005\t    forecast text and its history withheld together. It is built with the release work, which is not started.\n 11006\t- poc-v118 stays the product.\n 11827\t    - \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线 (推荐)\": the council's consensus;\n 11828\t    - \"换更强的模型再小测一次\": a stronger model or higher effort, with a small paid probe and a cap Alex names;\n 11829\t    - \"先停，我想谈谈\".\n 11830\t- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-23): \"结束这条线，预测暂缺上线 (推荐)\".\n 11831\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 11832\t  - The v13s judge line ends at its STOP. Nothing from it enters the product, and poc-v118 stays the product (D690).\n 11833\t  - The first release carries D726: number questions show the question and its sources with \"Forecast unavailable\", the band, the\n 11834\t    forecast text and the history withheld together.\n 11835\t  - The one next step, when release work opens, is a $0 check of the reader's screen on a stored number question that has a\n 11836\t    forecast and history: only the question, its sources and \"Forecast unavailable\" appear.\n 11837\t- **Kept for the record, not built:**\n 11838\t  - the D725 consistency finding (separate answers contradicted each other in 8 of 9 pairs, joint answers in none);\n 11839\t  - the open checker defects in `PAID-V13S-RESULT.md` §5;\n 11840\t  - the v13s request and harness in `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/`.\n     1\t/** Generate a browser fixture for instance isolation and host-driven updates. */\n     2\timport fs from 'node:fs/promises';\n     3\t\n     4\tconst page = await fs.readFile(new URL('../mock/index.html', import.meta.url), 'utf8');\n     5\tconst css = page.match(/<style>([\\s\\S]*?)<\\/style>/)[1];\n     6\tconst data = page.match(/<script id=\"data\" type=\"application\\/json\">([\\s\\S]*?)<\\/script>/)[1];\n     7\tconst script = page.slice(page.lastIndexOf('<script>') + 8, page.lastIndexOf('</script>'));\n     8\tconst fixture = `<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../../../web/design-system/fonts-embedded.css\"><style>${css}\n     9\tbody { margin:20px; background:var(--paper);font-family:var(--sans); } .hosts {display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px;} .host {height:540px;border:1px solid var(--rule);margin-top:16px;} .test-actions {display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;} .test-actions button {padding:10px;}</style></head><body class=\"hm-ui\"><h1>Thesis component verification</h1><div class=\"test-actions\"><button id=\"open-first\">Open first</button><button id=\"open-second\">Open second</button><button id=\"empty-history\">Open before first assessment</button><button id=\"invalid\">Reject invalid update</button><button id=\"destroy\">Destroy first</button><button id=\"recreate\">Recreate first</button></div><p id=\"result\" role=\"status\">Ready</p><div class=\"hosts\"><div class=\"host\" id=\"first\"></div><div class=\"host\" id=\"second\"></div></div><script id=\"fixture-data\" type=\"application/json\">${data}</script><script>${script}</script><script>\n    10\tconst dataset=JSON.parse(document.querySelector('#fixture-data').textContent);\n    11\tconst primary=dataset.theses.find(t=>t.id==='v3') || dataset.theses[0];\n    12\tlet first=Hivemind.createThesisExplorer(document.querySelector('#first'),{dataset});\n    13\tconst second=Hivemind.createThesisExplorer(document.querySelector('#second'),{dataset});\n    14\tfirst.showGraph({primaryId:primary.id});second.showGraph({primaryId:dataset.theses[0].id});\n    15\tconst result=document.querySelector('#result');\n    16\tdocument.querySelector('#open-first').onclick=()=>first.openThesis(primary.id);\n    17\tdocument.querySelector('#open-second').onclick=()=>second.openThesis(dataset.theses[0].id);\n    18\tdocument.querySelector('#empty-history').onclick=()=>first.openThesis(dataset.theses.find(t=>t.judgements[0]?.day>dataset.days[0]).id,dataset.days[0]);\n    19\tdocument.querySelector('#invalid').onclick=()=>{const bad=structuredClone(dataset);bad.theses[0].id=bad.theses[1].id;try{first.setDataset(bad);result.textContent='ERROR: accepted invalid data';}catch(error){result.textContent='Rejected: '+error.message;}};\n    20\tdocument.querySelector('#destroy').onclick=()=>{first.destroy();result.textContent='First destroyed; second remains mounted';};\n    21\tdocument.querySelector('#recreate').onclick=()=>{first.destroy();first=Hivemind.createThesisExplorer(document.querySelector('#first'),{dataset});first.showGraph({primaryId:primary.id});result.textContent='First recreated';};\n    22\tconst motionCheck=document.createElement('button');motionCheck.textContent='Check drawer motion';document.querySelector('.test-actions').append(motionCheck);\n    23\tmotionCheck.onclick=async()=>{\n    24\t  const passed=[];\n    25\t  const check=(condition,label)=>{if(!condition)throw new Error(label);passed.push(label);};\n    26\t  const frame=()=>new Promise(resolve=>requestAnimationFrame(resolve));\n    27\t  const wait=async(ms)=>{const start=performance.now();while(performance.now()-start<ms)await frame();};\n    28\t  const sheet=()=>document.querySelector('#first .sheet');\n    29\t  const panel=()=>document.querySelector('#first .sheet__panel');\n    30\t  const close=()=>document.querySelector('#first .sheet-close').click();\n    31\t  try{\n    32\t    motionCheck.focus();first.openThesis(primary.id);await wait(65);\n    33\t    const entering=panel().getBoundingClientRect();\n    34\t    check(!sheet().hidden&&entering.right>innerWidth&&entering.left<innerWidth,'opening has an intermediate slide frame');\n    35\t    await wait(300);check(Math.abs(panel().getBoundingClientRect().right-innerWidth)<1,'opening reaches the screen edge');\n    36\t    close();await wait(65);check(!sheet().hidden&&panel().getBoundingClientRect().right>innerWidth,'closing remains visible while sliding');\n    37\t    await wait(300);check(sheet().hidden&&document.activeElement===motionCheck,'closing hides and restores focus after exit');\n    38\t    first.openThesis(primary.id);await wait(80);close();await wait(60);first.openThesis(primary.id);await wait(350);\n    39\t    check(!sheet().hidden&&sheet().classList.contains('is-open')&&!sheet().classList.contains('is-transitioning'),'a reversed close finishes open');\n    40\t    close();first.setDataset(dataset);await wait(320);check(sheet().hidden,'dataset replacement cancels the closing animation');\n    41\t    first.openThesis(primary.id);await wait(70);first.destroy();await wait(320);check(!document.querySelector('#first .sheet'),'destroy cancels the opening animation');\n    42\t    first=Hivemind.createThesisExplorer(document.querySelector('#first'),{dataset});first.showGraph({primaryId:primary.id});\n    43\t    result.textContent='Passed '+passed.length+' drawer checks: '+passed.join('; ');\n    44\t  }catch(error){result.textContent='FAILED: '+error.message;}\n    45\t};\n    46\t</script></body></html>`;\n    47\tawait fs.mkdir(new URL('./dist/', import.meta.url), { recursive: true });\n    48\tawait fs.writeFile(new URL('./dist/verify.html', import.meta.url), fixture);\n    49\tconsole.log('Wrote poc/ui/dist/verify.html');\n    50\t\n    51\tconst response = await fs.readFile(\n    52\t  new URL('./test/fixtures/idea-card-v3.json', import.meta.url),\n    53\t  'utf8',\n    54\t);\n    55\tconst routing = `<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>Hivemind connector verification</title><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../../../web/design-system/fonts-embedded.css\"><style>${css}\n    12\tPUSHES = ['toward_first', 'toward_last', 'none']\n    13\tDIRECTIONS = ['first_is_bullish', 'last_is_bullish', 'same', 'opposite']\n    14\tASSET_LABELS = ['Strongly bullish', 'Bullish', 'Neutral', 'Bearish', 'Strongly bearish']\n    15\tYES_NO = ['Yes', 'No']\n    16\t\n    17\tLEGACY = {\n    18\t    'kind': {'对象观点': 'asset', '主题观点': 'theme'},\n    19\t    'tier': {'发生的事': 'fact', '当事人说的': 'party_statement', '第三方看法': 'third_party_view', '传闻': 'rumour'},\n    20\t    'candidate_outcome': {'归入已有的': 'merge', '接续': 'succession', '新观点': 'new', '不开': 'skip'},\n    21\t    'evidence_outcome': {'重复': 'repeat', '替代': 'replace', '新证据': 'new'},\n    22\t    'push': {'推向第一格': 'toward_first', '推向最后一格': 'toward_last', '不推': 'none'},\n    23\t    'direction': {'对方第一格是看多': 'first_is_bullish', '对方最后一格是看多': 'last_is_bullish', '同向': 'same', '反向': 'opposite'},\n    24\t    'label': {'强烈看多': 'Strongly bullish', '看多': 'Bullish', '中性': 'Neutral', '看空': 'Bearish', '强烈看空': 'Strongly bearish', '是': 'Yes', '否': 'No'},\n    25\t}\n    26\t\n    27\t\n    28\tdef canonical(field, value):\n    29\t    \"\"\"The canonical value of a closed field: a legacy value converted, a canonical one kept, anything else unchanged.\"\"\"\n    30\t    if not isinstance(value, str):\n    31\t        return value\n    32\t    return LEGACY[field].get(value.strip(), value)\n    33\t\n    34\t\n    35\tdef legacy(field, value):\n    36\t    \"\"\"The Chinese spelling of a canonical value, for a request built for a Chinese prompt version.\"\"\"\n    37\t    for old, new in LEGACY[field].items():\n    38\t        if new == value:\n    39\t            return old\n    40\t    return value\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\tdef extraction_answer(data):\n    44\t    \"\"\"An extraction answer with canonical kind, tier and standard rung labels; other fields untouched.\"\"\"\n    45\t    out = dict(data)\n    46\t    out['candidates'] = [dict(c, kind=canonical('kind', c.get('kind')),\n    47\t                              rungs=[dict(r, label=canonical('label', r.get('label'))) for r in c.get('rungs', [])]) for c in data.get('candidates', [])]\n    48\t    out['evidence'] = [dict(e, tier=canonical('tier', e.get('tier'))) for e in data.get('evidence', [])]\n    49\t    return out\n    50\t\n    51\t\n    52\tdef candidate(c):\npoc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:20:const API = document.body.dataset.api || 'http://127.0.0.1:8788';\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONPATH=src python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,glob,json,collections\nfrom hivemind import vocabulary,service\nfrom hivemind.views import store\nfor f in sorted(glob.glob('\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-?/prod/views.sqlite'\\\\''))+glob.glob('\\\\''poc/data/sealed-2026-10-24-run3-through-0815/views.sqlite'\\\\''):\n c=sqlite3.connect('\\\\''file:'\\\\''+f+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True);c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n yn={r[0] for r in c.execute('\\\\''select view_id from views'\\\\'') if {vocabulary.canonical('\\\\''label'\\\\'',x['\\\\''label'\\\\'']) for x in store.rungs_of(c,r[0])}=={'\\\\''Yes'\\\\'','\\\\''No'\\\\''}}\n print(f);cnt=collections.Counter();examples=[]\n for j in c.execute('\\\\''select * from judgements'\\\\''):\n  if j['\\\\''view_id'\\\\''] not in yn: continue\n  for field in ('\\\\''theme_pushes_json'\\\\'','\\\\''cited_views_json'\\\\'','\\\\''pushes_json'\\\\''):\n   if field not in j.keys(): continue\n   data=json.loads(j[field] or '\\\\''[]'\\\\'')\n   if not data: continue\n   if field=='\\\\''pushes_json'\\\\'': continue\n   vals=[v for v in data if (str(v) if not isinstance(v,dict) else v.get('\\\\''view_id'\\\\'',v.get('\\\\''theme_view_id'\\\\''))) not in yn]\n   if vals:\n    cnt[field]+=1\n    if sum(x[0]==field for x in examples)<3: examples.append((field,j['\\\\''view_id'\\\\''],j['\\\\''judgement_id'\\\\''],vals,j['\\\\''reasons'\\\\''][:550]))\n print(cnt,*examples,sep='\\\\''\\\\n'\\\\'')\n if '\\\\''old-1'\\\\'' in f:\n  print('\\\\''v8 switches'\\\\'',[tuple(x) for x in c.execute(\\\"select open, reason from view_switches where view_id='\\\\''v8'\\\\''\\\")], '\\\\''judgements,changed'\\\\'', tuple(c.execute(\\\"select count(*),sum(changed) from judgements where view_id='\\\\''v8'\\\\''\\\").fetchone()))\n print('\\\\''closed number'\\\\'',[(r[0],r[1]) for r in c.execute(\\\"select view_id,reason from view_switches where open=0\\\") if r[0] not in yn][:5])'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONPATH=src python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,glob,json,collections\nfrom hivemind import vocabulary,service\nfrom hivemind.views import store\nfor f in sorted(glob.glob('\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-?/prod/views.sqlite'\\\\''))+glob.glob('\\\\''poc/data/sealed-2026-10-24-run3-through-0815/views.sqlite'\\\\''):\n c=sqlite3.connect('\\\\''file:'\\\\''+f+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True);c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n yn={r[0] for r in c.execute('\\\\''select view_id from views'\\\\'') if {vocabulary.canonical('\\\\''label'\\\\'',x['\\\\''label'\\\\'']) for x in store.rungs_of(c,r[0])}=={'\\\\''Yes'\\\\'','\\\\''No'\\\\''}}\n print(f);cnt=collections.Counter();examples=[]\n for j in c.execute('\\\\''select * from judgements'\\\\''):\n  if j['\\\\''view_id'\\\\''] not in yn: continue\n  for field in ('\\\\''theme_pushes_json'\\\\'','\\\\''cited_views_json'\\\\'','\\\\''pushes_json'\\\\''):\n   if field not in j.keys(): continue\n   data=json.loads(j[field] or '\\\\''[]'\\\\'')\n   if not data: continue\n   if field=='\\\\''pushes_json'\\\\'': continue\n   vals=[v for v in data if (str(v) if not isinstance(v,dict) else v.get('\\\\''view_id'\\\\'',v.get('\\\\''theme_view_id'\\\\''))) not in yn]\n   if vals:\n    cnt[field]+=1\n    if sum(x[0]==field for x in examples)<3: examples.append((field,j['\\\\''view_id'\\\\''],j['\\\\''judgement_id'\\\\''],vals,j['\\\\''reasons'\\\\''][:550]))\n print(cnt,*examples,sep='\\\\''\\\\n'\\\\'')\n if '\\\\''old-1'\\\\'' in f:\n  print('\\\\''v8 switches'\\\\'',[tuple(x) for x in c.execute(\\\"select open, reason from view_switches where view_id='\\\\''v8'\\\\''\\\")], '\\\\''judgements,changed'\\\\'', tuple(c.execute(\\\"select count(*),sum(changed) from judgements where view_id='\\\\''v8'\\\\''\\\").fetchone()))\n print('\\\\''closed number'\\\\'',[(r[0],r[1]) for r in c.execute(\\\"select view_id,reason from view_switches where open=0\\\") if r[0] not in yn][:5])'\"","aggregated_output":"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite\nCounter({'theme_pushes_json': 314})\n('theme_pushes_json', 'v3', 16, [{'view_id': 'v6', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v7', 'push': 'toward_first'}], 'The supplied reference is the December 31, 2026 deadline; no market consensus or company shipping guidance is provided. That cutoff separates rung 1 (shipping by the date) from rung 2 (not shipping by then). The full-production report and its specific expectation of possible 2026 shipments, reinforced by the report that DSX factories are hosting Rubin infrastructure, make a start by the cutoff more likely. The hosting report is undated and neither item establishes that shipments have already begun, but the question asks for the most likely outc')\n('theme_pushes_json', 'v3', 21, [{'view_id': 'v6', 'push': 'toward_first'}], \"The available reference is NVIDIA's reported schedule for Rubin systems to begin shipping in fall 2026, which sits at rung 1; no separate consensus is supplied. That schedule, alongside the report that the systems are in full production, makes a start before the December 31 cutoff most likely. The reported Kyber delay concerns Rubin Ultra, while the possible NVL576 delay or limited volume concerns a larger system; neither establishes that the Rubin platform will not begin shipping. NVIDIA's statement that its roadmap is intact is consistent wit\")\n('theme_pushes_json', 'v3', 27, [{'view_id': 'v6', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v7', 'push': 'toward_first'}], \"The reference is NVIDIA's reported schedule for Rubin systems to begin shipping in fall 2026, which sits at rung 1; a more specific third-party report puts first shipments in Q3, also rung 1. Full production and the Q3/fall shipment reports make a start by year-end the most likely outcome. The delay reports concern Kyber, Rubin Ultra configurations, or NVL576, rather than establishing that the Rubin platform as a whole will miss its first shipment. The generic delay report gives no revised date, and NVIDIA said its roadmap remains intact. The n\")\nv8 switches [(1, 'created')] judgements,changed (75, 69)\nclosed number []\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite\nCounter({'theme_pushes_json': 208})\n('theme_pushes_json', 'v4', 12, [{'view_id': 'v5', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v6', 'push': 'toward_first'}], \"The forecast is that NVIDIA begins shipping Vera Rubin by 2026-12-31. Full production and the report that it could begin shipping later in 2026 support a 2026 start; NVIDIA's statement that DSX AI factories are hosting Rubin infrastructure adds support that the platform is reaching deployment sites. Hosting is not explicit confirmation of a shipment, but together the evidence makes a 2026 start more likely than no start by the deadline.\")\n('theme_pushes_json', 'v3', 14, [{'view_id': 'v5', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'view_id': 'v6', 'push': 'toward_last'}], 'The reference is rung 1: no consensus or company guidance is supplied, and the reported status quo is negotiation rather than a signed guarantee. The specific report of active negotiations supports a plausible path to signing during the year to the deadline; the updated AI-capex outlooks add some support for the project context, but neither establishes that NVIDIA will sign. On balance, the forecast remains Yes by the deadline, crossing the binary rung boundary from the reference.')\n('theme_pushes_json', 'v4', 18, [{'view_id': 'v5', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v6', 'push': 'toward_first'}], \"The reference is NVIDIA's reported schedule to begin shipping Rubin systems in fall 2026, which sits at rung 1. The forecast remains Yes: that schedule is within the deadline and is supported by full production; the factory-hosting statement and planned fall launch of a Vera Rubin CPU add support, though neither alone confirms that platform shipments have begun. No supplied evidence points to a delay beyond 2026.\")\nclosed number []\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-3/prod/views.sqlite\nCounter({'theme_pushes_json': 226})\n('theme_pushes_json', 'v2', 16, [{'view_id': 'v6', 'push': 'toward_last'}, {'view_id': 'v7', 'push': 'toward_last'}], 'The observable reference is rung 1: no signed OpenAI guarantee is reported, and no market consensus or NVIDIA commitment is supplied. That status is not itself a reason to forecast No. The specific report that NVIDIA was negotiating over the Ohio lease, together with the report that other companies adopted NVIDIA’s backstop offer, makes signing by the deadline more likely than not. The other deployment figures concern different companies and do not establish an OpenAI agreement; the evidence still does not confirm that one has been signed.')\n('theme_pushes_json', 'v5', 17, [{'view_id': 'v6', 'push': 'none'}, {'view_id': 'v7', 'push': 'none'}], 'The supplied evidence makes shipping by the deadline more likely than not: the analyst says Vera Rubin is in full production and could begin shipping later in 2026. This supports rung 1 over rung 2, though it is a qualified forecast rather than confirmation that shipments have begun. No supplied market consensus or company guidance provides an independent reference rung.')\n('theme_pushes_json', 'v5', 20, [{'view_id': 'v6', 'push': 'toward_first'}, {'view_id': 'v7', 'push': 'toward_first'}], \"The reference is NVIDIA's stated plan for a fall launch of a stand-alone CPU as part of Vera Rubin; that points to rung 1, although it is not an explicit commitment to ship the entire platform. The production report and fall launch plan make shipping by year-end more likely than not, so the forecast remains on rung 1 rather than moving to rung 2.\")\nclosed number []\npoc/data/sealed-2026-10-24-run3-through-0815/views.sqlite\nCounter()\nclosed number []\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
