a\nsrc/hivemind/views/judging.py:216:                 + ('; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views' if themes else '') + '.')\nsrc/hivemind/views/judging.py:269:    for entry in data.get('theme_pushes', []):\nsrc/hivemind/views/judging.py:271:            errors.append(f'{entry[\"view_id\"]} is named twice in theme_pushes')\nsrc/hivemind/views/judging.py:311:                                theme_pushes_json=json.dumps(data.get('theme_pushes', []), ensure_ascii=False),\npoc/reports/2026-10-26-theme-block/resend-three.txt:11:theme_pushes: [{\"view_id\": \"v1\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"view_id\": \"v2\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"view_id\": \"v28\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"view_id\": \"v35\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"}, {\"view_id\": \"v39\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}]\npoc/reports/2026-10-26-theme-block/resend-three.txt:24:theme_pushes: [{\"view_id\": \"v1\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"view_id\": \"v28\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"view_id\": \"v39\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}]\npoc/reports/2026-10-26-theme-block/resend-three.txt:37:theme_pushes: [{\"view_id\": \"v1\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"view_id\": \"v2\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"view_id\": \"v39\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}]\npoc/reports/2026-10-25-grouping-repair-01/baseline/src/hivemind/prompts/idea-v4.txt:1:You read an investor's idea against Hivemind, a library of research views. A view is a dated question about one company or theme with a five-step ladder of outcomes (position 1 the most bullish, position 5 the least) and the position the library currently judges true from the evidence to date. Views are written in Chinese; you answer in English and copy view ids exactly.\n   247\t      } finally {\n   248\t        if (mine === requestNumber) {\n   249\t          inFlight = null;\n   250\t          updateSendState();\n   251\t        }\n   252\t      }\n   253\t    }\n   254\t    async function loadLibrary() {\n   255\t      try {\n   256\t        const response = await fetch(`${API}/library`, { signal: libraryRequest.signal });\n   257\t        if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`Service returned ${response.status}`);\n   258\t        const next = fromBundles(await response.json());\n   259\t        if (next.coverage !== 'library')\n   260\t          throw new Error('The service did not return a complete library');\n   261\t        if (libraryRequest.signal.aborted) return;\n   262\t        library.setDataset(next, { day: next.as_of }); // the supplied snapshot defines the displayed date (thesis-ui.md)\n   263\t        data = next;\n   264\t      } catch {\n   265\t        // Keep the displayed snapshot when the optional live read is unavailable.\n   266\t      }\n   267\t    }\n   268\t    form.addEventListener('submit', run);\n   269\t    input.addEventListener('input', updateSendState);\n   270\t    libraryButton.addEventListener('click', showLibrary);\n   271\t    ideaButton.addEventListener('click', showIdea);\n   272\t    window.addEventListener(\n   273\t      'pagehide',\n   274\t      () => {\n   275\t        cancelIdea();\n   276\t        libraryRequest.abort();\n   277\t        library.destroy();\n   278\t        app?.destroy();\n   279\t        ideaDetail.destroy();\n     1\t\"\"\"Translate the mock's data (poc/mock/data.json, written by the pipeline in Chinese) into English for the\n     2\tfront-end mock, with gpt-6-luna through the same archived model call as the pipeline (a repeated run costs $0).\n     3\t\n     4\tEnumerations are mapped, not translated (tiers, view kinds, object ladder labels, judgement pushes). Everything\n     5\telse that the page shows is translated in batches: view questions and what they look at, ladder conditions,\n     6\tevidence one-liners and event times, each judgement's reasons and why-changed. Quotes, speakers, titles and dates\n     7\tstay as stored (quotes are the source's own words, almost all English). The Chinese ladder conditions are kept\n     8\tas `condition_zh` because the page reads the rung thresholds from them.\n     9\t\n    10\tUsage: python3 scripts/mock_translate.py [--dry] [--limit N]   → poc/mock/data.en.json\n    11\t\"\"\"\n    12\timport argparse\n    13\timport collections\n    14\timport glob\n    15\timport json\n    16\timport os\n    17\timport re\n    18\timport sys\n    19\t\n    20\tROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))\n    21\tsys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(ROOT, 'src'))\n    22\tfrom hivemind import config, model  # noqa: E402\n    23\t\n    24\tTIERS = {'发生的事': 'Fact', '当事人说的': 'Party statement', '第三方看法': 'Third-party view', '传闻': 'Rumour'}\n    25\tKINDS = {'对象观点': 'Company view', '主题观点': 'Theme view'}\n    26\tOBJECT_LABELS = {'强烈看多': 'Strongly bullish', '看多': 'Bullish', '中性': 'Neutral', '看空': 'Bearish', '强烈看空': 'Strongly bearish', '是': 'Yes', '否': 'No'}\n    27\tPUSHES = {'推向第一格': 'pushes toward rung 1', '推向最后一格': 'pushes toward rung 5', '不推': 'no push', '定格': 'settles the rung'}\n    28\tSCHEMA = {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['items'],\n    29\t          'properties': {'items': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['k', 'en'],\n    30\t                                                             'properties': {'k': {'type': 'string'}, 'en': {'type': 'string'}}}}}}\n    31\tSYSTEM = ('You translate short Chinese texts from an equity-research system into concise, natural financial English. '\n    32\t          'Keep every number, unit, ticker, company and product name, fiscal label (FY2027, Q1, H2) and date exactly as given. '\n    33\t          'Write 第 N 格 as \"rung N\" and 梯子 as \"ladder\"; 观点 is \"view\", 证据 is \"evidence\", 发生的事 is \"a fact\", 当事人说的 is \"a party statement\", '\n    34\t          '第三方看法 is \"a third-party view\", 传闻 is \"a rumour\". Translate questions as questions. Return one English text per key, every key, nothing else.')\n    35\tBATCH_CHARS = 5000\n    36\t\n    37\t\n    38\tdef collect(data):\n    39\t    \"\"\"Every distinct string the page shows, keyed by a stable id -> the original text.\"\"\"\n    40\t    todo = collections.OrderedDict()\n    41\t\n    42\t    def add(key, text):\n    43\t        if text and text.strip():\n    44\t            todo[key] = text\n    45\t    for v in data['views']:\n    46\t        add(f'v:{v[\"view_id\"]}:q', v['question'])\n    47\t        add(f'v:{v[\"view_id\"]}:l', v['looks_at'])\n    48\t        for r in v['rungs']:\n    49\t            add(f'v:{v[\"view_id\"]}:c{r[\"position\"]}', r['condition'])\n    50\t            if r['label'] not in OBJECT_LABELS:\n    51\t                add(f'v:{v[\"view_id\"]}:r{r[\"position\"]}', r['label'])\n    52\t        for n, j in enumerate(v['judgements']):\n    53\t            add(f'j:{v[\"view_id\"]}:{n}:why', j['why_changed'])\n    54\t            add(f'j:{v[\"view_id\"]}:{n}:reasons', j['reasons'])\n    55\t        for e in v['evidence']:\n    56\t            add(f'e:{e[\"id\"]}:line', e['one_line'])\n    57\t            add(f'e:{e[\"id\"]}:time', e['event_time'])\n    58\t    return todo\n    59\t\n    60\t\n    61\tdef batches(todo, done):\n    62\t    batch, size = [], 0\n    63\t    for key, text in todo.items():\n    64\t        if key in done:\n    65\t            continue\n    66\t        if batch and size + len(text) > BATCH_CHARS:\n    67\t            yield batch\n    68\t            batch, size = [], 0\n    69\t        batch.append((key, text))\n    70\t        size += len(text)\n    71\t    if batch:\n    72\t        yield batch\n    73\t\n    74\t\n    75\tCJK = re.compile(r'[一-鿿]')\n    76\tMONTHS = ['', 'Jan', 'Feb', 'Mar', 'Apr', 'May', 'Jun', 'Jul', 'Aug', 'Sep', 'Oct', 'Nov', 'Dec']\n    77\t\n    78\t\n    79\tdef polish(text):\n    80\t    \"\"\"Money and dates the model copied in Chinese units (\"300亿美元\", \"2026年8月26日\") written the English way; a\n    81\t    literal \"3500 hundred million\" becomes \"$350 billion\".\"\"\"\n    82\t    def yi_to_dollars(match):\n    83\t        n = float(match.group(1).replace(',', ''))\n    84\t        return f'${n / 10:g} billion'\n    85\t    text = re.sub(r'(\\d[\\d,.]*)\\s*万亿美元', lambda m: f'${float(m.group(1).replace(\",\", \"\")):g} trillion', text)\n    86\t    text = re.sub(r'(\\d[\\d,.]*)\\s*亿美元', yi_to_dollars, text)\n    87\t    text = re.sub(r'\\$?(\\d[\\d,.]*)\\s*hundred million(?: U\\.S\\. dollars| dollars)?', yi_to_dollars, text)\n    88\t    text = re.sub(r'(\\d[\\d,.]*)\\s*万亿', lambda m: f'{float(m.group(1).replace(\",\", \"\")):g} trillion', text)\n    89\t    text = re.sub(r'(\\d[\\d,.]*)\\s*亿', lambda m: f'{float(m.group(1).replace(\",\", \"\")) / 10:g} billion', text)\n    90\t    text = re.sub(r'(\\d[\\d,.]*)\\s*美元', r'$\\1', text)\n    91\t    text = re.sub(r'(\\d{4})\\s*年\\s*(\\d{1,2})\\s*月\\s*(\\d{1,2})\\s*日', lambda m: f'{MONTHS[int(m.group(2))]} {int(m.group(3))}, {m.group(1)}', text)\n    92\t    text = re.sub(r'(\\d{4})\\s*年\\s*(\\d{1,2})\\s*月', lambda m: f'{MONTHS[int(m.group(2))]} {m.group(1)}', text)\n    93\t    text = re.sub(r'(\\d{1,2})\\s*月\\s*(\\d{1,2})\\s*日', lambda m: f'{MONTHS[int(m.group(1))]} {int(m.group(2))}', text)\n    94\t    text = re.sub(r'(\\d{4})\\s*年', r'\\1', text)\n    95\t    text = re.sub(r'第\\s*([一二三四1-4])\\s*季度?', lambda m: 'Q' + str('一二三四'.find(m.group(1)) + 1 if m.group(1) in '一二三四' else m.group(1)), text)\n    96\t    text = re.sub(r'(\\d[\\d,.]*)\\s*%\\s*', r'\\1% ', text)\n    97\t    return re.sub(r'\\s{2,}', ' ', text).strip()\n    98\t\n    99\t\n   100\tFIX_SYSTEM = SYSTEM + ' The output must contain no Chinese characters at all: write money as $X billion or $X trillion (1亿 = $0.1 billion), dates as \"Aug 26, 2026\", quarters as Q1..Q4.'\n   101\t\n   102\t\n   103\tdef apply(data, done):\n   104\t    done = {k: polish(v) for k, v in done.items()}\n   105\t    out = json.loads(json.dumps(data))\n   106\t    for v in out['views']:\n   107\t        v['question'] = done.get(f'v:{v[\"view_id\"]}:q', v['question'])\n   108\t        v['looks_at'] = done.get(f'v:{v[\"view_id\"]}:l', v['looks_at'])\n   109\t        v['kind'] = KINDS.get(v['kind'], v['kind'])\n   110\t        for r in v['rungs']:\n   111\t            r['condition_zh'] = r['condition']\n   112\t            r['condition'] = done.get(f'v:{v[\"view_id\"]}:c{r[\"position\"]}', r['condition'])\n   113\t            r['label'] = OBJECT_LABELS.get(r['label'], done.get(f'v:{v[\"view_id\"]}:r{r[\"position\"]}', r['label']))\n   114\t        for n, j in enumerate(v['judgements']):\n   115\t            j['why_changed'] = done.get(f'j:{v[\"view_id\"]}:{n}:why', j['why_changed'])\n11:The theme block (D191, D195): an asset thesis is judged with every open, judged theme thesis in view and answers, in theme_pushes,\n81:    theme_item = properties['theme_pushes']['items']\n83:        properties['theme_pushes'] = {'type': 'array', 'items': dict(theme_item, properties=dict(theme_item['properties'], view_id={'type': 'string', 'enum': themes}))}\n85:        properties['theme_pushes'] = dict(properties['theme_pushes'], maxItems=0)\n103:    schema['required'].append('theme_pushes')\n104:    schema['properties']['theme_pushes'] = {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'object', 'additionalProperties': False, 'required': ['view_id', 'push'],\n216:                 + ('; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views' if themes else '') + '.')\n269:    for entry in data.get('theme_pushes', []):\n271:            errors.append(f'{entry[\"view_id\"]} is named twice in theme_pushes')\n311:                                theme_pushes_json=json.dumps(data.get('theme_pushes', []), ensure_ascii=False),\n   142\t\n   143\t\n   144\tdef is_number_question(kind, rungs, measure):\n   145\t    \"\"\"D695: an asset question with a five-rung number ladder (canonical labels, typed direction) and a measure that is not an event.\"\"\"\n   146\t    return (kind == 'asset' and len(rungs) == 5 and bool(measure) and measure not in identity.EVENT_MEASURES\n   147\t            and typed_direction(rungs) is not None and favourable_end(rungs) is not None)\n   148\t\n   149\t\n   150\tdef stored_is_number_question(conn, view_id):\n   151\t    v, key = store.view(conn, view_id), store.view_key(conn, view_id)\n   152\t    return bool(v) and is_number_question(v['kind'], store.rungs_of(conn, view_id), (key or {}).get('measure'))\n   153\t\n   154\t\n   155\tdef candidate_rungs(conn, c, outcome, target):\n   156\t    \"\"\"The candidate's rungs as the writer will store them (a successor is oriented like its predecessor).\"\"\"\n   157\t    if outcome == 'succession' and target:\n   158\t        from .writing import oriented_like\n   159\t        return oriented_like(c, store.rungs_of(conn, target), [])['rungs']\n   160\t    return c['rungs']\n   161\t\n   162\t\n   163\t# ---------- the reading graph ----------\n   164\t\n   165\tdef stored_edges(conn):\n   166\t    \"\"\"Every stored dependency at its effective target (a bound wait counts through the question it is bound to).\"\"\"\n   167\t    edges = {}\n   168\t    for (view_id,) in conn.execute('select distinct view_id from dependencies'):\n   169\t        for dep in store.dependencies_of(conn, view_id):\n   170\t            if dep['resolved_to']:\npoc/ui/src/components/thesis-detail.js:184:    <div class=\"detail-hero\"><h2 class=\"panel__title\" id=\"detailTitle\">${esc(v.question)}</h2><div class=\"detail-meta\">${latest ? badgeHtml(v, latest) : `<span class=\"chip\">${closing ? 'No data to verify' : 'Not assessed yet'}</span>`}<span class=\"detail-meta-item\">${SEP}<span>${latest ? `Last updated: ${esc(longDay(latest.day))}` : `Opens ${esc(longDay(v.created_day))}`}</span></span><span class=\"detail-meta-item\">${SEP}<span>Due: ${esc(longDay(v.due_day))}</span></span></div></div>\npoc/ui/src/model/thesis.schema.json:19:      \"minItems\": 0,\npoc/ui/src/model/thesis.schema.json:374:          \"minItems\": 2,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"agent_message","text":"I checked all 139 comparison questions and all 94 sealed questions. The sealed store uses Chinese Yes/No labels on 30 questions. I also found that `v8` is still open, so the proposed screen check would never exercise a stored closing reason."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,glob,re\nfor f in sorted(glob.glob('\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-?/prod/views.sqlite'\\\\'')):\n c=sqlite3.connect('\\\\''file:'\\\\''+f+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\n print(f)\n pat=re.compile(r'\\\\''.{0,150}(?:capex|hyperscaler|capital spending|infrastructure spending|capital expenditure).{0,200}'\\\\'',re.I)\n found=[]\n for vid,jid,day,reason,why in c.execute(\\\"select j.view_id,j.judgement_id,j.publication_day,j.reasons,j.why_changed from judgements j join view_keys k using(view_id) where k.measure in ('\\\\''event'\\\\'','\\\\''policy_event'\\\\'')\\\"):\n  for m in pat.finditer((reason or '\\\\'''\\\\'')+'\\\\'' '\\\\''+(why or '\\\\'''\\\\'')):\n   if re.search(r'\\\\''\\\\\"'$|billion|trillion|rung [345]|range|band|position [345]'\"'\\\\'',m[0],re.I):\n    found.append((vid,jid,day,m[0]))\n print(len(found));print(*found[:18],sep='\\\\''\\\\n'\\\\'')\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,glob,re\nfor f in sorted(glob.glob('\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-?/prod/views.sqlite'\\\\'')):\n c=sqlite3.connect('\\\\''file:'\\\\''+f+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True)\n print(f)\n pat=re.compile(r'\\\\''.{0,150}(?:capex|hyperscaler|capital spending|infrastructure spending|capital expenditure).{0,200}'\\\\'',re.I)\n found=[]\n for vid,jid,day,reason,why in c.execute(\\\"select j.view_id,j.judgement_id,j.publication_day,j.reasons,j.why_changed from judgements j join view_keys k using(view_id) where k.measure in ('\\\\''event'\\\\'','\\\\''policy_event'\\\\'')\\\"):\n  for m in pat.finditer((reason or '\\\\'''\\\\'')+'\\\\'' '\\\\''+(why or '\\\\'''\\\\'')):\n   if re.search(r'\\\\''\\\\\"'$|billion|trillion|rung [345]|range|band|position [345]'\"'\\\\'',m[0],re.I):\n    found.append((vid,jid,day,m[0]))\n print(len(found));print(*found[:18],sep='\\\\''\\\\n'\\\\'')\n'\"","aggregated_output":"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite\n12\n('v20', 499, '2026-08-13', 'undary to rung 1. The rung remains Yes and the reported $350 billion discussion is not a new independent confirmation. However, the updated v6 and v7 capex theme conclusions strengthen the demand backdrop supporting the same forecast; the repeated reports themselves do not change it.')\n('v25', 548, '2026-08-15', ' outlets are treated as one claim, not independent confirmation. The rung and the core $350 billion financing-report basis are unchanged. The updated hyperscaler capex conclusions add relevant support for the scale of chip demand behind the proposed financing, changing the supporting rationale without changing the forecast rung.')\n('v31', 653, '2026-08-19', 'argely restate the same plan and do not establish closing or provide a closing schedule, so the forecast remains uncertain rather than proven. The AI-capex themes modestly support project execution; the chip-export-control themes do not bear on this investment. The rung and the key supporting fact remain the same: NVIDIA announced the $1.5 billion plan,')\n('v30', 737, '2026-08-23', 'ompletion. The repeated reports add no independent closing information, and the expected chip purchases provide only modest strategic support. The AI-capex themes modestly reinforce the project context but do not change the binary forecast. The forecast remains rung 1 with the same implied $1.5 billion completion by December 31, 2026. The additional rep')\n('v17', 762, '2026-08-24', 'd NAVER’s expansion plan, do not establish that the investment has closed or that the financing condition will be met by the deadline. The broader AI-capex outlook supports the project’s prospects somewhat, but does not remove this specific closing condition. The rung and key supporting facts are unchanged: the planned $1 billion investment remains cond')\n('v10', 865, '2026-08-28', 'ta-center capex at rung 4 and 2027 capex at rung 4, strengthening the contextual support for Firmus financing and changing the supporting outlook, without changing the implied completion date.')\n('v29', 1022, '2026-09-03', 'artnership remains at the MOU stage with limited detail, plus a reported potential $125 billion backstop whose details are not final. Updated 2026–27 hyperscaler capex conclusions also strengthen the demand backdrop. These change the supporting risk and demand picture without moving the forecast across the binary rung boundary.')\n('v29', 1037, '2026-09-04', 'eing negotiated and NVIDIA cautioned that the MOUs may not lead to definitive agreements, but roughly a year remains to complete them. The updated AI-capex themes also support continuing demand for infrastructure financing. These factors leave completion by the deadline as the more likely outcome, without treating the $500 billion target as proof that a')\n('v29', 1037, '2026-09-04', 'greements are complete. The rung remains Yes, but the updated AI-capex themes add a stronger demand backdrop than the previous judgement had, changing the key support for the same forecast. Recent filings and reports reiterate that the arrangements remain MOUs or prelim')\n('v10', 1049, '2026-09-04', 'O later in 2026, makes completion by the deadline more likely than non-completion, though the reported interest is not a confirmed commitment. The AI-capex themes modestly support the commercial context, but do not establish that the investment will close. The rung and its key transaction facts are unchanged: the same report of approximately US$500 mill')\n('v31', 1060, '2026-09-04', \"nce now includes SB Energy's reported $3.2 billion first-half 2026 net loss and $139 million revenue, mostly from its legacy business. The updated AI-capex outlook also supports the project backdrop; neither changes the most likely completion outcome.\")\n('v10', 1080, '2026-09-05', 'fact remain as in the previous conclusion: the specific but unconfirmed report of about US$500 million of interest tied to a 2026 IPO. The updated AI-capex themes reinforce the commercial context but do not change the implied outcome or rung.')\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite\n4\n('v3', 175, '2026-07-20', ' The reported up-to-$500 billion is the possible full-build cost, not the size or terms of NVIDIA’s guarantee. The rung remains 2, but the updated AI-capex theme conclusion reinforces the forecast that the lease-related guarantee may proceed; it does not change the implied binary outcome or establish a guarantee amount.')\n('v31', 1024, '2026-09-01', 'y still make completion by the deadline more likely than non-completion, so the binary rung does not change. The rung remains Yes, but the updated AI-capex themes add relevant support for the scale and continuation of the data-center buildout. They do not establish that the specific $1.5 billion investment has closed or change the implied completion out')\n('v31', 1209, '2026-09-08', 'ut. The implied outcome therefore remains on the Yes side of the binary boundary. The rung and the core completion forecast are unchanged, but the AI-capex themes were updated since the prior judgement and now provide additional support for execution of the project. The specific $3 billion report is not a new supporting fact relative to the prior conclu')\n('v31', 1463, '2026-09-16', 'and project-investment figures are not themselves evidence that this specific investment has been paid. The rung remains Yes, but the updated 2027 AI-capex theme adds support for the underlying data-center build and thus for completion of the investment; the report of a $3 billion agreement is part of the existing support, not a newly established transf')\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-3/prod/views.sqlite\n5\n('v21', 468, '2026-08-11', 'reement to be signed; the evidence therefore supports Yes as the forecast, not as an already-proven outcome. The rung remains Yes, but the updated AI-capex themes reinforce the infrastructure-demand backdrop supporting the forecast. The newer $125 billion figure is an option across potential deals, not a confirmed Ohio-specific guarantee; repeated repor')\n('v36', 799, '2026-08-25', 'e past the binary rung boundary. The rung remains Yes, and the shipment-testing evidence is unchanged. The updated 2027 AI-capex theme now points to spending around $1 trillion, refreshing and strengthening the demand support for the same forecast without supplying a shipment date.')\n('v34', 945, '2026-08-30', ' or delay. Completion is still a forecast, not an established fact, and the repeated reports do not independently confirm a transfer of funds. The AI-capex themes support the project backdrop but do not establish completion. The rung and implied outcome are unchanged from the previous conclusion. The evidence reiterates the $1.5 billion plan and the pre')\n('v34', 1382, '2026-09-12', 'ot confirm that funds have transferred or clarify how it relates to the original $1.5 billion, but it strengthens the commitment case; the updated AI-capex outlook also modestly supports execution. The implied outcome remains on the Yes side of the binary boundary. The rung and implied completion outcome are unchanged, but the updated 2027 AI-capex outl')\n('v34', 1498, '2026-09-15', 'larger commitment, but its mention that SB Energy is seeking a Nasdaq listing to fund the project also leaves execution and timing unresolved. The AI-capex outlook supports the project backdrop, not proof of completion. The rung remains Yes, but e4452 adds a newly reported $3 billion investment agreement and Nasdaq-listing funding context, changing the ')\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
