ime.\\\\n- e5077 [fact; wccftech.com; original source Valve, as reported by Pierre-Loup Griffais ; from gnews:873613bcc953fd8e4f59a872 2026-09-16] Valve enabled the NVIDIA driver in SteamOS\\\\u2019s main development tree, allowing certain NVIDIA GPU generations to initialize and display an image.\\\\n    Quote: Griffais reports that Valve has now enabled the NVIDIA driver in the main SteamOS development tree, and this makes certain NVIDIA GPU generations initialize and display an image under SteamOS.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4913; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5078 [fact; finance.yahoo.com author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3f21db1f9791e20f80909da8 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported Q2 FY2027 total revenue of $96.22 billion, up 105.8% year over year.\\\\n    Quote: Q2 FY2027 revenue landed at $96.22 billion, up 105.8% year over year\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3729; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5081 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com author; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:3f21db1f9791e20f80909da8 2026-09-16] NVIDIA management guided Q3 FY2027 total revenue to $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%.\\\\n    Quote: Management then guided Q3 to $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2670; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5088 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:5c5a96c670714dee86769d87 2026-09-16] NVIDIA revenue grew 85% year over year in fiscal Q1 2027.\\\\n    Quote: In the first quarter of fiscal 2027, The company's revenue climbed 85% year-over-year (YoY).\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4170; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5089 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:5c5a96c670714dee86769d87 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported revenue of $96.2 billion in fiscal Q2 2027, up 106% year over year.\\\\n    Quote: Further, in the second quarter, its top line hit $96.2 billion. That was a 106% increase YoY.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4851; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5090 [party_statement; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:5c5a96c670714dee86769d87 2026-09-16] NVIDIA expects fiscal Q3 2027 revenue of $108 billion, which the author calculates would be more than 89% above the year-earlier quarter.\\\\n    Quote: Nvidia expects third-quarter revenue to reach $108 billion. Even at that level, the company would grow revenue by more than 89% compared with the same period a year earlier.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4047; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5092 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:5c5a96c670714dee86769d87 2026-09-16] NVIDIA has started shipping systems based on its Vera Rubin architecture.\\\\n    Quote: Nvidia has also started shipping systems based on its next-generation Vera Rubin architecture, providing another potential source of growth.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4166; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5096 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source IREN ; from gnews:3f2255dadc23c13fcdfe5ef3 2026-09-16] IREN signed a roughly US$5.50 billion, five-year partnership with NVIDIA for IREN\\\\u2019s AI cloud services platform; the item gives no signing date.\\\\n    Quote: Recently, JPMorgan analyst Richard Choe issued a rare double-upgrade on IREN after the company signed a roughly US$5.50 billion, five-year partnership with Nvidia tied to its fast-growing AI cloud services platform.\\\\n- e5097 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source IREN ; from gnews:3f2255dadc23c13fcdfe5ef3 2026-09-16] IREN has a US$3.65 billion GPU financing facility; the item does not specify its term or date.\\\\n    Quote: Among recent announcements, the US$3.65 billion GPU financing facility stands out alongside the Nvidia deal.\\\\n- e5098 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source IREN ; from gnews:3f2255dadc23c13fcdfe5ef3 2026-09-16] IREN plans to scale AI Cloud capacity to 480 MW by the end of 2026, supported by its GPU financing facility.\\\\n    Quote: It underpins IREN's goal of scaling to 480MW of AI Cloud capacity by the end of 2026, and ties directly into the same theme as the Nvidia partnership: aggressive, contract-backed expansion.\\\\n- e5099 [party_statement; benzinga.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:906d80c706aa948ee141e852 2026-09-16] Jensen Huang said roughly $400 billion of venture financing flowed into AI companies over six months, creating demand for compute and data centers.\\\\n    Quote: Huang said roughly $400 billion in venture financing flowed into AI companies over six months, creating jobs and massive demand for compute, which is subsequently driving demand for data centers.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2791; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5100 [fact; fool.com (author); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:147e79a4a1f10279da449944 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported $27.0 billion of revenue billed to Taiwan-headquartered customers in fiscal Q2 2027, 28% of quarterly revenue.\\\\n    Quote: During the fiscal second quarter of 2027 (the period ended July 26), $27.0 billion of Nvidia's revenue was billed to customers headquartered in Taiwan. That's 28% of the quarter's $96.2 billion total.\\\\n- e5101 [fact; fool.com (author); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:147e79a4a1f10279da449944 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported $8.9 billion of revenue billed to Taiwan-headquartered customers in fiscal Q2 2026, about 19% of quarterly revenue.\\\\n    Quote: A year earlier, it was $8.9 billion, or about 19%\\\\n- e5102 [fact; fool.com (author); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:147e79a4a1f10279da449944 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported about $12 billion of revenue billed to Taiwan-headquartered customers in the preceding quarter, roughly 15% of quarterly revenue.\\\\n    Quote: Three months before the latest quarter, it was about $12 billion, or roughly 15%.\\\\n- e5103 [fact; fool.com (author); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:147e79a4a1f10279da449944 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported fiscal Q2 2027 revenue billed to customers headquartered in the United States of $60.1 billion, Taiwan of $27.0 billion, China including Hong Kong of $7.9 billion, and the rest of the world of $1.3 billion.\\\\n    Quote: On that basis, the United States led the fiscal second quarter at $60.1 billion, or about 62% of revenue. Taiwan came second at $27.0 billion. China, including Hong Kong, contributed $7.9 billion, and the rest of the world combined for just $1.3 billion.\\\\n- e5104 [fact; fool.com (author); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:147e79a4a1f10279da449944 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported that customers headquartered outside the U.S. accounted for 38% of revenue in fiscal Q2 2027, versus 30% in fiscal Q2 2026.\\\\n    Quote: Altogether, customers headquartered outside the U.S. accounted for 38% of the quarter's revenue, against 30% a year earlier.\\\\n- e5105 [fact; fool.com (author); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:147e79a4a1f10279da449944 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported total revenue of $96.2 billion in fiscal Q2 2027, up 106% year over year, with about 92% from Data Center.\\\\n    Quote: Companywide revenue totaled $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year, and about 92% of it came from the data center business.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4244; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5106 [fact; fool.com (author); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:147e79a4a1f10279da449944 2026-09-16] One direct customer accounted for 16% of NVIDIA's total revenue, approximately $15 billion, in fiscal Q2 2027.\\\\n    Quote: One direct customer accounted for 16% of Nvidia's total revenue in the quarter -- about $15 billion billed to a single buyer.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2767; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5107 [fact; fool.com (author); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:147e79a4a1f10279da449944 2026-09-16] Two direct customers accounted for 23% and 16% of NVIDIA's revenue, respectively, in fiscal Q2 2026.\\\\n    Quote: In the same quarter a year earlier, two direct customers represented 23% and 16% of revenue.\\\\n- e5108 [party_statement; fool.com (author); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:147e79a4a1f10279da449944 2026-09-16] NVIDIA management forecast total revenue of $108.0 billion for fiscal Q3 2027.\\\\n    Quote: Management's forecast for the fiscal third quarter, now underway, is $108.0 billion of revenue -- and growth like that is ultimately a claim about what customers keep spending.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4855; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5110 [fact; Zacks.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:bc6926bf31d3a4d8006dce46 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported consolidated revenue of $96.2 billion in fiscal Q2 2027, up 106% year over year and 18% quarter over quarter.\\\\n    Quote: The company's consolidated revenues reached $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year and 18% quarter over quarter.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5002; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5111 [party_statement; Zacks.com; original source NVIDIA management 2026-08-26; from gnews:bc6926bf31d3a4d8006dce46 2026-09-16] NVIDIA management forecast fiscal Q3 2027 revenue of about $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, up 12% sequentially at the midpoint.\\\\n    Quote: Management projects revenues of around $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, for the fiscal third quarter of 2027, up 12% sequentially at the midpoint.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5005, e5314; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5114 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Nokia ; from gnews:3c52e58b83c308775f689177 2026-09-16] Nokia said its AI-RAN platform had advanced from evaluation to live field trials with eight global operators.\\\\n    Quote: Nokia ( NYSE:NOK ) stock is rising in early Wednesday trading, up 6% to $10.39 after the company said its artificial intelligence-powered radio access network (AI-RAN) platform is moving from evaluation to live field trials at eight global operators.\\\\n- e5115 [third_party_view; John Bromels; original source John Bromels 2026-09-16; from gnews:ea516c504dd7e1c928df6d60 2026-09-16] The author calculates that NVIDIA revenue grew 1,150% over the five years before publication.\\\\n    Quote: Over the last five years, Nvidia's revenue has grown 1,150%\\\\n- e5118 [fact; gurufocus.com; original source CoreWeave ; from gnews:7518d37391aa449621d707a1 2026-09-16] CoreWeave brought NVIDIA\\\\u2019s multi-rack Vera Rubin NVL72 platform online, connecting hundreds of Rubin GPUs; the deployment follows its June launch of a single rack.\\\\n    Quote: CoreWeave ( CRWV ) shares climbed about 3% on Wednesday trading after the AI cloud company said it had brought Nvidia's ( NVDA ) multi-rack Vera Rubin NVL72 platform online. The new deployment connects hundreds of Rubin GPUs into a unified computing cluster designed to support large-scale artificial intelligence workloads. The rollout builds on CoreWeave's June launch of a single Vera Rubin NVL72 \\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5140; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5119 [third_party_view; Zacks; original source WSTS ; from gnews:fc6c2e31b8c175953657a182 2026-09-16] WSTS forecast global semiconductor sales of $1.51 trillion in calendar 2026, up 89.9%.\\\\n    Quote: WSTS expects global semiconductor sales to grow 89.9% in 2026 to $1.51 trillion, highlighting the extraordinary strength of the current cycle.\\\\n- e5120 [third_party_view; Zacks; original source IDC ; from gnews:fc6c2e31b8c175953657a182 2026-09-16] IDC forecast semiconductor revenue growth of 52.8% in calendar 2026, driven primarily by AI infrastructure investment.\\\\n    Quote: IDC also expects exceptional growth in 2026, with semiconductor revenue rising 52.8%, driven overwhelmingly by AI infrastructure investment.\\\\n- e5121 [third_party_view; Zacks; original source Gartner ; from gnews:fc6c2e31b8c175953657a182 2026-09-16] Gartner forecast global semiconductor revenue of $1.56 trillion in calendar 2026, up 92%.\\\\n    Quote: Gartner expects semiconductor revenue to grow 92% in 2026 to $1.56 trillion.\\\\n- e5123 [third_party_view; Zacks; original source Technavio ; from gnews:fc6c2e31b8c175953657a182 2026-09-16] Technavio estimates military and aerospace semiconductor-market growth at a 6% CAGR through 2029.\\\\n    Quote: Tachnavio estimates that semiconductors used in the military and aerospace market will grow at a 6% CAGR through 2029.\\\\n- e5124 [fact; Zacks; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:fc6c2e31b8c175953657a182 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported FY2027 second-quarter revenue growth of 106% year over year and 18% sequentially; Data Center revenue was $89 billion, up 117% year over year and 18% sequentially.\\\\n    Quote: NVIDIA's second-quarter fiscal 2027 revenue surged 106% year over year and 18% sequentially, while Data Center revenue jumped 117% year over year and 18% sequentially to $89 billion.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4672, e5199; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5125 [party_statement; Zacks; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:fc6c2e31b8c175953657a182 2026-09-16] NVIDIA management said AI demand was accelerating and the infrastructure buildout was expanding across frontier AI labs, startups, open-model developers, enterprises, sovereign AI and physical AI.\\\\n    Quote: Management said AI demand is accelerating, with the buildout expanding beyond the major hyperscalers to multiple frontier AI labs, startups, the open-model ecosystem, enterprises, sovereign AI initiatives and physical AI.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3493; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5127 [party_statement; Zacks; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:fc6c2e31b8c175953657a182 2026-09-16] NVIDIA management said more than 350 factories across 30 countries were ramping the Vera Rubin platform.\\\\n    Quote: Management has said that more than 350 factories across 30 countries are ramping NVIDIA's Vera Rubin platform.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e938; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5129 [third_party_view; Zacks; original source Analysts ; from gnews:fc6c2e31b8c175953657a182 2026-09-16] Analysts forecast NVIDIA revenue growth of 88% and earnings growth of 93.5% in FY2027, followed by revenue growth of 65.5% and earnings growth of 66% in FY2028.\\\\n    Quote: Analysts currently expect revenue and earnings to grow a respective 88% and 93.5% this year followed by a respective 65.5% and 66% in the next.\\\\n- e5134 [third_party_view; trefis.com; original source trefis.com 2026-09-16; from gnews:106a61a1ef10fb3ba6adb1cd 2026-09-16] Trefis calculates NVIDIA trailing-twelve-month revenue at $302.97 billion, up 83.4% year over year; the exact twelve-month period is not specified.\\\\n    Quote: Revenue over the trailing twelve months is $302.97 billion, up 83.4% from a year earlier.\\\\n- e5136 [party_statement; trefis.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:106a61a1ef10fb3ba6adb1cd 2026-09-16] Vera Rubin shipments started in August 2026, and NVIDIA management expects the platform to account for about 20% of Data Center revenue in fiscal Q3 2027.\\\\n    Quote: Vera Rubin shipments started in August 2026, and management expects that platform to be about 20% of data center revenue in fiscal Q3 2027.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3820; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5137 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, quoted by finance.yahoo.com; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:8593bc8819641cdd48950c75 2026-09-16] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said demand for NVIDIA's products was accelerating.\\\\n    Quote: And demand is accelerating.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2869; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5138 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, quoted by finance.yahoo.com; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:8593bc8819641cdd48950c75 2026-09-16] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said the Vera Rubin platform was now in full production.\\\\n    Quote: Vera Rubin, now in full production, was built to power exactly this moment.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3774; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5142 [third_party_view; MarketBeat author; original source MarketBeat author 2026-09-16; from gnews:b98d0a9596b1d1e0a9609645 2026-09-16] The author reports Oracle\\\\u2019s backlog grew to more than $650 billion and Nebius\\\\u2019s backlog increased fourfold.\\\\n    Quote: Critical players like Oracle (NASDAQ: ORCL), now ubiquitous across cloud instances regardless of hyperscaler, saw backlogs grow to more than $650 billion, while neoclouds like Nebius (NASDAQ: NBIS) reported far larger increases, with Nebius's backlog up 4x.\\\\n- e5145 [third_party_view; Michael Burry, quoted from his post on X; original source Michael Burry 2026-09-14; from gnews:a52efd4d6f50652742b93398 2026-09-16] Michael Burry said competition in AI is coming up fast and will slow the benefits.\\\\n    Quote: 2. Competition is coming up fast, slowing benefits...\\\\n- e5146 [party_statement; fool.com (author Jennifer Saibil); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:a52efd4d6f50652742b93398 2026-09-16] The article says NVIDIA expects AI-related capital expenditures to reach $3 trillion to $4 trillion by 2030.\\\\n    Quote: Nvidia expects to reach $3 trillion to $4 trillion by 2030.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e1496; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5147 [party_statement; benzinga.com, reporting Jensen Huang\\\\u2019s remarks at the All-In Summit; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:814422423846b7b421275ebe 2026-09-16] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said the industry needs 50, 100 or even 1,000 neoclouds because hyperscalers plan infrastructure annually and their forecasts can quickly become obsolete as AI demand changes.\\\\n    Quote: Huang said Nvidia would be happy with five hyperscalers, but argued the industry ultimately needs 50, 100 or even 1,000 neoclouds. The reason is speed: hyperscalers typically plan their infrastructure once a year, while AI market dynamics are moving so rapidly that those forecasts can quickly become obsolete.\\\\n- e5148 [party_statement; benzinga.com, reporting Jensen Huang\\\\u2019s remarks at the All-In Summit; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:814422423846b7b421275ebe 2026-09-16] Jensen Huang said NVIDIA is helping regional cloud partners bring additional gigawatts of capacity online in Australia and Southeast Asia; no delivery date was specified.\\\\n    Quote: Huang pointed to activity in Australia and Southeast Asia, saying Nvidia is helping bring additional gigawatts of capacity online through regional cloud partners.\\\\n- e5150 [fact; cnbc.com; original source Snap ; from gnews:28eafda87919cbcc2d744118 2026-09-16] Snap is partnering with NVIDIA, AWS and Salesforce to support an enterprise sales push for its Specs AR glasses; no period or scale of NVIDIA business was specified.\\\\n    Quote: Snap is partnering with Nvidia, Amazon Web Services and Salesforce as part of an enterprise sales push centered on its $2,000 Specs augmented reality glasses.\\\\n- e5159 [fact; fool.com author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ea4633ed3e4ad9d71383673f 2026-09-17] NVIDIA revenue increased 106% year over year in the latest reported quarter.\\\\n    Quote: revenue increased by 106% year over year last quarter\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3025; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5161 [third_party_view; fool.com author; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:ea4633ed3e4ad9d71383673f 2026-09-17] Wall Street analysts expect NVIDIA revenue to grow 90% year over year in FY2027 Q3.\\\\n    Quote: For the remainder of fiscal 2027, Wall Street analysts expect 90% growth in Q3\\\\n- e5162 [third_party_view; fool.com author; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:ea4633ed3e4ad9d71383673f 2026-09-17] Wall Street analysts expect NVIDIA revenue to grow 65% year over year in FY2027 Q4.\\\\n    Quote: and 65% growth in Q4.\\\\n- e5163 [fact; TechCrunch; original source Emerald AI, Google, and NVIDIA 2026-09-17; from gnews:4bf9544d82b0d4574011d0a2 2026-09-17] Emerald AI formed a coalition with Google and NVIDIA to use Emerald AI\\\\u2019s technology to secure grid capacity for additional data centers.\\\\n    Quote: Grid software unicorn Emerald AI has formed a coalition with Google and Nvidia that will use the startup\\\\u2019s technology to secure space on the grid for more data centers.\\\\n- e5164 [party_statement; TechCrunch, reporting AEMA\\\\u2019s claim; original source AI Energy Management Alliance ; from gnews:4bf9544d82b0d4574011d0a2 2026-09-17] The AI Energy Management Alliance said demand response could enable an additional 100 GW of data centers to connect to the grid.\\\\n    Quote: Pausing noncritical tasks and shifting some compute loads, AEMA says, could allow an additional 100 gigawatts of data centers to connect to the grid.\\\\n- e5165 [fact; TechCrunch; original source Emerald AI ; from gnews:4bf9544d82b0d4574011d0a2 2026-09-17] Emerald AI recently raised $150 million in a Series A led by Energize Capital and DCVC to support wider rollout of its technology.\\\\n    Quote: The startup also recently raised $150 million in a Series A led by Energize Capital and DCVC, giving it the sort of funding needed to roll out the technology on a wider scale.\\\\n- e5166 [party_statement; Ayse Coskun, quoted by TechCrunch; original source Ayse Coskun ; from gnews:4bf9544d82b0d4574011d0a2 2026-09-17] Emerald AI chief scientist Ayse Coskun said the company\\\\u2019s technology could reduce, but not eliminate, the data-center industry\\\\u2019s need for new power generation.\\\\n    Quote: Ayse Coskun, Emerald AI\\\\u2019s chief scientist, told TechCrunch that her company\\\\u2019s technology promises to blunt the industry\\\\u2019s need for new generating sources, but it won\\\\u2019t eliminate it entirely.\\\\n- e5172 [third_party_view; Hayden Capital, as quoted by Insider Monkey; original source Hayden Capital ; from gnews:81badd809629cf7b5ba30af9 2026-09-17] Hayden Capital said supply growth was already beginning, citing recent announcements from SK Hynix, Samsung, and CXMT.\\\\n    Quote: falling token prices require supply to increase, which is already starting to happen (see the recent announcements from SK Hynix, Samsung, and CXMT).\\\\n- e5186 [fact; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:509f491c104308dfdd480587 2026-09-17] NVIDIA reported total revenue of $96.2 billion in its latest reported quarter.\\\\n    Quote: the company's latest $96.2 billion quarter\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4656; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5190 [party_statement; John Bromels, The Motley Fool, quoting Eric Xu; original source Huawei rotating chairman Eric Xu 2026-09-17; from gnews:90eeb17159f8e9139586875f 2026-09-17] Huawei rotating chairman Eric Xu said Huawei lacks capacity to meet demand in China and does not plan a fully fledged international-market expansion.\\\\n    Quote: Another of Huawei's rotating chairmen, Eric Xu, told reporters, \\\\\\\"Since we don't have enough capacity to even satisfy the demand in China, we don't have a plan to expand into the international market in a fully fledged way.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5276, e5340; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5193 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source ASUS 2026-09-17; from gnews:4425f01994c0a126351f2bad 2026-09-17] ASUS began shipping its ExpertCenter Pro ET900N G3 deskside AI supercomputer, powered by NVIDIA\\\\u2019s GB300 Grace Blackwell Ultra Desktop Superchip.\\\\n    Quote: The ASUS ExpertCenter Pro ET900N G3 deskside AI supercomputer is now shipping.\\\\n- e5194 [fact; ASUS and Poesis, in a Business Wire release republished by finance.yahoo.com; original source ASUS and Poesis 2026-09-17; from gnews:4425f01994c0a126351f2bad 2026-09-17] ASUS and Poesis reported completing a week-long experiment deploying autonomous AI agents to trade in financial markets on an ASUS system powered by NVIDIA\\\\u2019s GB300 Grace Blackwell Ultra Desktop Superchip.\\\\n    Quote: SAN FRANCISCO, September 17, 2026 --( BUSINESS WIRE )--ASUS and Poesis today announced the results of a week-long experiment that successfully deployed agentic AI to trade autonomously in financial markets.\\\\n- e5196 [party_statement; TechCrunch reporter Kate Park, reporting Huawei\\\\u2019s statement at Huawei Connect; original source Huawei 2026-09-17; from gnews:d95188870b47d6bc96119e87 2026-09-17] Huawei said it moved the planned Ascend 960DT AI chip launch forward to Q1 2027 from Q3 2027, increasing competitive pressure on NVIDIA.\\\\n    Quote: Huawei is moving up the launch of its next-generation Ascend 960DT AI chip to the first quarter of 2027, as it races to challenge Nvidia, the company said on Thursday at its Huawei Connect conference.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5173, e5273; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5197 [party_statement; TechCrunch reporter Kate Park, reporting Huawei\\\\u2019s statement; original source Huawei ; from gnews:d95188870b47d6bc96119e87 2026-09-17] Huawei said its Atlas 950 SuperCluster, based on its Peerium Computing Architecture, can connect up to 256,000 accelerator cards.\\\\n    Quote: Huawei\\\\u2019s Atlas 950 SuperPoD and SuperCluster are the first systems based on the architecture. The company says an Atlas 950 SuperCluster can connect up to 256,000 accelerator cards.\\\\n- e5198 [third_party_view; TechCrunch reporter Kate Park, quoting analyst Rui Ma\\\\u2019s post on X; original source Rui Ma ; from gnews:d95188870b47d6bc96119e87 2026-09-17] Analyst Rui Ma said Huawei\\\\u2019s announced system referred to 4,096 Ascend 960 chips, versus a previously stated 15,488-chip scale for the Atlas 960 SuperPoD, despite the chip arriving earlier.\\\\n    Quote: China tech analyst Rui Ma said on X that Huawei had previously said its Atlas 960 SuperPoD would scale to 15,488 Ascend 960 chips, while this week\\\\u2019s announcement referred to a system with 4,096 chips. \\\\u201cThe chip itself is coming WAY earlier, but the SuperPoD they announced is much smaller than what they originally laid out,\\\\u201d Ma wrote.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5339; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5200 [fact; CRN; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3a284e233d8b31c62dc66b33 2026-09-18] NVIDIA reported revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year, for the quarter ended in June 2026.\\\\n    Quote: The company had reported a 106 percent year-over-year increase in revenue to $96.2 billion for the period that ended in June\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3694; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5204 [third_party_view; CRN, citing Yahoo Finance; original source Financial analysts surveyed by Yahoo Finance ; from gnews:3a284e233d8b31c62dc66b33 2026-09-18] Yahoo Finance's analyst consensus estimated NVIDIA FY2027 revenue at $411 billion.\\\\n    Quote: financial analysts on average estimate will make $411 billion in revenue for its current fiscal year, according to Yahoo Finance\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4294; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5205 [third_party_view; CRN; original source CRN 2026-09-18; from gnews:3a284e233d8b31c62dc66b33 2026-09-18] CRN reported that NVIDIA-related AI infrastructure supply constraints were producing channel-partner lead times of up to a year.\\\\n    Quote: For channel partners, supply constraints have translated into long lead times, sometimes stretching out to as long as a year.\\\\n- e5207 [third_party_view; An unnamed director-level employee, quoted by CRN; original source An unnamed director-level employee at a large U.S. solution provider ; from gnews:3a284e233d8b31c62dc66b33 2026-09-18] An unnamed director-level employee at a large U.S. solution provider said enterprise customers could wait eight to 12 months to receive AI infrastructure.\\\\n    Quote: \\\\u201cHow do I explain to an enterprise that it might be literally eight to 12 months before they even see infrastructure, let alone put it into production?\\\\u201d\\\\n- e5208 [third_party_view; Richard Rudometkin, quoted by CRN; original source Richard Rudometkin, vice president of global sales at International Computer Concepts ; from gnews:3a284e233d8b31c62dc66b33 2026-09-18] International Computer Concepts VP Richard Rudometkin said Supermicro could ship certain GPU-accelerated systems in about two weeks, versus 12 to 16 weeks from Dell, MSI, or other vendors.\\\\n    Quote: \\\\u201cThey\\\\u2019ve done a really good job of planning, and they\\\\u2019ve taken [on the] risk. They\\\\u2019ve brought product in, but you know it\\\\u2019s paying off for them because if we have a project and we go to Dell or we go to MSI or [someone else], they\\\\u2019re telling us 12 to 16 weeks, and Supermicro is saying, \\\\u2018I can ship two weeks from Friday,\\\\u2019\\\\u201d\\\\n- e5215 [fact; The Motley Fool author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:a7b0dfa6b48b220718e5096c 2026-09-18] NVIDIA's second-quarter revenue grew 106% year over year, and adjusted net income grew 118%; the item does not specify the quarter's fiscal year.\\\\n    Quote: The company grew revenue 106% year over year in the second quarter, and adjusted net income surged by 118%.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5002; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5217 [fact; uk.finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3742f4ebc0994af8eb404431 2026-09-18] NVIDIA reported second-quarter revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year.\\\\n    Quote: Second-quarter revenue hit $96.2bn, up 106% year on year.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3234; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5220 [fact; The Motley Fool author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:12a943c49b0c41542e6110b5 2026-09-18] NVIDIA reported total revenue of $96.2 billion for the quarter ended July 26, 2026, up 18% quarter over quarter and 106% year over year.\\\\n    Quote: For the quarter ended July 26, 2026, Nvidia reported total revenue of $96.2 billion, up 18% from the prior quarter and 106% from a year ago.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2745; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5222 [party_statement; The Motley Fool author; original source NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress ; from gnews:12a943c49b0c41542e6110b5 2026-09-18] NVIDIA reported hyperscale revenue of $49 billion, up 13% quarter over quarter, and ACIE revenue of $40 billion, up 25%, in the quarter ended July 26, 2026.\\\\n    Quote: Hyperscale revenue was $49 billion, up 13% from the prior quarter, while the ACIE side grew even faster to $40 billion, up 25%.\\\\n- e5223 [party_statement; The Motley Fool author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:12a943c49b0c41542e6110b5 2026-09-18] NVIDIA guided next-quarter total revenue to about $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, citing continued strength in its AI Data Center business as the primary growth driver.\\\\n    Quote: First, it guided total revenue for the next quarter to about $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, and said growth would be driven primarily by continued strength in the AI data center business.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3585; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5225 [fact; The Motley Fool author; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:12a943c49b0c41542e6110b5 2026-09-18] Broadcom reported revenue of $29.6 billion, up 86% year over year, and AI semiconductor sales of $16.7 billion, up 221% year over year and 54% quarter over quarter, for the quarter ended August 2, 2026.\\\\n    Quote: For the quarter ended Aug. 2, Broadcom reported $29.6 billion in revenue, up 86% year over year. AI semiconductor sales accounted for $16.7 billion, more than half of total revenue, and surged 221% from a year earlier and 54% from the prior quarter.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4382; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5226 [party_statement; The Motley Fool author, recounting a Reuters report; original source Broadcom management ; from gnews:12a943c49b0c41542e6110b5 2026-09-18] Broadcom projected AI semiconductor revenue of about $58 billion in FY2026, up 186% year over year, about $115 billion in FY2027, and $230 billion in FY2028.\\\\n    Quote: about $58 billion in AI semiconductor revenue for fiscal 2026, up 186% from the prior year, followed by roughly $115 billion in fiscal 2027 and $230 billion in fiscal 2028, according to a Reuters report . Those are Broadcom's own projections, not outside analyst estimates.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4383, e5286; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5234 [fact; qz.com; original source NVIDIA, Google and Emerald AI 2026-09-18; from gnews:7f7770b988d0550ff0ee82c2 2026-09-18] NVIDIA, Google and Emerald AI announced the launch of the AI Energy Management Alliance to promote grid-responsive AI data centers in exchange for faster grid connections.\\\\n    Quote: NVIDIA, Google $GOOGL , and Emerald AI announced the launch of the AI Energy Management Alliance, a coalition aimed at getting AI data centers to dynamically manage their electricity consumption in response to grid conditions, with the goal of securing faster connections to the power grid in return.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5240, e5265; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5235 [third_party_view; qz.com, reporting Sivaram's remarks according to Engadget; original source Varun Sivaram, Emerald AI CEO ; from gnews:7f7770b988d0550ff0ee82c2 2026-09-18] Emerald AI CEO Varun Sivaram said new data centers can wait ten years or longer for grid access, while average grid utilization is around 50%.\\\\n    Quote: Getting a new data center onto the grid can take ten years or longer, Sivaram noted, because utilities are obligated to guarantee sufficient capacity for peak demand periods. Yet average grid utilization hovers around 50%, which means data centers willing to flex their consumption could tap into substantial headroom on the existing network without forcing expensive new buildout.\\\\n- e5236 [third_party_view; qz.com, citing Fortune; original source Fortune ; from gnews:7f7770b988d0550ff0ee82c2 2026-09-18] A poll cited by Fortune found roughly 70% of Americans would object to a data center being built in their community, chiefly citing local power strain and higher utility bills.\\\\n    Quote: Roughly 70% of Americans would object to a data center being built in their community , citing strain on local power resources and higher utility bills as their leading concerns.\\\\n- e5237 [third_party_view; qz.com, citing Data Center Watch data reported by Fortune; original source Data Center Watch ; from gnews:7f7770b988d0550ff0ee82c2 2026-09-18] Data Center Watch data cited by Fortune said community opposition stalled or halted 48 data-center projects representing more than $156 billion in planned construction last year.\\\\n    Quote: Community opposition stalled or halted 48 projects representing more than $156 billion in planned construction last year alone, according to Data Center Watch data cited by Fortune.\\\\n- e5238 [party_statement; qz.com, reporting NVIDIA and Emerald AI's statement; original source NVIDIA and Emerald AI ; from gnews:7f7770b988d0550ff0ee82c2 2026-09-18] NVIDIA and Emerald AI said they are working with energy and infrastructure partners on AI facilities designed to respond to grid conditions in real time.\\\\n    Quote: NVIDIA and Emerald AI said they are already working with energy and infrastructure partners on AI facilities that can respond to grid conditions in real time.\\\\n- e5240 [fact; James Darley, Energy Digital; original source Google and NVIDIA ; from gnews:45e913c48ad820276ac6aaf6 2026-09-18] Google and NVIDIA announced this week that they founded the AI Energy Management Alliance (AEMA).\\\\n    Quote: Google and NVIDIA , two of the AI boom's leading lights and two of the world's most valuable companies, have this week announced they have founded the AI Energy Management Alliance, or AEMA.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5234; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5241 [party_statement; James Darley, Energy Digital, reporting Varun Sivaram's statement in Fortune; original source Varun Sivaram, Founder and CEO of Emerald AI ; from gnews:45e913c48ad820276ac6aaf6 2026-09-18] NVIDIA, Digital Realty and Emerald AI plan to turn on a nearly 100-megawatt power-flexible AI factory in Virginia later in 2026.\\\\n    Quote: Later this year in Virginia, NVIDIA, Digital Realty and Emerald AI will turn on the world's first power-flexible AI factory at nearly 100 megawatts, designed to prove that a data center can be a precise, controllable load, instead of drawing constant, unyielding power 24/7 and putting unprecedented strain on a rigid grid.\\\\n- e5244 [fact; Yahoo Finance; original source Nscale ; from gnews:f730ea7bda284baea7749a1c 2026-09-18] Nscale filed publicly for a New York IPO to acquire infrastructure to meet demand for AI compute; the item gives no filing date beyond its publication day.\\\\n    Quote: London-based AI data center company Nscale has filed publicly for an initial public offering (IPO) in New York to acquire the infrastructure needed to meet the global demand for artificial intelligence compute power.\\\\n- e5245 [rumour; Yahoo Finance; original source Bloomberg ; from gnews:f730ea7bda284baea7749a1c 2026-09-18] Bloomberg reported that Nscale is seeking to raise up to $3 billion in its IPO; Nscale's filings did not disclose the listing's size or scope.\\\\n    Quote: The company did not disclose the size and scope of its listing in its filings. However, a Bloomberg report cited that the company is seeking to raise as much as $3 billion in the IPO.\\\\n- e5246 [fact; Yahoo Finance; original source Nscale ; from gnews:f730ea7bda284baea7749a1c 2026-09-18] Nscale reported revenue of $140.6 million for the six months ended June 30, 2026, versus $10.4 million for the same period in 2025.\\\\n    Quote: For the six-month period ending June 30, the company generated $140.6 million in revenue, up significantly from $10.4 million during the same period in the prior year.\\\\n- e5247 [fact; Yahoo Finance; original source Nscale ; from gnews:f730ea7bda284baea7749a1c 2026-09-18] Nscale reported a net loss of $1.02 billion for the six months ended June 30, 2026, compared with $368.9 million for the same period in 2025.\\\\n    Quote: However, net losses expanded to $1.02 billion for the period, compared to $368.9 million in the previous year.\\\\n- e5248 [fact; Yahoo Finance; original source Nscale ; from gnews:f730ea7bda284baea7749a1c 2026-09-18] Nscale reported controlling more than 10 GW of power capacity across its AI hubs as of August 2026.\\\\n    Quote: Nscale manages hyperscale AI hubs located in Norway, Portugal, Texas, and West Virginia, controlling over 10 gigawatts of power capacity as of August 2026.\\\\n- e5249 [fact; Yahoo Finance; original source Nscale ; from gnews:f730ea7bda284baea7749a1c 2026-09-18] Nscale reported about $103 billion in total contract value; the item does not specify the contracts' period.\\\\n    Quote: The firm holds about $103 billion in total contract value.\\\\n- e5250 [fact; Yahoo Finance; original source Nscale ; from gnews:f730ea7bda284baea7749a1c 2026-09-18] Nscale disclosed a $45 billion agreement for Anthropic to use compute resources at its Monarch Compute Campus in West Virginia.\\\\n    Quote: Major commitments include a $45-billion agreement with Anthropic to utilize compute resources at Nscale's flagship Monarch Compute Campus in West Virginia.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5384; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5260 [party_statement; benzinga.com, reporting Huang's CNBC interview; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:7218ec5f13c26358ef736b14 2026-09-18] Huang said the rate of AI token generation increased 25-fold in less than a year.\\\\n    Quote: Meanwhile, AI usage continues to climb. Huang said the rate of token generation has increased 25-fold in less than a year.\\\\n- e5261 [party_statement; benzinga.com, reporting Huang's CNBC interview; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:7218ec5f13c26358ef736b14 2026-09-18] Huang said open models account for nearly 70% of generated tokens, compared with about 30% previously.\\\\n    Quote: Open models now account for nearly 70% of generated tokens, up from about 30%.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e1032 (); both are in force: Jensen Huang said that open models account for one in every four tokens generated today.\\\\n- e5262 [party_statement; benzinga.com, reporting Huang's CNBC interview; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:7218ec5f13c26358ef736b14 2026-09-18] Huang expects AI testing to become a third major infrastructure category alongside training and inference, requiring additional data centers and creating another source of compute demand.\\\\n    Quote: In fact, Huang expects testing to become a third major category of AI infrastructure alongside training and inference. He said large testing environments will require additional data centers, creating another source of compute demand.\\\\n- e5264 [party_statement; benzinga.com, reporting Huang's CNBC interview; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:7218ec5f13c26358ef736b14 2026-09-18] Huang said cloud providers are raising prices as older contracts expire, boosting revenue forecasts and investing in more infrastructure.\\\\n    Quote: As older contracts expire, cloud providers are raising prices, boosting revenue forecasts and investing in more infrastructure, Huang said.\\\\n- e5265 [fact; BGR.com, reporting NVIDIA\\\\u2019s announcement; original source NVIDIA 2026-09-18; from gnews:109fc9fd6937796c01c45a8c 2026-09-18] NVIDIA announced a partnership with Google and Emerald AI to form the AI Energy Management Alliance, which is intended to develop and manage flexible AI data 