ubin NVL72 platform online, connecting hundreds of Rubin GPUs; the deployment follows its June launch of a single rack.\\\\n    Quote: CoreWeave ( CRWV ) shares climbed about 3% on Wednesday trading after the AI cloud company said it had brought Nvidia's ( NVDA ) multi-rack Vera Rubin NVL72 platform online. The new deployment connects hundreds of Rubin GPUs into a unified computing cluster designed to support large-scale artificial intelligence workloads. The rollout builds on CoreWeave's June launch of a single Vera Rubin NVL72 \\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5140; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5119 [third_party_view; Zacks; original source WSTS ; from gnews:fc6c2e31b8c175953657a182 2026-09-16] WSTS forecast global semiconductor sales of $1.51 trillion in calendar 2026, up 89.9%.\\\\n    Quote: WSTS expects global semiconductor sales to grow 89.9% in 2026 to $1.51 trillion, highlighting the extraordinary strength of the current cycle.\\\\n- e5120 [third_party_view; Zacks; original source IDC ; from gnews:fc6c2e31b8c175953657a182 2026-09-16] IDC forecast semiconductor revenue growth of 52.8% in calendar 2026, driven primarily by AI infrastructure investment.\\\\n    Quote: IDC also expects exceptional growth in 2026, with semiconductor revenue rising 52.8%, driven overwhelmingly by AI infrastructure investment.\\\\n- e5121 [third_party_view; Zacks; original source Gartner ; from gnews:fc6c2e31b8c175953657a182 2026-09-16] Gartner forecast global semiconductor revenue of $1.56 trillion in calendar 2026, up 92%.\\\\n    Quote: Gartner expects semiconductor revenue to grow 92% in 2026 to $1.56 trillion.\\\\n- e5123 [third_party_view; Zacks; original source Technavio ; from gnews:fc6c2e31b8c175953657a182 2026-09-16] Technavio estimates military and aerospace semiconductor-market growth at a 6% CAGR through 2029.\\\\n    Quote: Tachnavio estimates that semiconductors used in the military and aerospace market will grow at a 6% CAGR through 2029.\\\\n- e5124 [fact; Zacks; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:fc6c2e31b8c175953657a182 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported FY2027 second-quarter revenue growth of 106% year over year and 18% sequentially; Data Center revenue was $89 billion, up 117% year over year and 18% sequentially.\\\\n    Quote: NVIDIA's second-quarter fiscal 2027 revenue surged 106% year over year and 18% sequentially, while Data Center revenue jumped 117% year over year and 18% sequentially to $89 billion.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4672, e5199; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5125 [party_statement; Zacks; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:fc6c2e31b8c175953657a182 2026-09-16] NVIDIA management said AI demand was accelerating and the infrastructure buildout was expanding across frontier AI labs, startups, open-model developers, enterprises, sovereign AI and physical AI.\\\\n    Quote: Management said AI demand is accelerating, with the buildout expanding beyond the major hyperscalers to multiple frontier AI labs, startups, the open-model ecosystem, enterprises, sovereign AI initiatives and physical AI.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3493; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5127 [party_statement; Zacks; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:fc6c2e31b8c175953657a182 2026-09-16] NVIDIA management said more than 350 factories across 30 countries were ramping the Vera Rubin platform.\\\\n    Quote: Management has said that more than 350 factories across 30 countries are ramping NVIDIA's Vera Rubin platform.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e938; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5129 [third_party_view; Zacks; original source Analysts ; from gnews:fc6c2e31b8c175953657a182 2026-09-16] Analysts forecast NVIDIA revenue growth of 88% and earnings growth of 93.5% in FY2027, followed by revenue growth of 65.5% and earnings growth of 66% in FY2028.\\\\n    Quote: Analysts currently expect revenue and earnings to grow a respective 88% and 93.5% this year followed by a respective 65.5% and 66% in the next.\\\\n- e5134 [third_party_view; trefis.com; original source trefis.com 2026-09-16; from gnews:106a61a1ef10fb3ba6adb1cd 2026-09-16] Trefis calculates NVIDIA trailing-twelve-month revenue at $302.97 billion, up 83.4% year over year; the exact twelve-month period is not specified.\\\\n    Quote: Revenue over the trailing twelve months is $302.97 billion, up 83.4% from a year earlier.\\\\n- e5136 [party_statement; trefis.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:106a61a1ef10fb3ba6adb1cd 2026-09-16] Vera Rubin shipments started in August 2026, and NVIDIA management expects the platform to account for about 20% of Data Center revenue in fiscal Q3 2027.\\\\n    Quote: Vera Rubin shipments started in August 2026, and management expects that platform to be about 20% of data center revenue in fiscal Q3 2027.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3820; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5137 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, quoted by finance.yahoo.com; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:8593bc8819641cdd48950c75 2026-09-16] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said demand for NVIDIA's products was accelerating.\\\\n    Quote: And demand is accelerating.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2869; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5138 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, quoted by finance.yahoo.com; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:8593bc8819641cdd48950c75 2026-09-16] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said the Vera Rubin platform was now in full production.\\\\n    Quote: Vera Rubin, now in full production, was built to power exactly this moment.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3774; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5142 [third_party_view; MarketBeat author; original source MarketBeat author 2026-09-16; from gnews:b98d0a9596b1d1e0a9609645 2026-09-16] The author reports Oracle\\\\u2019s backlog grew to more than $650 billion and Nebius\\\\u2019s backlog increased fourfold.\\\\n    Quote: Critical players like Oracle (NASDAQ: ORCL), now ubiquitous across cloud instances regardless of hyperscaler, saw backlogs grow to more than $650 billion, while neoclouds like Nebius (NASDAQ: NBIS) reported far larger increases, with Nebius's backlog up 4x.\\\\n- e5145 [third_party_view; Michael Burry, quoted from his post on X; original source Michael Burry 2026-09-14; from gnews:a52efd4d6f50652742b93398 2026-09-16] Michael Burry said competition in AI is coming up fast and will slow the benefits.\\\\n    Quote: 2. Competition is coming up fast, slowing benefits...\\\\n- e5146 [party_statement; fool.com (author Jennifer Saibil); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:a52efd4d6f50652742b93398 2026-09-16] The article says NVIDIA expects AI-related capital expenditures to reach $3 trillion to $4 trillion by 2030.\\\\n    Quote: Nvidia expects to reach $3 trillion to $4 trillion by 2030.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e1496; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5147 [party_statement; benzinga.com, reporting Jensen Huang\\\\u2019s remarks at the All-In Summit; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:814422423846b7b421275ebe 2026-09-16] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said the industry needs 50, 100 or even 1,000 neoclouds because hyperscalers plan infrastructure annually and their forecasts can quickly become obsolete as AI demand changes.\\\\n    Quote: Huang said Nvidia would be happy with five hyperscalers, but argued the industry ultimately needs 50, 100 or even 1,000 neoclouds. The reason is speed: hyperscalers typically plan their infrastructure once a year, while AI market dynamics are moving so rapidly that those forecasts can quickly become obsolete.\\\\n- e5148 [party_statement; benzinga.com, reporting Jensen Huang\\\\u2019s remarks at the All-In Summit; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:814422423846b7b421275ebe 2026-09-16] Jensen Huang said NVIDIA is helping regional cloud partners bring additional gigawatts of capacity online in Australia and Southeast Asia; no delivery date was specified.\\\\n    Quote: Huang pointed to activity in Australia and Southeast Asia, saying Nvidia is helping bring additional gigawatts of capacity online through regional cloud partners.\\\\n- e5150 [fact; cnbc.com; original source Snap ; from gnews:28eafda87919cbcc2d744118 2026-09-16] Snap is partnering with NVIDIA, AWS and Salesforce to support an enterprise sales push for its Specs AR glasses; no period or scale of NVIDIA business was specified.\\\\n    Quote: Snap is partnering with Nvidia, Amazon Web Services and Salesforce as part of an enterprise sales push centered on its $2,000 Specs augmented reality glasses.\\\\n- e5159 [fact; fool.com author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ea4633ed3e4ad9d71383673f 2026-09-17] NVIDIA revenue increased 106% year over year in the latest reported quarter.\\\\n    Quote: revenue increased by 106% year over year last quarter\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3025; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5161 [third_party_view; fool.com author; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:ea4633ed3e4ad9d71383673f 2026-09-17] Wall Street analysts expect NVIDIA revenue to grow 90% year over year in FY2027 Q3.\\\\n    Quote: For the remainder of fiscal 2027, Wall Street analysts expect 90% growth in Q3\\\\n- e5162 [third_party_view; fool.com author; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:ea4633ed3e4ad9d71383673f 2026-09-17] Wall Street analysts expect NVIDIA revenue to grow 65% year over year in FY2027 Q4.\\\\n    Quote: and 65% growth in Q4.\\\\n- e5163 [fact; TechCrunch; original source Emerald AI, Google, and NVIDIA 2026-09-17; from gnews:4bf9544d82b0d4574011d0a2 2026-09-17] Emerald AI formed a coalition with Google and NVIDIA to use Emerald AI\\\\u2019s technology to secure grid capacity for additional data centers.\\\\n    Quote: Grid software unicorn Emerald AI has formed a coalition with Google and Nvidia that will use the startup\\\\u2019s technology to secure space on the grid for more data centers.\\\\n- e5164 [party_statement; TechCrunch, reporting AEMA\\\\u2019s claim; original source AI Energy Management Alliance ; from gnews:4bf9544d82b0d4574011d0a2 2026-09-17] The AI Energy Management Alliance said demand response could enable an additional 100 GW of data centers to connect to the grid.\\\\n    Quote: Pausing noncritical tasks and shifting some compute loads, AEMA says, could allow an additional 100 gigawatts of data centers to connect to the grid.\\\\n- e5165 [fact; TechCrunch; original source Emerald AI ; from gnews:4bf9544d82b0d4574011d0a2 2026-09-17] Emerald AI recently raised $150 million in a Series A led by Energize Capital and DCVC to support wider rollout of its technology.\\\\n    Quote: The startup also recently raised $150 million in a Series A led by Energize Capital and DCVC, giving it the sort of funding needed to roll out the technology on a wider scale.\\\\n- e5166 [party_statement; Ayse Coskun, quoted by TechCrunch; original source Ayse Coskun ; from gnews:4bf9544d82b0d4574011d0a2 2026-09-17] Emerald AI chief scientist Ayse Coskun said the company\\\\u2019s technology could reduce, but not eliminate, the data-center industry\\\\u2019s need for new power generation.\\\\n    Quote: Ayse Coskun, Emerald AI\\\\u2019s chief scientist, told TechCrunch that her company\\\\u2019s technology promises to blunt the industry\\\\u2019s need for new generating sources, but it won\\\\u2019t eliminate it entirely.\\\\n- e5172 [third_party_view; Hayden Capital, as quoted by Insider Monkey; original source Hayden Capital ; from gnews:81badd809629cf7b5ba30af9 2026-09-17] Hayden Capital said supply growth was already beginning, citing recent announcements from SK Hynix, Samsung, and CXMT.\\\\n    Quote: falling token prices require supply to increase, which is already starting to happen (see the recent announcements from SK Hynix, Samsung, and CXMT).\\\\n- e5186 [fact; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:509f491c104308dfdd480587 2026-09-17] NVIDIA reported total revenue of $96.2 billion in its latest reported quarter.\\\\n    Quote: the company's latest $96.2 billion quarter\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4656; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5190 [party_statement; John Bromels, The Motley Fool, quoting Eric Xu; original source Huawei rotating chairman Eric Xu 2026-09-17; from gnews:90eeb17159f8e9139586875f 2026-09-17] Huawei rotating chairman Eric Xu said Huawei lacks capacity to meet demand in China and does not plan a fully fledged international-market expansion.\\\\n    Quote: Another of Huawei's rotating chairmen, Eric Xu, told reporters, \\\\\\\"Since we don't have enough capacity to even satisfy the demand in China, we don't have a plan to expand into the international market in a fully fledged way.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5276, e5340; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5193 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source ASUS 2026-09-17; from gnews:4425f01994c0a126351f2bad 2026-09-17] ASUS began shipping its ExpertCenter Pro ET900N G3 deskside AI supercomputer, powered by NVIDIA\\\\u2019s GB300 Grace Blackwell Ultra Desktop Superchip.\\\\n    Quote: The ASUS ExpertCenter Pro ET900N G3 deskside AI supercomputer is now shipping.\\\\n- e5194 [fact; ASUS and Poesis, in a Business Wire release republished by finance.yahoo.com; original source ASUS and Poesis 2026-09-17; from gnews:4425f01994c0a126351f2bad 2026-09-17] ASUS and Poesis reported completing a week-long experiment deploying autonomous AI agents to trade in financial markets on an ASUS system powered by NVIDIA\\\\u2019s GB300 Grace Blackwell Ultra Desktop Superchip.\\\\n    Quote: SAN FRANCISCO, September 17, 2026 --( BUSINESS WIRE )--ASUS and Poesis today announced the results of a week-long experiment that successfully deployed agentic AI to trade autonomously in financial markets.\\\\n- e5196 [party_statement; TechCrunch reporter Kate Park, reporting Huawei\\\\u2019s statement at Huawei Connect; original source Huawei 2026-09-17; from gnews:d95188870b47d6bc96119e87 2026-09-17] Huawei said it moved the planned Ascend 960DT AI chip launch forward to Q1 2027 from Q3 2027, increasing competitive pressure on NVIDIA.\\\\n    Quote: Huawei is moving up the launch of its next-generation Ascend 960DT AI chip to the first quarter of 2027, as it races to challenge Nvidia, the company said on Thursday at its Huawei Connect conference.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5173, e5273; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5197 [party_statement; TechCrunch reporter Kate Park, reporting Huawei\\\\u2019s statement; original source Huawei ; from gnews:d95188870b47d6bc96119e87 2026-09-17] Huawei said its Atlas 950 SuperCluster, based on its Peerium Computing Architecture, can connect up to 256,000 accelerator cards.\\\\n    Quote: Huawei\\\\u2019s Atlas 950 SuperPoD and SuperCluster are the first systems based on the architecture. The company says an Atlas 950 SuperCluster can connect up to 256,000 accelerator cards.\\\\n- e5198 [third_party_view; TechCrunch reporter Kate Park, quoting analyst Rui Ma\\\\u2019s post on X; original source Rui Ma ; from gnews:d95188870b47d6bc96119e87 2026-09-17] Analyst Rui Ma said Huawei\\\\u2019s announced system referred to 4,096 Ascend 960 chips, versus a previously stated 15,488-chip scale for the Atlas 960 SuperPoD, despite the chip arriving earlier.\\\\n    Quote: China tech analyst Rui Ma said on X that Huawei had previously said its Atlas 960 SuperPoD would scale to 15,488 Ascend 960 chips, while this week\\\\u2019s announcement referred to a system with 4,096 chips. \\\\u201cThe chip itself is coming WAY earlier, but the SuperPoD they announced is much smaller than what they originally laid out,\\\\u201d Ma wrote.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5339; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5200 [fact; CRN; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3a284e233d8b31c62dc66b33 2026-09-18] NVIDIA reported revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year, for the quarter ended in June 2026.\\\\n    Quote: The company had reported a 106 percent year-over-year increase in revenue to $96.2 billion for the period that ended in June\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3694; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5204 [third_party_view; CRN, citing Yahoo Finance; original source Financial analysts surveyed by Yahoo Finance ; from gnews:3a284e233d8b31c62dc66b33 2026-09-18] Yahoo Finance's analyst consensus estimated NVIDIA FY2027 revenue at $411 billion.\\\\n    Quote: financial analysts on average estimate will make $411 billion in revenue for its current fiscal year, according to Yahoo Finance\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4294; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5205 [third_party_view; CRN; original source CRN 2026-09-18; from gnews:3a284e233d8b31c62dc66b33 2026-09-18] CRN reported that NVIDIA-related AI infrastructure supply constraints were producing channel-partner lead times of up to a year.\\\\n    Quote: For channel partners, supply constraints have translated into long lead times, sometimes stretching out to as long as a year.\\\\n- e5207 [third_party_view; An unnamed director-level employee, quoted by CRN; original source An unnamed director-level employee at a large U.S. solution provider ; from gnews:3a284e233d8b31c62dc66b33 2026-09-18] An unnamed director-level employee at a large U.S. solution provider said enterprise customers could wait eight to 12 months to receive AI infrastructure.\\\\n    Quote: \\\\u201cHow do I explain to an enterprise that it might be literally eight to 12 months before they even see infrastructure, let alone put it into production?\\\\u201d\\\\n- e5208 [third_party_view; Richard Rudometkin, quoted by CRN; original source Richard Rudometkin, vice president of global sales at International Computer Concepts ; from gnews:3a284e233d8b31c62dc66b33 2026-09-18] International Computer Concepts VP Richard Rudometkin said Supermicro could ship certain GPU-accelerated systems in about two weeks, versus 12 to 16 weeks from Dell, MSI, or other vendors.\\\\n    Quote: \\\\u201cThey\\\\u2019ve done a really good job of planning, and they\\\\u2019ve taken [on the] risk. They\\\\u2019ve brought product in, but you know it\\\\u2019s paying off for them because if we have a project and we go to Dell or we go to MSI or [someone else], they\\\\u2019re telling us 12 to 16 weeks, and Supermicro is saying, \\\\u2018I can ship two weeks from Friday,\\\\u2019\\\\u201d\\\\n- e5215 [fact; The Motley Fool author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:a7b0dfa6b48b220718e5096c 2026-09-18] NVIDIA's second-quarter revenue grew 106% year over year, and adjusted net income grew 118%; the item does not specify the quarter's fiscal year.\\\\n    Quote: The company grew revenue 106% year over year in the second quarter, and adjusted net income surged by 118%.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5002; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5217 [fact; uk.finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3742f4ebc0994af8eb404431 2026-09-18] NVIDIA reported second-quarter revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year.\\\\n    Quote: Second-quarter revenue hit $96.2bn, up 106% year on year.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3234; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5220 [fact; The Motley Fool author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:12a943c49b0c41542e6110b5 2026-09-18] NVIDIA reported total revenue of $96.2 billion for the quarter ended July 26, 2026, up 18% quarter over quarter and 106% year over year.\\\\n    Quote: For the quarter ended July 26, 2026, Nvidia reported total revenue of $96.2 billion, up 18% from the prior quarter and 106% from a year ago.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2745; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5222 [party_statement; The Motley Fool author; original source NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress ; from gnews:12a943c49b0c41542e6110b5 2026-09-18] NVIDIA reported hyperscale revenue of $49 billion, up 13% quarter over quarter, and ACIE revenue of $40 billion, up 25%, in the quarter ended July 26, 2026.\\\\n    Quote: Hyperscale revenue was $49 billion, up 13% from the prior quarter, while the ACIE side grew even faster to $40 billion, up 25%.\\\\n- e5223 [party_statement; The Motley Fool author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:12a943c49b0c41542e6110b5 2026-09-18] NVIDIA guided next-quarter total revenue to about $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, citing continued strength in its AI Data Center business as the primary growth driver.\\\\n    Quote: First, it guided total revenue for the next quarter to about $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, and said growth would be driven primarily by continued strength in the AI data center business.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3585; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5225 [fact; The Motley Fool author; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:12a943c49b0c41542e6110b5 2026-09-18] Broadcom reported revenue of $29.6 billion, up 86% year over year, and AI semiconductor sales of $16.7 billion, up 221% year over year and 54% quarter over quarter, for the quarter ended August 2, 2026.\\\\n    Quote: For the quarter ended Aug. 2, Broadcom reported $29.6 billion in revenue, up 86% year over year. AI semiconductor sales accounted for $16.7 billion, more than half of total revenue, and surged 221% from a year earlier and 54% from the prior quarter.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4382; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5226 [party_statement; The Motley Fool author, recounting a Reuters report; original source Broadcom management ; from gnews:12a943c49b0c41542e6110b5 2026-09-18] Broadcom projected AI semiconductor revenue of about $58 billion in FY2026, up 186% year over year, about $115 billion in FY2027, and $230 billion in FY2028.\\\\n    Quote: about $58 billion in AI semiconductor revenue for fiscal 2026, up 186% from the prior year, followed by roughly $115 billion in fiscal 2027 and $230 billion in fiscal 2028, according to a Reuters report . Those are Broadcom's own projections, not outside analyst estimates.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4383, e5286; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5234 [fact; qz.com; original source NVIDIA, Google and Emerald AI 2026-09-18; from gnews:7f7770b988d0550ff0ee82c2 2026-09-18] NVIDIA, Google and Emerald AI announced the launch of the AI Energy Management Alliance to promote grid-responsive AI data centers in exchange for faster grid connections.\\\\n    Quote: NVIDIA, Google $GOOGL , and Emerald AI announced the launch of the AI Energy Management Alliance, a coalition aimed at getting AI data centers to dynamically manage their electricity consumption in response to grid conditions, with the goal of securing faster connections to the power grid in return.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5240, e5265; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5235 [third_party_view; qz.com, reporting Sivaram's remarks according to Engadget; original source Varun Sivaram, Emerald AI CEO ; from gnews:7f7770b988d0550ff0ee82c2 2026-09-18] Emerald AI CEO Varun Sivaram said new data centers can wait ten years or longer for grid access, while average grid utilization is around 50%.\\\\n    Quote: Getting a new data center onto the grid can take ten years or longer, Sivaram noted, because utilities are obligated to guarantee sufficient capacity for peak demand periods. Yet average grid utilization hovers around 50%, which means data centers willing to flex their consumption could tap into substantial headroom on the existing network without forcing expensive new buildout.\\\\n- e5236 [third_party_view; qz.com, citing Fortune; original source Fortune ; from gnews:7f7770b988d0550ff0ee82c2 2026-09-18] A poll cited by Fortune found roughly 70% of Americans would object to a data center being built in their community, chiefly citing local power strain and higher utility bills.\\\\n    Quote: Roughly 70% of Americans would object to a data center being built in their community , citing strain on local power resources and higher utility bills as their leading concerns.\\\\n- e5237 [third_party_view; qz.com, citing Data Center Watch data reported by Fortune; original source Data Center Watch ; from gnews:7f7770b988d0550ff0ee82c2 2026-09-18] Data Center Watch data cited by Fortune said community opposition stalled or halted 48 data-center projects representing more than $156 billion in planned construction last year.\\\\n    Quote: Community opposition stalled or halted 48 projects representing more than $156 billion in planned construction last year alone, according to Data Center Watch data cited by Fortune.\\\\n- e5238 [party_statement; qz.com, reporting NVIDIA and Emerald AI's statement; original source NVIDIA and Emerald AI ; from gnews:7f7770b988d0550ff0ee82c2 2026-09-18] NVIDIA and Emerald AI said they are working with energy and infrastructure partners on AI facilities designed to respond to grid conditions in real time.\\\\n    Quote: NVIDIA and Emerald AI said they are already working with energy and infrastructure partners on AI facilities that can respond to grid conditions in real time.\\\\n- e5240 [fact; James Darley, Energy Digital; original source Google and NVIDIA ; from gnews:45e913c48ad820276ac6aaf6 2026-09-18] Google and NVIDIA announced this week that they founded the AI Energy Management Alliance (AEMA).\\\\n    Quote: Google and NVIDIA , two of the AI boom's leading lights and two of the world's most valuable companies, have this week announced they have founded the AI Energy Management Alliance, or AEMA.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5234; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5241 [party_statement; James Darley, Energy Digital, reporting Varun Sivaram's statement in Fortune; original source Varun Sivaram, Founder and CEO of Emerald AI ; from gnews:45e913c48ad820276ac6aaf6 2026-09-18] NVIDIA, Digital Realty and Emerald AI plan to turn on a nearly 100-megawatt power-flexible AI factory in Virginia later in 2026.\\\\n    Quote: Later this year in Virginia, NVIDIA, Digital Realty and Emerald AI will turn on the world's first power-flexible AI factory at nearly 100 megawatts, designed to prove that a data center can be a precise, controllable load, instead of drawing constant, unyielding power 24/7 and putting unprecedented strain on a rigid grid.\\\\n- e5244 [fact; Yahoo Finance; original source Nscale ; from gnews:f730ea7bda284baea7749a1c 2026-09-18] Nscale filed publicly for a New York IPO to acquire infrastructure to meet demand for AI compute; the item gives no filing date beyond its publication day.\\\\n    Quote: London-based AI data center company Nscale has filed publicly for an initial public offering (IPO) in New York to acquire the infrastructure needed to meet the global demand for artificial intelligence compute power.\\\\n- e5245 [rumour; Yahoo Finance; original source Bloomberg ; from gnews:f730ea7bda284baea7749a1c 2026-09-18] Bloomberg reported that Nscale is seeking to raise up to $3 billion in its IPO; Nscale's filings did not disclose the listing's size or scope.\\\\n    Quote: The company did not disclose the size and scope of its listing in its filings. However, a Bloomberg report cited that the company is seeking to raise as much as $3 billion in the IPO.\\\\n- e5246 [fact; Yahoo Finance; original source Nscale ; from gnews:f730ea7bda284baea7749a1c 2026-09-18] Nscale reported revenue of $140.6 million for the six months ended June 30, 2026, versus $10.4 million for the same period in 2025.\\\\n    Quote: For the six-month period ending June 30, the company generated $140.6 million in revenue, up significantly from $10.4 million during the same period in the prior year.\\\\n- e5247 [fact; Yahoo Finance; original source Nscale ; from gnews:f730ea7bda284baea7749a1c 2026-09-18] Nscale reported a net loss of $1.02 billion for the six months ended June 30, 2026, compared with $368.9 million for the same period in 2025.\\\\n    Quote: However, net losses expanded to $1.02 billion for the period, compared to $368.9 million in the previous year.\\\\n- e5248 [fact; Yahoo Finance; original source Nscale ; from gnews:f730ea7bda284baea7749a1c 2026-09-18] Nscale reported controlling more than 10 GW of power capacity across its AI hubs as of August 2026.\\\\n    Quote: Nscale manages hyperscale AI hubs located in Norway, Portugal, Texas, and West Virginia, controlling over 10 gigawatts of power capacity as of August 2026.\\\\n- e5249 [fact; Yahoo Finance; original source Nscale ; from gnews:f730ea7bda284baea7749a1c 2026-09-18] Nscale reported about $103 billion in total contract value; the item does not specify the contracts' period.\\\\n    Quote: The firm holds about $103 billion in total contract value.\\\\n- e5250 [fact; Yahoo Finance; original source Nscale ; from gnews:f730ea7bda284baea7749a1c 2026-09-18] Nscale disclosed a $45 billion agreement for Anthropic to use compute resources at its Monarch Compute Campus in West Virginia.\\\\n    Quote: Major commitments include a $45-billion agreement with Anthropic to utilize compute resources at Nscale's flagship Monarch Compute Campus in West Virginia.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5384; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5260 [party_statement; benzinga.com, reporting Huang's CNBC interview; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:7218ec5f13c26358ef736b14 2026-09-18] Huang said the rate of AI token generation increased 25-fold in less than a year.\\\\n    Quote: Meanwhile, AI usage continues to climb. Huang said the rate of token generation has increased 25-fold in less than a year.\\\\n- e5261 [party_statement; benzinga.com, reporting Huang's CNBC interview; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:7218ec5f13c26358ef736b14 2026-09-18] Huang said open models account for nearly 70% of generated tokens, compared with about 30% previously.\\\\n    Quote: Open models now account for nearly 70% of generated tokens, up from about 30%.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e1032 (); both are in force: Jensen Huang said that open models account for one in every four tokens generated today.\\\\n- e5262 [party_statement; benzinga.com, reporting Huang's CNBC interview; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:7218ec5f13c26358ef736b14 2026-09-18] Huang expects AI testing to become a third major infrastructure category alongside training and inference, requiring additional data centers and creating another source of compute demand.\\\\n    Quote: In fact, Huang expects testing to become a third major category of AI infrastructure alongside training and inference. He said large testing environments will require additional data centers, creating another source of compute demand.\\\\n- e5264 [party_statement; benzinga.com, reporting Huang's CNBC interview; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:7218ec5f13c26358ef736b14 2026-09-18] Huang said cloud providers are raising prices as older contracts expire, boosting revenue forecasts and investing in more infrastructure.\\\\n    Quote: As older contracts expire, cloud providers are raising prices, boosting revenue forecasts and investing in more infrastructure, Huang said.\\\\n- e5265 [fact; BGR.com, reporting NVIDIA\\\\u2019s announcement; original source NVIDIA 2026-09-18; from gnews:109fc9fd6937796c01c45a8c 2026-09-18] NVIDIA announced a partnership with Google and Emerald AI to form the AI Energy Management Alliance, which is intended to develop and manage flexible AI data centers.\\\\n    Quote: Recently, Nvidia announced that it has teamed up with Google and Emerald AI to form the AI Energy Management Alliance (AEMA).\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5234, e5302; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5266 [third_party_view; Varun Sivaram, quoted by Fortune and retold by BGR.com; original source Varun Sivaram ; from gnews:109fc9fd6937796c01c45a8c 2026-09-18] Emerald AI founder Varun Sivaram estimated that flexible data centers could free up 100 GW of power.\\\\n    Quote: By Sivaram's calculations, flexible data centers could free up 100 GW of power, which would be reflected not only in electricity use but also bills.\\\\n- e5273 [fact; Channel Insider; original source Huawei ; from gnews:7d83454ace7462ccdd8aaeb9 2026-09-18] Huawei unveiled the Atlas 960E SuperPoD and moved the planned Ascend 960DT launch forward to Q1 2027.\\\\n    Quote: The AI giant unveiled the Atlas 960E SuperPoD and accelerated the launch of its Ascend 960DT AI chip to the first quarter of 2027.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5196; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5274 [party_statement; Channel Insider; original source Huawei ; from gnews:7d83454ace7462ccdd8aaeb9 2026-09-18] Huawei plans a new Ascend generation annually, with Ascend 970 scheduled for 2028 and Ascend 980 for 2029.\\\\n    Quote: The company also plans to introduce a new Ascend generation each year, with the Ascend 970 and 980 scheduled for 2028 and 2029, respectively.\\\\n- e5275 [third_party_view; Channel Insider; original source Reuters ; from gnews:7d83454ace7462ccdd8aaeb9 2026-09-18] Reuters reported that Huawei cannot produce enough AI computing equipment to meet demand in China.\\\\n    Quote: Reuters reported that Huawei is already struggling to produce enough AI computing equipment to satisfy demand in China.\\\\n- e5276 [party_statement; Channel Insider; original source Eric Xu, Huawei rotating chairman ; from gnews:7d83454ace7462ccdd8aaeb9 2026-09-18] Huawei rotating chairman Eric Xu said Huawei has no current plans for large-scale overseas expansion, citing insufficient production to meet demand in China.\\\\n    Quote: Rotating chairman Eric Xu said the company therefore has no plans for a large-scale overseas expansion for now.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5190; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5277 [party_statement; Channel Insider; original source Huawei ; from gnews:7d83454ace7462ccdd8aaeb9 2026-09-18] Huawei said its CANN software has more than 5,200 monthly active developers and is now under sustained, community-driven open-source development.\\\\n    Quote: The company said CANN has moved to sustained, community-driven open-source development and now has more than 5,200 monthly active developers.\\\\n- e5278 [party_statement; Channel Insider; original source Huawei ; from gnews:7d83454ace7462ccdd8aaeb9 2026-09-18] Huawei said Ascend supports more than 90 third-party open-source projects, including PyTorch, Triton, vLLM, and veRL.\\\\n    Quote: Huawei also highlighted that Ascend supports more than 90 third-party open-source projects, including PyTorch, Triton, vLLM, and veRL.\\\\n- e5279 [party_statement; Channel Insider; original source Huawei ; from gnews:7d83454ace7462ccdd8aaeb9 2026-09-18] Huawei said more than 40 models have been natively pretrained on its Ascend hardware and CANN software.\\\\n    Quote: More than 40 models have been natively pretrained on Ascend and CANN.\\\\n- e5280 [rumour; Channel Insider; original source Channel Insider ; from gnews:7d83454ace7462ccdd8aaeb9 2026-09-18] DeepSeek reportedly plans to deploy 160,000 Huawei AI chips at a data center in Inner Mongolia.\\\\n    Quote: DeepSeek reportedly plans to deploy 160,000 Huawei AI chips at a data center in Inner Mongolia , a project that could further expand Huawei\\\\u2019s role in China\\\\u2019s AI infrastructure market.\\\\n- e5285 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Broadcom 2026-09-02; from gnews:ad29d60c2dff48278b88758a 2026-09-18] Broadcom reported that total revenue grew 86% and AI semiconductor revenue grew 221% in the quarter ended September 2, 2026.\\\\n    Quote: during the quarter, the firm's revenue grew by 86%, AI semiconductor revenue jumped by 221%\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5007; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5286 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source Broadcom ; from gnews:ad29d60c2dff48278b88758a 2026-09-18] Broadcom's FY2026 guidance implied 186% growth in AI revenue for FY2026.\\\\n    Quote: fiscal year 2026 guidance implied 186% annual AI revenue growth\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5226; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5287 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source Hock Tan, Broadcom CEO ; from gnews:ad29d60c2dff48278b88758a 2026-09-18] Broadcom CEO Hock Tan said Broadcom could generate $115 billion in annual AI chip sales in 2027 and $230 billion in 2028.\\\\n    Quote: CEO Tan reaffirmed that Broadcom Inc. (NASDAQ:AVGO) could pull in $115 billion in annual AI chip sales in 2027 and a whopping $230 billion in 2028.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4982; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5288 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source finance.yahoo.com ; from gnews:ad29d60c2dff48278b88758a 2026-09-18] Estimates cited by the article suggest OpenAI and Anthropic could account for 71% of Broadcom's XPU deployment in fiscal 2027 and 2028.\\\\n    Quote: estimates have suggested that 71% of Broadcom Inc. (NASDAQ:AVGO) 's fiscal 2027 and 2028 XPU deployment could rely on OpenAI and Anthropic\\\\n- e5289 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source Intel Corporation ; from gnews:d7c05e7b0777edd1a79bc806 2026-09-18] Intel reported second-quarter data center and server revenue of $6.26 billion, up 59% year over year.\\\\n    Quote: The firm's second quarter results saw its data center and server business's revenue sit at $6.26 billion to beat analyst estimates of $5.37 billion. The growth for the business was 59% which suprassed overall revenue growth of 25%.\\\\n- e5290 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source Dario Amodei, Anthropic ; from gnews:d7c05e7b0777edd1a79bc806 2026-09-18] Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei said safety concerns required a slowdown in AI development.\\\\n    Quote: His remarks followed Anthropic's Dario Amodei, who outlined that safety concerns necessitated a slowdown\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4904; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5291 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA ; from gnews:d7c05e7b0777edd1a79bc806 2026-09-18] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said AI development did not need to slow down.\\\\n    Quote: where CEO Jensen Huang insisted that AI development did not have to slow down.\\\\n- e5292 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA ; from gnews:d7c05e7b0777edd1a79bc806 2026-09-18] Jensen Huang argued that AI labs with safety concerns should delay product launches until those concerns are resolved rather than call for a broader slowdown in AI development.\\\\n    Quote: Huang countered by arguing that labs with safety concerns should delay launching products until said concerns had been resolved, instead of pushing for a broader slowdown.\\\\n- e5294 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA Corporation ; from gnews:d7c05e7b0777edd1a79bc806 2026-09-18] NVIDIA's Q3 guidance implied 117% year-over-year total revenue growth.\\\\n    Quote: its Q3 guidance implied a 117% annual revenue growth.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e4523 (2026-08-26); both are in force: NVIDIA management guided to total revenue growth of about 90% year over year in FY2027 Q3.\\\\n- e5296 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source Piper Sandler ; from gnews:d7c05e7b0777edd1a79bc806 2026-09-18] Piper Sandler initiated coverage of NVIDIA with an Overweight rating and a $300 price target, citing an 80% share of AI compute among other factors.\\\\n    Quote: Piper Sandler is quite optimistic about NVIDIA, though, as it initiated coverage with an Overweight rating and a $300 price target on the back of 80% share in AI compute and other factors.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2411; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5297 [fact; benzinga.com; original source Salesforce ; from gnews:cbf072e65acf3391f77465fd 2026-09-18] Salesforce unveiled Koa, its first CRM reasoning model for Agentforce, built on NVIDIA Nemotron 3 Super and running inside Salesforce infrastructure.\\\\n    Quote: Salesforce also unveiled Koa, its first CRM reasoning model for Agentforce, built on Nvidia Nemotron 3 Super and running inside Salesforce infrastructure.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5043; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5298 [party_statement; benzinga.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:cbf072e65acf3391f77465fd 2026-09-18] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said companies are rapidly building NVIDIA-powered AI factories.\\\\n    Quote: companies are rapidly building Nvidia-powered \\\\\\\"AI factories\\\\\\\"\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e569; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5299 [party_statement; benzinga.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:cbf072e65acf3391f77465fd 2026-09-18] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang described the AI infrastructure spending flywheel as \\\\u201creally, really flying.\\\\u201d\\\\n    Quote: the infrastructure spending flywheel as \\\\\\\"really, really flying.\\\\\\\"\\\\n- e5300 [party_statement; benzinga.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cbf072e65acf3391f77465fd 2026-09-18] NVIDIA forecast third-quarter revenue of $108 billion, plus or minus 2%.\\\\n    Quote: the company forecast third-quarter revenue of $108 billion, plus or minus 2%.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3521; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5301 [fact; Zacks author; original source Anthropic ; from gnews:64b3da817a58392d7d1677e7 2026-09-18] Anthropic signed a $13.7 billion compute agreement earlier in September 2026.\\\\n    Quote: Earlier this month, Anthropic inked a $13.7 billion compute agreement\\\\n- e5302 [fact; tedmag.com; original source Emerald AI, Google and NVIDIA 2026-09-18; from gnews:8c54ac0fb564af052a3f1062 2026-09-18] Emerald AI, Google and NVIDIA announced the launch of the AI Energy Management Alliance to advance data centers that adjust electricity use to grid conditions.\\\\n    Quote: Today, Emerald AI , Google and NVIDIA announced the launch of the AI Energy Management Alliance (AEMA) , a first-of-its-kind coalition advancing data centers that can dynamically manage their electricity use in response to grid conditions.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5265; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5303 [fact; tedmag.com; original source AI Energy Management Alliance (AEMA) 2026-09-18; from gnews:8c54ac0fb564af052a3f1062 2026-09-18] AEMA plans to develop technical and operational approaches, work with utilities on data-center interconnection solutions and advocate for policies recognizing grid-responsive demand.\\\\n    Quote: Together, AEMA will develop technical and operational approaches, collaborate with utilities on interconnection solutions and advocate for policies that recognize grid-responsive demand.\\\\n- e5311 [fact; Zacks.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:57a69374b8fa083ce36ecfb1 2026-09-18] NVIDIA reported total revenue of $96.2 billion in FY2027 Q2, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially.\\\\n    Quote: According to NVIDIA\\\\u2019s Aug. 26 press release, the company\\\\u2019s total revenues reached $96.2 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4896; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5314 [party_statement; Zacks.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:57a69374b8fa083ce36ecfb1 2026-09-18] NVIDIA guided FY2027 Q3 revenue to $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, about 12% above FY2027 Q2 revenue at the guidance midpoint.\\\\n    Quote: Looking ahead, NVIDIA expects profitability to remain strong and projects revenues to reach $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, in the fiscal third quarter of 2027, up 12% sequentially from the midpoint.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5111; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5320 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA 2026-08-27; from gnews:2052184744bec4b89ecab744 2026-09-19] NVIDIA reported fiscal Q2 2027 revenue of $96.2 billion, more than double year over year.\\\\n    Quote: Nvidia reported its second-quarter fiscal 2027 earnings on Aug. 27. Revenue for the quarter rose to a record $96.2 billion, more than double year-over-year (YoY).\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4002; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5323 [party_statement; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA 2026-08-27; from gnews:2052184744bec4b89ecab744 2026-09-19] NVIDIA guided to Q3 FY2027 revenue of $108 billion, plus or minus 2% (about $106 billion to $110 billion).\\\\n    Quote: Looking forward, Nvidia expects third-quarter revenue of $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, which implies a range of about $106 billion to $110 billion.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3816; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5326 [fact; fool.com (Erin Kennedy); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:2f6f0f1163e6efb6a56dab58 2026-09-19] NVIDIA reported FY2026 revenue of approximately $215.9 billion, up nearly 65.5% year over year.\\\\n    Quote: In the fiscal year ended Jan. 25, 2026, according to its latest annual report, revenue reached approximately $215.9 billion. This was a massive increase of nearly 65.5% compared with the prior year.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4273; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5330 [rumour; MakeUseOf, Shaheer Khan; original source MakeUseOf, reporting a VideoCardz report about AMD's testing ; from gnews:e2709d56a76e24a1439d35f5 2026-09-19] AMD is reportedly testing up to 8X FSR Multi Frame Generation in newer RDNA 4 drivers, which the article says could give it an edge over NVIDIA's DLSS 4.5.\\\\n    Quote: However, AMD is testing FSR Multi Frame Generation of up to 8X in newer drivers for RDNA 4 GPUs (via VideoCardz), and that might arrive sooner than expected and give it an edge over DLSS 4.5.\\\\n- e5331 [party_statement; Ian Buck, NVIDIA Vice President; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:5a42294e229a65208f691101 2026-09-19] NVIDIA said The Matrix is adopting NVLink Fusion for its next-generation Raptor XPU, while AWS and Annapurna Labs are collaborating to integrate custom IP into NVHBM; the timing and commercial scale were not specified.\\\\n    Quote: Early partners include the startup The Matrix, which is adopting NVLink Fusion for its next-generation Raptor XPU to connect Vera and NVLink Switch racks, building a complete NVLink 72 architecture that incorporates The Matrix chip. Amazon AWS and Annapurna Labs are also collaborating with us to integrate custom IP into the base die of NVHBM, unlocking 30% to 40% of computing resources on their cu\\\\n- e5332 [party_statement; Ian Buck, NVIDIA Vice President; original source Ian Buck ; from gnews:5a42294e229a65208f691101 2026-09-19] NVIDIA Vice President Ian Buck said computational demand in AgentX increased 100-fold on purely numerical tasks; no period was specified.\\\\n    Quote: In the AgentX benchmark, computational demand has increased by a factor of 100 on purely numerical tasks.\\\\n- e5333 [party_statement; Ian Buck, NVIDIA Vice President; original source Ian Buck ; from gnews:5a42294e229a65208f691101 2026-09-19] Ian Buck said hourly rental rates for NVIDIA A100 instances have risen rather than declined over time, describing demand as robust; no period or rate was given.\\\\n    Quote: In fact, if you track the hourly instance rental rates for the A100\\\\u2014released at the onset of the COVID\\\\u201119 pandemic\\\\u2014you'll find that they have not declined over time but have instead risen, with demand remaining robust.\\\\n- e5338 [party_statement; korben.info; original source Huawei 2026-09-17; from gnews:4d60cc40cc0b61c1a9c9fb5d 2026-09-19] Huawei described its Atlas 960 SuperPoD as a planned cluster of more than 4,000 accelerators, intended to make up for individual-chip performance differences with NVIDIA.\\\\n    Quote: Huawei stacks them: its Atlas 960 SuperPoD, a cluster of more than 4,000 accelerators linked together via fiber optics, is meant to compensate through sheer numbers for what each chip concedes to the American company.\\\\n- e5339 [third_party_view; korben.info; original source korben.info 2026-09-19; from gnews:4d60cc40cc0b61c1a9c9fb5d 2026-09-19] The reported Atlas 960 SuperPoD cluster is smaller than the 15,000-chip system Huawei mentioned the prior year.\\\\n    Quote: One small detail though: this machine is notably more modest than the 15,000-chip monster mentioned last year. The chip is arriving earlier, but the cluster has shrunk.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5198; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5340 [party_statement; korben.info; original source Huawei ; from gnews:4d60cc40cc0b61c1a9c9fb5d 2026-09-19] Huawei said its chip production is insufficient to meet demand in China.\\\\n    Quote: The group even admits it isn't producing enough to meet Chinese demand.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5190; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5341 [fact; korben.info; original source Huawei 2026-09-17; from gnews:4d60cc40cc0b61c1a9c9fb5d 2026-09-19] Huawei is open-sourcing CANN, its in-house software equivalent to NVIDIA's CUDA, which is compatible with PyTorch.\\\\n    Quote: the company is also open-sourcing its in-house equivalent, CANN, already compatible with widely used tools like PyTorch.\\\\n- e5352 [third_party_view; supercarblondie.com; original source Wall Street analysts ; from gnews:01edb4d1fa96705133b29207 2026-09-19] Wall Street analysts expected NVIDIA total revenue of around $411 billion in FY2027.\\\\n    Quote: Wall Street analysts expect Nvidia to generate around $411 billion in revenue in fiscal 2027.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4375; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5355 [fact; fool.com author Daniel Sparks; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:5feec912090c2af6467eed38 2026-09-19] NVIDIA reported fiscal Q2 2027 revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year.\\\\n    Quote: Nvidia's revenue in the fiscal second quarter of 2027 (ended July 26) rose 106% year over year to $96.2 billion\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4630; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5363 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:e5b9c11e2c8ef9754946a897 2026-09-20] NVIDIA reported FY2027 second-quarter revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year.\\\\n    Quote: Nvidia grew revenue 106% year over year in the second quarter of fiscal 2027 (a period that ended July 26), reaching $96.2 billion.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3577; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5365 [third_party_view; Daniel Sparks; original source Daniel Sparks 2026-09-20; from gnews:e5b9c11e2c8ef9754946a897 2026-09-20] Daniel Sparks calculated that NVIDIA's year-over-year revenue growth accelerated for four consecutive quarters, from 62% to 73%, 85%, and 106% in FY2027's second quarter.\\\\n    Quote: The company's year-over-year revenue growth rate has now accelerated for four straight quarters, moving from 62% last fall to 73%, then 85%, and now 106%.\\\\n- e5368 [third_party_view; Daniel Sparks; original source Daniel Sparks 2026-09-20; from gnews:e5b9c11e2c8ef9754946a897 2026-09-20] Daniel Sparks judged that NVIDIA's current stock stall looked more like prior stalls that ended as revenue grew, citing accelerating revenue and a supply-limited FY2028 outlook.\\\\n    Quote: With revenue accelerating and next fiscal year's ceiling set by supply, today, I think, looks a lot more like the stalls the stock grew its way out of.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4696; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5378 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source finance.yahoo.com 2026-09-20; from gnews:a3d42b6d7a8a55a22f4a742b 2026-09-20] Some analyst models estimate that SpaceX accounts for approximately 5% of NVIDIA revenue; the models' period is not specified.\\\\n    Quote: According to some analyst models, SpaceX accounts for approximately 5% of NVIDIA's revenue.\\\\n- e5383 [party_statement; Cailian Press, reporting Nscale\\\\u2019s prospectus; original source Nscale ; from gnews:a7ac49717831582bc5bb87db 2026-09-20] Nscale said that at the end of August 2026 it had 7 MW of active capacity in its own data centers and 48 MW in leased space under contracts totaling $2.6 billion, with 1.3 GW of capacity being prepared.\\\\n    Quote: Nscale stated that, as of the end of August this year, its in-house data centers hosted 7 megawatts of active computing capacity, while an additional 48 megawatts were operating in leased data center space, under contracts totaling $2.6 billion. Furthermore, 1.3 gigawatts of capacity is currently being prepared.\\\\n- e5384 [fact; Cailian Press; original source Nscale and Anthropic ; from gnews:a7ac49717831582bc5bb87db 2026-09-20] Nscale signed a six-year agreement in August 2026 for Anthropic to lease capacity at Nscale\\\\u2019s West Virginia data center, valued at up to $45 billion.\\\\n    Quote: Last month, Nscale signed a landmark agreement with Anthropic to lease capacity at its flagship data center in West Virginia. The six-year deal is valued at up to $45 billion.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5250; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5385 [party_statement; Cailian Press, reporting Nscale\\\\u2019s estimate; original source Nscale ; from gnews:a7ac49717831582bc5bb87db 2026-09-20] Nscale estimated that its West Virginia data center, including a 2 GW gas-fired power plant, would cost about $70 billion and begin phased commissioning by the end of 2027.\\\\n    Quote: Nscale estimates that this data center, currently under construction, is expected to begin phased commissioning by the end of next year, with a total cost of approximately US$70 billion, including a 2 GW natural-gas-fired power plant to support its operations.\\\\n- e5386 [fact; TechRadar; original source Snap ; from gnews:77161fd7c5b3587babd3a661 2026-09-20] Snap is collaborating with NVIDIA to provide access to its open-source extended-reality AI platform for businesses developing immersive-device applications.\\\\n    Quote: Snap is collaborating with Nvidia for access to an open-source extended reality AI platform that businesses can use when developing applications for immersive devices.\\\\n- e109 [fact; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA\\\\u2019s Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenue in fiscal Q1 2027, equal to 92% of total sales.\\\\n    Quote: During the first quarter of fiscal 2027, the Data Center segment generated $75.25 billion in revenues, accounting for 92% of total sales.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e327, e1691, e1931; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e436 [fact; fool.com analyst; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dadd84590540a466aea01b3c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA reported $193.7 billion of Data Center revenue in FY2026.\\\\n    Quote: For comparison, Nvidia's data center revenue in fiscal 2026 (which ended in January this year) was $193.7 billion.\\\\n- e449 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source SK Hynix ; from gnews:c73b90b63a733c6ab712fcdd 2026-07-14] SK Hynix is slowing its HBM4 capacity ramp to redirect capacity to conventional DRAM, where shortages have pushed operating margins above HBM\\\\u2019s.\\\\n    Quote: SK Hynix is deliberately slowing its HBM4 ramp to redirect capacity into conventional DRAM, where shortages have pushed operating margins above HBM's.\\\\n- e1135 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:bdd09874d53aef7b27866d44 2026-07-26] SemiAnalysis forecast that NVIDIA's Data Center revenue in the second half of FY2027 would exceed analyst estimates by 20%.\\\\n    Quote: Even though SemiAnalysis reported the delays, it's still bullish on Nvidia, forecasting that the chipmaker's data center revenue will exceed analyst estimates by 20% in the second half of its fiscal 2027.\\\\n- e2295 [third_party_view; Morningstar (analyst); original source Morningstar 2026-08-19; from gnews:7ce47efd62fa17b9aa29e258 2026-08-19] Morningstar cites NVIDIA Data Center revenue of $3 billion in FY2020 and $194 billion in FY2026, and estimates $361 billion in FY2027, up 86% year over year.\\\\n    Quote: Nvidia\\\\u2019s DC business has achieved exponential growth already, rising from $3 billion in fiscal 2020 to $194 billion in fiscal 2026, and we estimate it will be $361 billion in fiscal 2027, representing 86% annual growth.\\\\n- e2635 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source Anthropic ; from gnews:093b9d63d05081b51dec3c77 2026-08-25] Anthropic plans to deploy up to 2 GW of AMD Instinct MI450 GPUs in Helios beginning in the first half of 2027; the deal could be worth tens of billions of dollars over time.\\\\n    Quote: Anthropic plans to deploy up to 2 gigawatts of the Instinct MI450 GPUs in its Helios system beginning in the first half of 2027 \\\\u2014 a deal that could be worth tens of billions of dollars over time.\\\\n- e2650 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from nvidianews:nvidia-announces-financial-results-for-second-quarter-fiscal-2027 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported Q2 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $89.0 billion, up 117% year over year.\\\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue of $89.0 billion, up 117% from a year ago\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2668; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e2681 [party_statement; NVIDIA; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from extra:2799d8731e89b90c9bd3f108 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said its Q3 FY2027 outlook assumes no Data Center compute revenue from China.\\\\n    Quote: NVIDIA is not assuming any Data Center compute revenue from China in its outlook.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e1639, e2715, e3045, e4450; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e2686 [fact; Colette Kress; original source Amazon Web Services 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] AWS plans to deploy an additional 2 million NVIDIA GPUs, along with Vera CPUs, from Q2 FY2027 through Q2 FY2029.\\\\n    Quote: AWS is deploying an additional 2 million GPUs starting this quarter through the second quarter of fiscal '29 along with Vera, CPUs, some integrated with Rubin, other standalone.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2664, e2787, e2878, e2879, e3056; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e2691 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA said customer forecasts indicate demand for its growth would double next year, while its supply-constrained revenue outlook is approximately 70% growth in FY2028.\\\\n    Quote: Customers forecasts point to our growth, doubling next year. However, as I mentioned earlier, we expect to grow approximately 70% as we are supply constrained.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2846, e2950, e2973, e3114, e3210, e3326, e5202; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e2720 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA guided Q3 FY2027 total revenue to $108 billion, plus or minus 2%.\\\\n    Quote: Total revenue is expected to be $108 billion, plus or minus 2%.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3400; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e2721 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA expects Vera Rubin to account for about 20% of Data Center revenue in Q3 FY2027.\\\\n    Quote: We see Vera Rubin accounting for about 20% of data center revenue in Q3.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2882, e3264, e3706, e4343; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e2723 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from edgar:NVDA:0001045810-26-000073:q2fy27cfocommentary.htm 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported Q2 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $89.0 billion, up 117% year over year and 18% sequentially, driven by the Blackwell Ultra ramp.\\\\n    Quote: Data Center revenue for the second quarter was a record $89.0 billion, up 117% from a year ago and up 18% sequentially, driven by the ramp of our Blackwell Ultra infrastructure.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2668, e2756, e2819, e2842, e3041, e3181; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e3399 [third_party_view; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Daniel Sparks 2026-08-28; from gnews:387b486b6e29491b9c8506df 2026-08-28] Daniel Sparks calculated that Data Center revenue rose from 87.9% of NVIDIA total revenue in fiscal Q2 2026 to 92.5% in fiscal Q2 2027, increasing each quarter in between.\\\\n    Quote: A year ago, in the second quarter of fiscal 2026, data center revenue was 87.9% of Nvidia's total. The share rose to 89.8% the next quarter, then 91.5%, then 92.2%, then 92.5% in the quarter just reported.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3707; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e3401 [third_party_view; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Daniel Sparks 2026-08-28; from gnews:387b486b6e29491b9c8506df 2026-08-28] Daniel Sparks calculated that Data Center revenue would be $99.9 billion in fiscal Q3 2027 if NVIDIA total revenue reaches its $108.0 billion guidance midpoint and Data Center remains 92.5% of the mix.\\\\n    Quote: Hold the data center mix at last quarter's 92.5%, and data center revenue works out to $99.9 billion -- about $100 million short of the line.\\\\n- e3406 [party_statement; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:387b486b6e29491b9c8506df 2026-08-28] NVIDIA said hyperscale-business growth should reaccelerate in fiscal Q4 2027 as Vera Rubin supply builds.\\\\n    Quote: And the company said growth in its hyperscale business (sales to the giant cloud computing providers and the biggest consumer internet companies) should reaccelerate in the fiscal fourth quarter as Vera Rubin supply builds.\\\\n- e4001 [third_party_view; theguardian.com; original source theguardian.com 2026-09-03; from gnews:774c4b3a90a519fc0d3c9024 2026-09-03] Meta, OpenAI and Microsoft are developing their own AI chips to reduce reliance on NVIDIA processors.\\\\n    Quote: For Nvidia, building up its open source business may help it cushion a demand slowdown from customers such as \\\\u2060Meta, OpenAI and Microsoft, which are developing their own AI chips to cut reliance \\\\u200bon its costly and \\\\u200bsupply-constrained processors.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4038; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e4202 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst), reporting Colette Kress's statement; original source Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO ; from gnews:bbd72d5fbff98d39746e6cb9 2026-09-04] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said NVIDIA could reach $40 billion in revenue per gigawatt of computing capacity installed with Vera Rubin, compared with about $25 billion with Blackwell and $18 billion with Hopper.\\\\n    Quote: Nvidia used to collect about $18 billion in revenue for every gigawatt of computing capacity it helped install with Hopper. With Blackwell, that figure rose to $25 billion. Kress says that with Vera Rubin, the company can reach $40 billion per gigawatt.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2887; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e4248 [party_statement; fool.com (Manali Pradhan); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:49351bd6de4706de524baf5f 2026-09-05] NVIDIA said it has improved visibility into memory and manufacturing capacity and the land, power, and data-center infrastructure needed for product deployment.\\\\n    Quote: However, this time, the company has much better visibility into memory and manufacturing capacity, as well as the land, power, and data-center infrastructure needed to deploy its products.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e4220 (); both are in force: NVIDIA warned that shortages of land, power, and other data-center infrastructure could delay customer hardware deployments.\\\\n- e4274 [third_party_view; calcalistech.com; original source calcalistech.com 2026-09-06; from gnews:478c25b436f87e8f421d54ed 2026-09-06] The article estimates NVIDIA FY2027 revenue at about $400 billion, up about 85% year over year.\\\\n    Quote: This year, however, revenue is expected to jump to about $400 billion, an increase of about 85% from the previous year.\\\\n- e4278 [third_party_view; calcalistech.com; original source calcalistech.com 2026-09-06; from gnews:478c25b436f87e8f421d54ed 2026-09-06] About 92% of NVIDIA revenue comes from data-center infrastructure, including chips and connectivity.\\\\n    Quote: Approximately 92% of Nvidia\\\\u2019s revenue comes from data center infrastructure, including chips and connectivity.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3797; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e4519 [party_statement; Trefis; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:fd039f68d65be67fc1005bcc 2026-09-09] NVIDIA's ACIE business\\\\u2014sovereign, NeoCloud and enterprise Data Center revenue\\\\u2014grew 138% year over year to $40 billion in fiscal Q2 2027.\\\\n    Quote: ACIE, the sovereign, NeoCloud and enterprise side of the data center business, grew 138% year over year to $40 billion in fiscal Q2 2027.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2875; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e4803 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:6ff9cd0726de49630ffec230 2026-09-12] In the second quarter, NVIDIA's ACIE customers grew 25% sequentially versus 13% growth from hyperscale cloud providers, and ACIE represented roughly half of Data Center revenue.\\\\n    Quote: During the second quarter, the ACIE segment delivered 25% sequential growth (versus 13% from the hyperscale cloud providers) and now represents roughly half of data center revenue.\\\\n- e4905 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:7708a5ba7485f4ee381ccc41 2026-09-14] NVIDIA reported an order backlog of more than $2 trillion in its Q2 release.\\\\n    Quote: as part of its Q2 release, NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA) outlined that its order backlog was more than $2 trillion.\\\\n- e5064 [third_party_view; Manali Pradhan, CFA; original source Manali Pradhan, CFA 2026-09-15; from gnews:9fd93b942948c5002e13eb0b 2026-09-15] Manali Pradhan estimated Vera Rubin systems would contribute about 20% of NVIDIA Data Center revenue in Q3 FY2027.\\\\n    Quote: Vera Rubin systems are expected to contribute about one-fifth of Nvidia's Data Center revenue in the third quarter.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3820; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5068 [third_party_view; Manali Pradhan, CFA; original source Manali Pradhan, CFA 2026-09-15; from gnews:9fd93b942948c5002e13eb0b 2026-09-15] Manali Pradhan said anticipated Q4 hyperscaler revenue reacceleration could mean less Q3 revenue upside from hyperscalers than from ACIE or other drivers.\\\\n    Quote: Additionally, since hyperscaler revenue is expected to reaccelerate in the fourth quarter, it may provide less upside to third-quarter revenue results than ACIE or other growth drivers.\\\\n- e5073 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source University of Manchester team ; from nvblog:uk-air-pollution-research-earth-2 2026-09-16] The University of Manchester team trained NVIDIA Earth-2 CorrDiff on Isambard-AI for UK air-quality forecasting.\\\\n    Quote: Working with the NVIDIA Earth-2 team, Topping and colleagues generated training data from existing chemistry-climate simulations, then trained Earth-2 CorrDiff \\\\u2014 a generative downscaling model \\\\u2014 on Isambard-AI, the U.K.\\\\u2019s national AI supercomputer in Bristol.\\\\n- e5079 [fact; finance.yahoo.com author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3f21db1f9791e20f80909da8 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported Q2 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $89.02 billion, up 117% year over year.\\\\n    Quote: Data Center alone at $89.02 billion, up 117%\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4065; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5109 [fact; Zacks.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:bc6926bf31d3a4d8006dce46 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $89 billion in fiscal Q2 2027, up 117% year over year and 18% sequentially.\\\\n    Quote: NVIDIA's Data Center business remains the primary growth driver, generating $89 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, up 117% from a year ago and 18% sequentially, according to the company's Aug. 26 press release.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5003; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5116 [fact; GuruFocus; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:d9a8cf969d7dedc50100397a 2026-09-16] NVIDIA Data Center revenue was $89 billion in its latest quarter, approximately 92.5% of total quarterly sales.\\\\n    Quote: Data-center revenue reached $89 billion , roughly 92.5% of Nvidia's latest quarterly sales,\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4208; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5176 [fact; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source Huawei ; from gnews:b92950ba2b0021244a331afa 2026-09-17] Huawei has shipped more than 1,000 supernode systems to over 370 customers.\\\\n    Quote: Huawei has already shipped more than 1,000 supernode systems to more than 370 customers.\\\\n- e5179 [third_party_view; Tom's Hardware, reporting C4ADS's findings; original source C4ADS ; from gnews:75cbbaecc2d997d4fa762033 2026-09-17] C4ADS reported that 56 Nvidia chips worth $1.7 million were sold to China through research-institution purchases from July 2025 to January 2026.\\\\n    Quote: C4ADS says that it tracked 56 chips worth $1.7 million sold this way in the report's July 2025 to January 2026 period.\\\\n- e5180 [third_party_view; Tom's Hardware, reporting C4ADS's findings; original source C4ADS ; from gnews:75cbbaecc2d997d4fa762033 2026-09-17] C4ADS reported that its 2024 investigation found $6.48 million worth of silicon heading to China through research-institution purchases across multiple years of government records.\\\\n    Quote: Additionally, it says that its 2024 investigation covering multiple years of government records revealed $6.48 million worth of silicon heading to China in this manner.\\\\n- e5181 [third_party_view; Tom's Hardware, reporting C4ADS's findings; original source C4ADS ; from gnews:75cbbaecc2d997d4fa762033 2026-09-17] C4ADS found $13.4 million of Nvidia A100, H100/GH100, and AD102-series GPUs routed through Vietnam, India, and Malaysia between 2022 and 2025.\\\\n    Quote: C4ADS analyzed transactions between 2022 and 2025, and found $13.4 million of Nvidia A100, H100/GH100, and AD102-series GPUs routed through the aforementioned countries, in a \\\\\\\"consistent pattern.\\\\\\\"\\\\n- e5182 [third_party_view; Tom's Hardware, reporting C4ADS's findings; original source C4ADS ; from gnews:75cbbaecc2d997d4fa762033 2026-09-17] C4ADS's data showed Hong Kong importer Profit New Limited traded $8.7 million of silicon in one day in March 2025, ahead of tighter export controls in April 2025.\\\\n    Quote: The former traded trading $8.7 million of silicon in a single day in March 2025, likely in preparation for April 2025's tightened export controls.\\\\n- e5183 [third_party_view; Tom's Hardware, reporting C4ADS's findings; original source C4ADS ; from gnews:75cbbaecc2d997d4fa762033 2026-09-17] C4ADS attributed $4.6 billion worth of Nvidia hardware imports into China to opaque ownership and shell-company activity involving Megaspeed International.\\\\n    Quote: According to C4ADS, this method accounted for $4.6 billion worth of intelligent sand migrating to China, on the account of just one entity, Megaspeed International.\\\\n- e5184 [third_party_view; Tom's Hardware, reporting an earlier Epoch AI estimate; original source Epoch AI ; from gnews:75cbbaecc2d997d4fa762033 2026-09-17] Epoch AI estimated that smuggled GPUs make up around one-third, and possibly most, of China's AI compute power.\\\\n    Quote: Another earlier report by Epoch AI estimates that around a third (and possibly most of) China's AI compute power is comprised of smuggled GPUs.\\\\n- e5185 [fact; gurufocus.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:509f491c104308dfdd480587 2026-09-17] NVIDIA Data Center revenue reached $89 billion in its latest reported quarter.\\\\n    Quote: Data-center revenue reached $89 billion\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4232; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5199 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:824eb11f9b37d2a3489d6e59 2026-09-18] NVIDIA reported second-quarter total revenue of $96 billion, up 106% year over year, and Data Center revenue of $89 billion, up 117% year over year.\\\\n    Quote: The company recently reported terrific second-quarter results, with revenue up 106% year over year to $96 billion, and revenue from data centers up 117% to $89 billion.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5124; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5218 [fact; uk.finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3742f4ebc0994af8eb404431 2026-09-18] NVIDIA Data Center revenue more than doubled to $89 billion in the second quarter.\\\\n    Quote: Data centre revenue more than doubled to $89bn\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2907; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5221 [fact; The Motley Fool author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:12a943c49b0c41542e6110b5 2026-09-18] NVIDIA's Data Center segment generated about $89 billion in revenue in the quarter ended July 26, 2026.\\\\n    Quote: About $89 billion of that came from its data center segment.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3398; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5227 [third_party_view; The Motley Fool author; original source The Motley Fool author 2026-09-18; from gnews:12a943c49b0c41542e6110b5 2026-09-18] The author used NVIDIA's roughly 70% FY2028 total-revenue growth outlook and its latest-quarter Data Center revenue of $89 billion as a proxy for AI revenue, reasoning that the segment is overwhelmingly driven by AI computing demand.\\\\n    Quote: Nvidia expects total revenue to grow about 70% in fiscal 2028, starting from an already enormous base of nearly $100 billion per quarter. The company does not report a stand-alone \\\\\\\"AI revenue\\\\\\\" figure, but data center revenue ($89 billion in the latest quarter) is a reasonable proxy, since that business is overwhelmingly driven by AI computing demand.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4717, e5295; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5263 [party_statement; benzinga.com, reporting Huang's CNBC interview; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:7218ec5f13c26358ef736b14 2026-09-18] Huang said NVIDIA Grace Blackwell systems rent for about $16 per GPU hour now, versus roughly $5 under some contracts signed a year earlier.\\\\n    Quote: Huang also pointed to rising rental prices as evidence of tight demand. He said NVIDIA Grace Blackwell systems can now rent for about $16 per GPU hour, compared with roughly $5 under some contracts signed a year ago.\\\\n- e5269 [party_statement; CRN, reporting Kapusta\\\\u2019s interview; original source Chris Kapusta, GDT 2026-09-17; from gnews:35efa49dae24bb21af438112 2026-09-18] GDT executive Chris Kapusta said GDT was selling AI infrastructure and related services to roughly 20 neoclouds.\\\\n    Quote: In a Thursday interview with CRN before the acquisition was announced , GDT executive Chris Kapusta said the Dallas-based solution provider has been selling AI infrastructure and related services to roughly 20 neoclouds, the new class of cloud services providers that almost exclusively focus on fulfilling demand for AI compute.\\\\n- e5270 [third_party_view; CRN; original source Gartner ; from gnews:35efa49dae24bb21af438112 2026-09-18] Gartner forecast that neoclouds would represent 20% of the $267 billion AI cloud market by 2030.\\\\n    Quote: According to research firm Gartner, neoclouds are expected to represent 20 percent of the $267 billion AI cloud market by 2030, underlining their competitiveness against hyperscalers.\\\\n- e5293 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA Corporation ; from gnews:d7c05e7b0777edd1a79bc806 2026-09-18] NVIDIA reported Q2 Data Center revenue of $89 billion, up 117% year over year.\\\\n    Quote: NVIDIA Corporation (NASDAQ:NVDA)'s data center revenue doubled to $89 billion in Q2 for a 117% bump\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4178; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5304 [third_party_view; Benzinga, reporting Brad Gerstner\\\\u2019s remarks at the All-In Summit; original source Brad Gerstner ; from gnews:4256ae7ea51b8cf4d4bb371b 2026-09-18] Brad Gerstner estimated that Anthropic, OpenAI and xAI had combined annualized revenue of roughly $100 billion based on July figures and need to reach at least $180 billion by year-end 2026.\\\\n    Quote: Gerstner estimated that Anthropic, OpenAI and SpaceX (NASDAQ: SPCX ), which owns xAI, had a combined run rate of roughly $100 billion based on figures circulating in July. Gerstner said the companies need to reach at least $180 billion by year-end, up about 80% from his July estimate, \\\\\\\"just to keep the AI trade intact.\\\\\\\"\\\\n- e5305 [rumour; Benzinga; original source Benzinga, reporting an unspecified source ; from gnews:4256ae7ea51b8cf4d4bb371b 2026-09-18] Anthropic\\\\u2019s reported revenue run rate was $65 billion in July 2026, up from $47 billion in May 2026.\\\\n    Quote: Anthropic's revenue run rate reportedly reached $65 billion in July, up from $47 billion in May.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2204; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5306 [third_party_view; Benzinga, reporting Brad Gerstner\\\\u2019s remarks at the All-In Summit; original source Brad Gerstner ; from gnews:4256ae7ea51b8cf4d4bb371b 2026-09-18] Brad Gerstner said Microsoft and Alphabet are building toward $1.5 trillion in annual capital expenditures, which requires AI-lab customers to pay for the capacity.\\\\n    Quote: \\\\\\\"If you're going to build a trillion and a half dollars a year in capex, somebody has to pay for it,\\\\\\\" he said.\\\\n- e5309 [fact; Harsh Chauhan, fool.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ad94c78d09fe41fc3f29bbca 2026-09-18] NVIDIA reported $164 billion of Data Center segment revenue in the first six months of FY2027.\\\\n    Quote: The company has generated $164 billion in revenue from its data center segment in the first six months of fiscal 2027.\\\\n- e5310 [third_party_view; Harsh Chauhan, fool.com; original source Harsh Chauhan 2026-09-18; from gnews:ad94c78d09fe41fc3f29bbca 2026-09-18] The author calculated that NVIDIA\\\\u2019s first-six-month FY2027 Data Center revenue implies a full-year run rate of just under $330 billion.\\\\n    Quote: That translates into an annual run rate of just under $330 billion for the full year.\\\\n- e5312 [fact; Zacks.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:57a69374b8fa083ce36ecfb1 2026-09-18] NVIDIA Data Center revenue was $89 billion in FY2027 Q2, up 117% year over year and 18% sequentially.\\\\n    Quote: The Data Center business remained the key growth driver, with revenues rising 117% year over year and 18% sequentially to $89 billion.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5003; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5356 [fact; fool.com author Daniel Sparks; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:5feec912090c2af6467eed38 2026-09-19] NVIDIA reported $89 billion of Data Center revenue in fiscal Q2 2027.\\\\n    Quote: with $89 billion of that coming from data centers.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e3398; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5364 [fact; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:e5b9c11e2c8ef9754946a897 2026-09-20] NVIDIA reported FY2027 second-quarter Data Center revenue of $89.0 billion, up 117% year over year.\\\\n    Quote: Data center revenue climbed 117% to $89.0 billion.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4848; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n\\\\n[Themes in force, 7]\\\\n- v16 (chip-export-controls, due 2026-12-31) Will the U.S. Senate pass the Remote Access Security Act by December 31, 2026?: now rung 2 No; judged 2026-08-19; reasons: No market consensus is supplied. The deadline reference is passage by December 31, 2026 (rung 1); the alternative is that the Senate has not passed RASA by then (rung 2). RASA had passed the House but was still awaiting Senate action on July 23, and the August 19 report says it had still not passed.\\\\n- v22 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will Taiwan\\\\u2019s Ministry of Economic Affairs adopt performance-threshold export controls for advanced chips by January 31, 2027?: now rung 2 No; judged 2026-07-28; reasons: The reference is rung 2: no formal adoption by the deadline is indicated in the available plan or timeline. The consultations and reported consideration make adoption more plausible than before, but the Ministry set no timeline; that evidence does not make formal adoption by January 31, 2027 the mor\\\\n- v26 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will Taiwan adopt a criminal ban on all AI chip exports to China by January 31, 2027?: now rung 1 No; judged 2026-07-29; reasons: The reference is rung 1: the supplied evidence says Taiwan is considering a ban, not that it has adopted one. That consideration, in the context of an investigation into suspected smuggling, raises the prospect of action, but the evidence gives no adopted measure, legislative stage, or timetable. Th\\\\n- v27 (chip-export-controls, due 2026-12-31) Will the U.S. Department of Commerce conclude its investigation into Chinese firms\\\\u2019 access to advanced U.S. chips by December 31, 2026?: now rung 2 No; judged 2026-08-07; reasons: The reference is rung 2 (No): no market consensus or Commerce completion deadline is supplied, and the stated status is a formal investigation, not a scheduled conclusion. The evidence makes non-conclusion by December 31, 2026 more likely: Commerce is still examining access through computing capacit\\\\n- v6 (ai-capex, due 2027-02-28) How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?: now rung 4 $700 billion to below $800 billion; judged 2026-09-19; reasons: The market reference for the four companies is roughly $720\\\\u2013745 billion, which sits in rung 4. The evidence implies about $760 billion for the four: the direct four-company estimate is $760 billion, and the later Amazon and Alphabet figures are consistent with company spending plans already reflecte\\\\n- v7 (ai-capex, due 2028-02-29) How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?: now rung 4 $1.1 trillion to below $1.2 trillion; judged 2026-09-19; reasons: The market reference is BofA's $1.08 trillion 2027 estimate for five companies; using the carried Oracle adjustment of roughly $100\\\\u2013$150 billion, the four-company reference is about $930\\\\u2013$980 billion, in rung 3. NVIDIA's $1.3 trillion forecast for the top five, adjusted by the same Oracle amount, im\\\\n- v9 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will China authorize purchases of Nvidia H200 chips by AI companies by January 31, 2027?: now rung 2 Yes; judged 2026-09-20; updated since this thesis was last judged; reasons: The reference is rung 1: no Chinese authorization by the deadline. The evidence favors a narrow, selective authorization by January 31, 2027, rather than no authorization: reports name prospective buyers, and one item says limited H200 imports were recently allowed. This is not a forecast of broad a\\\\n\\\\nAnswer per the JSON schema: one calculation for the family and one answer per member.\\\",\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/paid-plan.json:5026:  \\\"user\\\": \\\"[Family] members:\\\\nThesis v8 (NVDA, asset, focus \\\\\\\"NVIDIA Data Center segment revenue in FY2027\\\\\\\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\\\\nLadder: rung 1 Strongly bullish: FY2027 Data Center revenue is at least $400 billion. / rung 2 Bullish: FY2027 Data Center revenue is at least $350 billion and less than $400 billion. / rung 3 Neutral: FY2027 Data Center revenue is at least $300 billion and less than $350 billion. / rung 4 Bearish: FY2027 Data Center revenue is at least $250 billion and less than $300 billion. / rung 5 Strongly bearish: FY2027 Data Center revenue is less than $250 billion.\\\\n\\\\nRelations: none.\\\\nShared quantities, one forecast each per scenario: NVIDIA, revenue, company, FY2027 Q3; NVIDIA, revenue, company, FY2027 Q4.\\\\nOutcome keys (population | measure | scope | period), to be used exactly: v8 = NVIDIA | revenue | Data Center | FY2027.\\\\n\\\\n[Evidence in view for the family, 237 items]\\\\n- e111 [fact; tradingview.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:25d0b1d2a9dfe0bb99432e1a 2026-07-06] NVIDIA reported fiscal Q1 2027 revenue of $81.62 billion, up 85% year over year.\\\\n    Quote: First-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues climbed 85% year over year to $81.62 billion, while non-GAAP earnings per share jumped 140% to $1.87.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e273, e274, e326, e478, e1401, e1425; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e1040 [fact; 247wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source OpenAI ; from gnews:4f1770366917aea8eed6ae4c 2026-07-24] OpenAI selected AMD to deploy 6 GW of GPUs, a planned deployment that could affect NVIDIA's competitive position in AI accelerators.\\\\n    Quote: OpenAI selected AMD to deploy 6 gigawatts of GPUs\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e914, e1243; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e1041 [fact; 247wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source Meta ; from gnews:4f1770366917aea8eed6ae4c 2026-07-24] Meta signed for a deployment of up to 6 GW of AMD Instinct GPUs, a competing accelerator commitment relevant to NVIDIA's FY2027 revenue outlook.\\\\n    Quote: Meta signed for up to 6 gigawatts of Instinct GPUs\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e571; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e1510 [third_party_view; insidermonkey.com; original source insidermonkey.com 2026-07-31; from gnews:39deea97b690ac7b56dada0b 2026-07-31] NVIDIA has roughly $1 trillion in confirmed Blackwell and Vera Rubin chip orders through 2027.\\\\n    Quote: The company already has roughly $1 trillion in confirmed orders for its Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips through 2027,\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e272; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e2452 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:835fa8a6ac898ca3973d586c 2026-08-23] NVIDIA guided to $65 billion in Q4 FY2026 revenue and reported actual revenue of $68 billion.\\\\n    Quote: For Q4 FY 2026, Nvidia expected $65 billion in revenue; it ended up producing $68 billion.\\\\n- e2649 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from nvidianews:nvidia-announces-financial-results-for-second-quarter-fiscal-2027 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported Q2 FY2027 revenue of $96.2 billion, up 18% quarter over quarter and 106% year over year.\\\\n    Quote: NVIDIA (NASDAQ: NVDA) today reported revenue for the second quarter ended July 26, 2026, of $96.2 billion, up 18% from the previous quarter and up 106% from a year ago.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2667, e4536; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e2652 [party_statement; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from nvidianews:nvidia-announces-financial-results-for-second-quarter-fiscal-2027 2026-08-26] NVIDIA guided Q3 FY2027 revenue to $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%, with no Data Center compute revenue