ews:3f2255dadc23c13fcdfe5ef3 2026-09-16] IREN plans to scale AI Cloud capacity to 480 MW by the end of 2026, supported by its GPU financing facility.\\\\n    Quote: It underpins IREN's goal of scaling to 480MW of AI Cloud capacity by the end of 2026, and ties directly into the same theme as the Nvidia partnership: aggressive, contract-backed expansion.\\\\n- e5099 [party_statement; benzinga.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:906d80c706aa948ee141e852 2026-09-16] Jensen Huang said roughly $400 billion of venture financing flowed into AI companies over six months, creating demand for compute and data centers.\\\\n    Quote: Huang said roughly $400 billion in venture financing flowed into AI companies over six months, creating jobs and massive demand for compute, which is subsequently driving demand for data centers.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2791; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5100 [fact; fool.com (author); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:147e79a4a1f10279da449944 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported $27.0 billion of revenue billed to Taiwan-headquartered customers in fiscal Q2 2027, 28% of quarterly revenue.\\\\n    Quote: During the fiscal second quarter of 2027 (the period ended July 26), $27.0 billion of Nvidia's revenue was billed to customers headquartered in Taiwan. That's 28% of the quarter's $96.2 billion total.\\\\n- e5101 [fact; fool.com (author); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:147e79a4a1f10279da449944 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported $8.9 billion of revenue billed to Taiwan-headquartered customers in fiscal Q2 2026, about 19% of quarterly revenue.\\\\n    Quote: A year earlier, it was $8.9 billion, or about 19%\\\\n- e5102 [fact; fool.com (author); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:147e79a4a1f10279da449944 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported about $12 billion of revenue billed to Taiwan-headquartered customers in the preceding quarter, roughly 15% of quarterly revenue.\\\\n    Quote: Three months before the latest quarter, it was about $12 billion, or roughly 15%.\\\\n- e5103 [fact; fool.com (author); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:147e79a4a1f10279da449944 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported fiscal Q2 2027 revenue billed to customers headquartered in the United States of $60.1 billion, Taiwan of $27.0 billion, China including Hong Kong of $7.9 billion, and the rest of the world of $1.3 billion.\\\\n    Quote: On that basis, the United States led the fiscal second quarter at $60.1 billion, or about 62% of revenue. Taiwan came second at $27.0 billion. China, including Hong Kong, contributed $7.9 billion, and the rest of the world combined for just $1.3 billion.\\\\n- e5104 [fact; fool.com (author); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:147e79a4a1f10279da449944 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported that customers headquartered outside the U.S. accounted for 38% of revenue in fiscal Q2 2027, versus 30% in fiscal Q2 2026.\\\\n    Quote: Altogether, customers headquartered outside the U.S. accounted for 38% of the quarter's revenue, against 30% a year earlier.\\\\n- e5105 [fact; fool.com (author); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:147e79a4a1f10279da449944 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported total revenue of $96.2 billion in fiscal Q2 2027, up 106% year over year, with about 92% from Data Center.\\\\n    Quote: Companywide revenue totaled $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year, and about 92% of it came from the data center business.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4244; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e5106 [fact; fool.com (author); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:147e79a4a1f10279da449944 2026-09-16] One direct customer accounted for 16% of NVIDIA's total revenue, approximately $15 billion, in fiscal Q2 2027.\\\\n    Quote: One direct customer accounted for 16% of Nvidia's total revenue in the quarter -- about $15 billion billed to a single buyer.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the