ed-forward market estimate is about $372.5 billion, in rung 2 ($350 billion to less than $400 billion).'), ('v8', '2026-07-31', 2630, 'The carried-forward market estimate is about $372.5 billion, which sits in rung 2 ($350 billion to less than $400 billion).'), ('v1', '2026-08-02', 2692, 'No aggregate market consensus or NVIDIA guidance is supplied, so there is no external reference figure to place on the ladder. The carried base case of roughly $10–11 billion is in rung 4.'), ('v8', '2026-08-02', 2694, 'Analyst consensus is the reference; no numeric consensus is supplied in the current evidence. The carried comparison places it below the implied outcome, most consistently on rung 2 ($350bn to below $400bn).'), ('v1', '2026-08-03', 2728, 'No aggregate market consensus or NVIDIA guidance for total FY2027 credit-support obligations is supplied. The carried base estimate of about $10–11 billion is the available reference and sits in rung 4; the reported $250 billion Ohio proposal is not itself an established reference for committed obligations.'), ('v1', '2026-08-05', 2808, 'No aggregate market consensus or NVIDIA guidance for total FY2027 credit-support commitments is supplied. The carried base estimate of about $10–11 billion is rung 4; the reported $250 billion Ohio guarantee headline, if fully committed, would be in rung 5, but is not the most reliable reference for the committed amount by the due date.'), ('v8', '2026-08-05', 2805, 'Analyst consensus; no numeric figure is supplied in this view. The carried comparison places the reference most consistently in rung 2 ($350bn to below $400bn).'), ('v1', '2026-08-06', 2871, 'No explicit market consensus or aggregate NVIDIA guidance is supplied. The carried non-Ohio estimate of about $10–11 billion is rung 4; the carried estimate including a discounted Ohio contribution is about $20–21 billion, rung 5. The reported $250 billion Ohio figure, if taken in full, would also be rung 5 but is not the reference forecast used here.'), ('v8', '2026-08-09', 2975, 'Analyst consensus, as described in the previous conclusion, is $350bn to below $400bn: rung 2. No exact consensus estimate is supplied.'), ('v8', '2026-08-25', 4589, \\\\\\\"The carried-forward analyst-consensus reference is $350 billion to below $400 billion, rung 2. Morningstar's FY2027 estimate of $361 billion is likewise rung 2.\\\\\\\")] [('v8', '2026-08-09', 2975, 'Analyst consensus, as described in the previous conclusion, is $350bn to below $400bn: rung 2. No exact consensus estimate is supplied.'), ('v8', '2026-08-25', 4589, \\\\\\\"The carried-forward analyst-consensus reference is $350 billion to below $400 billion, rung 2. Morningstar's FY2027 estimate of $361 billion is likewise rung 2.\\\\\\\"), ('v8', '2026-08-26', 5093, \\\\\\\"Analyst consensus carried forward from the previous judgement is $350 billion to below $400 billion, rung 2. Morningstar's $361 billion FY2027 estimate is also in rung 2.\\\\\\\"), ('v8', '2026-08-27', 5304, \\\\\\\"The carried-forward market consensus is $350 billion to below $400 billion, which is rung 2; Morningstar's specific $361 billion FY2027 estimate is also rung 2.\\\\\\\")]\\\\ncontrol 2 v6 2026-09-19 [Decimal('1190.00'), Decimal('730'), Decimal('800'), Decimal('1300.0')] [('1190.00', False), ('730', True), ('800', True), ('1300.0', True)] [Decimal('1080.00'), Decimal('900'), Decimal('1100.0')]\\\\ncontrol 2 v14 2026-09-20 [Decimal('419'), Decimal('81.6'), Decimal('96.2'), Decimal('113.5'), Decimal('110.16'), Decimal('127')] [('419', False), ('81.6', True), ('96.2', True), ('113.5', True), ('110.16', True), ('127', False)] [Decimal('411'), Decimal('400'), Decimal('450'), Decimal('215.9'), Decimal('405')]\\\\ncontrol 2 v9 2026-09-20 [Decimal('410'), Decimal('164'), Decimal('100'), Decimal('108'), Decimal('146')] [('410', False), ('164', True), ('100', True), ('108', True), ('146', False)] [Decimal('414'), Decimal('400'), Decimal('450')]\\\\ncontrol 2 v29 2026-09-20 [Decimal('53'), D