j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''reference'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''reasons'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''])\\\\n  for e in raw['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''cites'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']:\\\\n   if tag(ed[e],r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''70%|(?:396|419|660|680) billion'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):print(ed[e][:720])\\\\n eids={r[0] for r in v.execute('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''select evidence_id from evidence_links where view_id=?'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',(id,))}\\\\n if id=='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v9'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':left=eids;le=set(ed);lc=set(raw['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''cites'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''])\\\\n if id=='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v14'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':print('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''overlap'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',len(left),len(eids),len(left&eids),len(le&set(ed)),len(lc&set(raw['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''cites'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''])))\\\\nfor j in v.execute(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"select * from judgements where view_id in ('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v14'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v9'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'') and publication_day='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''2026-09-20'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"):\\\\n d,raw=req(a,j); ed=evidence(user(d));r=figures(j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''implied_outcome'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')\\\\n print(j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''view_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''ladder'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',list(map(tuple,v.execute(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"select position,lo,hi from rungs where view_id=?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",(j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''view_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],)))))\\\\n for e in ed.values():\\\\n  if (j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''view_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']=='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v9'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'' and bool({D(414),D(146)}&set(figures(e,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')))) or (j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''view_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']=='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v14'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'' and e.startswith('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''- e3943 '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')):print(e[:1000])\\\\n'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"2 v9 7939 161 2\\\\n2 v9 8046 143 3\\\\n2 v14 8729 119 2\\\\n2 v9 8737 123 2\\\\n2 v29 8734 35 3\\\\n2 v6 8595 31 4\\\\n3 v3 9183 200 1\\\\n3 v41 9166 15 3\\\\n3 v35 9177 69 2\\\\nRELATED\\\\noverlap 1287 1329 106 5 0\\\\nv21 8730 Q1 and Q2 revenue plus the Q3 guidance midpoint total $285.8 billion; extending the approximately 12% sequential growth implied by Q3 guidance into Q4 gives about $121 billion, or approximately $407 billion for FY2027. Against FY2026 revenue of $215.94 billion, that implies about 88% growth; the CFO's approximately 70% full-year outlook is a lower check, implying about $367 billion, but also falls in rung 1. Wall Street's current FY2027 growth expectations are about 87–90% (Zacks: 87.4–88%; $411 billion revenue implies about 90% versus FY2026), placing the reference at rung 1. The ladder's cited 42% estimate is not the current market reference. The market reference is roughly 87–90% FY2027 growth (Zacks estimates 87.4–88%, while the $411 billion estimate implies about 90% against FY2026 revenue), which is rung 1; the ladder's cited 42% estimate is not the current reference. Q1 and Q2 revenue plus Q3 guidance total $285.8 billion. Carrying forward the approximately 12% sequential growth implied by Q3 guidance gives Q4 revenue of about $121 billion, FY2027 revenue near $407 billion, and growth of about 88% from FY2026's $215.94 billion. The CFO's approximately 70% growth outlook implies about $367 billion, also rung 1. Supplier constraints temper the faster run-rate case, but the reported results and Q3 guide still imply growth well above the 60% boundary.\\\\n- e3108 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source Colette Kress 2026-08-26; from gnews:b39d8c4b1f73b622347a66e4 2026-08-28] CFO Colette Kress guided to 70% growth for NVIDIA revenue for the full fiscal year; the article says this was ahead of analyst estimates.\\\\n    Quote: As if this weren't enough, Kress guided 70% growth for the full fiscal year, which was ahead of analyst estimates.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4226, e4227, e4386, e4400, e4913; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e4900 [party_statement; crn.com; original source Colette Kress, NVIDIA CFO ; from gnews:3a284e233d8b31c62dc66b33 2026-09-18] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said NVIDIA expected revenue to grow approximately 70% next year because of supply constraints.\\\\n    Quote: we expect to grow approximately 70 percent as we are supply constrained.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4400; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\nv35 8732 About $671–$678 billion: NVIDIA's 70% FY2028 growth outlook implies about $673 billion, analyst estimates put FY2028 at $678 billion, and applying Zacks' 63.2% growth estimate to the cited $411 billion FY2027 base gives about $671 billion. Analyst consensus of about $678 billion for FY2028 (e4348), which is rung 2. Zacks' 63.2% FY2028 growth estimate (e4703), applied to the cited $411 billion FY2027 estimate, implies about $671 billion and is also in rung 2. The market reference is analyst consensus of about $678 billion for FY2028, which sits at rung 2. The current implied outcome remains around $671–$678 billion: NVIDIA's 70% outlook is about $673 billion, while the analyst forecast is $678 billion; applying Zacks' 63.2% growth estimate to the cited $411 billion FY2027 estimate gives about $671 billion. These figures remain below the $700 billion rung-1 boundary. Chip-volume and customer-demand evidence, together with favorable export-control and capex themes, support the upper end, but supply and infrastructure constraints, earlier Huawei launches, and memory tightness temper the upside; none supplies a quantified revision that takes FY2028 revenue across $700 billion.\\\\n- e4859 [party_statement; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f94df9a4bc981f0c32ba5797 2026-09-17] NVIDIA forecast 70% total revenue growth, to about $673 billion, in the fiscal year ending January 2028 (FY2028).\\\\n    Quote: It's the latest forecast from Nvidia that points to continuing massive growth for the next six quarters, and comes shortly after the company revealed that it expected 70% growth in the fiscal year ending in January 2028, or about $673 billion, which caused analyst expectations to shoot up.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4043, e4919, e4926; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e4858 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, quoted by CNBC; original source Jensen Huang 2026-09-17; from gnews:f94df9a4bc981f0c32ba5797 2026-09-17] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang forecast that NVIDIA would sell twice as many chips in 2027 as in 2026.\\\\n    Quote: \\\\\\\"I expect Nvidia to sell twice as many chips as this next year as we do this year,\\\\\\\" Huang told the media before a summit with King Charles III in Scotland.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4860, e4922; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e2800 (2026-08-26); both are in force: NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said available supply supported 70% growth in 20\\\\nv17 8725 Approximately 70% FY2028 revenue growth, or about $673 billion using the cited roughly $396 billion FY2027 base. This follows NVIDIA’s explicit supply-constrained outlook; the forecast of twice as many chips sold in calendar 2027 is supportive but does not supply a directly comparable FY2028 revenue-growth figure. NVIDIA’s approximately 70% FY2028 growth guidance is the primary reference and is rung 1. Analyst expectations of 63.2%–65.5% are also rung 1; the LSEG-tracked 44% estimate is a rung-3 counterestimate. The company’s approximately 70% FY2028 growth guidance is the primary reference and sits at rung 1; the more recent analyst estimates of 63.2%–65.5% also sit at rung 1, while the 44% LSEG estimate is a rung-3 counterweight. The implied outcome remains about 70%: NVIDIA says supply supports that growth, while demand is higher. The newer forecast of twice as many chips sold in calendar 2027 supports strong volume but does not translate directly into FY2028 revenue growth or displace the company’s supply-constrained outlook. The implied outcome stays above the 60% rung boundary.\\\\n- e2532 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA expects total revenue to grow approximately 70% in FY2028, with supply constraining the outlook.\\\\n    Quote: We expect to grow revenue by approximately 70% in fiscal 2028. This is a supply-constrained outlook.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2630, e2787, e3155; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e2697 [third_party_view; CNBC; original source CNBC 2026-08-26; from gnews:6ac7c90b82734575d8de60bf 2026-08-26] CNBC calculated that NVIDIA revenue would reach $673 billion in FY2028 if FY2027 revenue is $396 billion, the consensus projection.\\\\n    Quote: Based on the consensus projection for revenue of $396 billion for fiscal 2027, which ends in January, sales next year would hit $673 billion.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2421; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e3759 [third_party_view; Yahoo Finance; original source Yahoo Finance 2026-09-02; from gnews:e0b66adc8bcdc7a1b971cda0 2026-09-02] Yahoo Finance analyst estimates showed average Street expectations of 63% NVIDIA revenue growth in FY2028, versus the company’s 70% guidance.\\\\n    Quote: Yahoo Finance analyst estimates show the Street modeling 63% year-over-year revenue growth for Nvidia in fiscal year 2028 on average, below the 70% target it just guided to.\\\\n- e4066 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:0af492eafa8a1c2529e56b7c 2026-09-06] NVIDIA management said its 70% FY2028 revenue-growth outlook reflects supply constraints, primarily memory shortages, rather than a limit on demand, and excludes China Data Center revenue.\\\\n    Quote: Management said the 70% figure shows supply constraints, primarily memory component shortages, rather than a ceiling on actual demand, and the outlook excludes China data center revenue.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2911; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n- e4858 [party_statement; Jensen Huang, quoted by CNBC; original source Jensen Huang 2026-09-17; from gnews:f94df9a4bc981f0c32ba5797 2026-09-17] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang forecast that NVIDIA would sell twice as many chips in 2027 as in 2026.\\\\n    Quote: \\\\\\\"I expect Nvidia to sell twice as many chips as this next year as we do this year,\\\\\\\" Huang told the media before a summit with King Charles III in Scotland.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4860, e4922; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e2800 (2026-08-26); both are in force: NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang said available supply supported 70% growth in 20\\\\n- e4859 [party_statement; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f94df9a4bc981f0c32ba5797 2026-09-17] NVIDIA forecast 70% total revenue growth, to about $673 billion, in the fiscal year ending January 2028 (FY2028).\\\\n    Quote: It's the latest forecast from Nvidia that points to continuing massive growth for the next six quarters, and comes shortly after the company revealed that it expected 70% growth in the fiscal year ending in January 2028, or about $673 billion, which caused analyst expectations to shoot up.\\\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4043, e4919, e4926; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\\\\nv14 ladder [(1, 450000000000.0, None), (2, 400000000000.0, 450000000000.0), (3, 350000000000.0, 400000000000.0), (4, 300000000000.0, 350000000000.0), (5, None, 300000000000.0)]\\\\n- e3943 [party_statement; The Motley Fool author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:89698c9955cf8aa35b642970 2026-09-04] NVIDIA's FY2027 Q3 guidance implied total revenue growth of 12% sequentially at the midpoint.\\\\n    Quote: In the meantime, Nvidia's fiscal 2027 third-quarter guidance implies 12% sequential growth at the midpoint.\\\\nv9 ladder [(1, 450000000000.0, None), (2, 400000000000.0, 450000000000.0), (3, 350000000000.0, 400000000000.0), (4, 300000000000.0, 350000000000.0), (5, None, 300000000000.0)]\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r45.stream:85:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_44\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,json,pathlib,re,collections,decimal\\\\nD=decimal.Decimal\\\\ndef db(i,name='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''views'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):\\\\n c=sqlite3.connect((pathlib.Path(f'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{i}/prod'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')/(name+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.sqlite'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')).resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',uri=True)\\\\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\\\\n return c\\\\ndef req(a,j):\\\\n c=a.execute('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''select * from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',(j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],)).fetchone()\\\\n assert c and c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']==j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] and c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''purpose'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']=='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''judge'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',dict(j)\\\\n d=json.loads(c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''request_json'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''])\\\\n return d,json.loads(c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''answer_json'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''])\\\\nEVID=re.compile(r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\"'^- (e'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\[.*?(?=\\\\\\\"'^- e'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+ \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\[|\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Z)'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',re.M|re.S)\\\\ndef evidence(t):\\\\n b=t.split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''[Evidence in view under this thesis, '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[0]\\\\n m=dict((x.group(1),x.group(0).strip()) for x in EVID.finditer(b))\\\\n assert len(m)==int(b.split()[0]),(len(m),b[:20])\\\\n return m\\\\ndef user(d):\\\\n return next(m['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''content'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] for m in d['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''messages'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] if m['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''role'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']=='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''user'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')\\\\nUNIT=r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''(?:trillion(?:s)?|billions?|millions?|bn|mm|[BTM]|%|percent(?:age points?)?)'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\nNUM=r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+(?:,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d{3})*(?:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+)?'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\nFIG=re.compile(rf'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''(?<\\\\\\\"'!['\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\w.])(?P<sign>[+−-])?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'$?'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*(?P<lo>{NUM})(?:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*[-–—]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'$?'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*(?P<hi>{NUM}))?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*(?P<unit>{UNIT})(?\\\\\\\"'![a-zA-Z0-9])'\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',re.I)\\\\nMULT={'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''trillion'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''trillions'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''t'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''billion'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''billions'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''bn'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''b'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''million'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''millions'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''mm'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''m'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')}\\\\ndef figures(t,unit):\\\\n out=[]\\\\n for m in FIG.finditer(t or '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):\\\\n  u=m['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''unit'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''].lower()\\\\n  if (u in MULT)\\\\\\\"'!=(unit=='\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):continue\\\\n  mult=MULT.get(u,1)\\\\n  if m['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''sign'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] in ('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''-'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''−'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):mult=-mult\\\\n  for g in ('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''lo'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''hi'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):\\\\n   if m[g]:out.append(D(m[g].replace('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''))*mult)\\\\n return out\\\\ndef snippets(ed):\\\\n return [re.split(r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (?:It replaces|Opinion, not verified:)'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',b,1)[0].split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[1] for b in ed.values()]\\\\ndef prior_text(t):\\\\n return t.split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''[Previous conclusion'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nAnswer per'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[0].split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[1]\\\\ndef tag(x,pattern): return bool(re.search(pattern,x or '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',re.I))\\\\ndef record(i):\\\\n v=db(i);a=db(i,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''archive'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')\\\\n return (v,a,v.execute(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"select j.*,k.unit from judgements j join view_keys k using(view_id) where k.unit in ('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''percent'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'') order by judgement_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"))\\\\nfor i,caps in {1:['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v4'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v8'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v5'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v7'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],2:['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v14'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v9'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v21'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v17'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''v35'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\