omer demand supports a modest uplift, discounted for uncertain timing and conversion to NVIDIA revenue.\\\\n2026-08-17 3603 3608 About $389 billion: add reported Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion and guided Q2 revenue of $91 billion, then carry 12% sequential growth into Q3 (about $101.9 billion) and Q4 (about $114.1 billion). The resulting roughly $388.7 billion is below the $400 billion rung boundary. | About $448B. The Q2 guide and acceleration commentary, SemiAnalysis's H2 FY2027 tracking, and stronger demand/capex signals lift the prior ~$445B estimate modestly; I discount SpaceX's end-2027 target and OpenAI capacity phased in from 2028 for limited FY2027 contribution.\\\\n2026-08-18 3742 3747 About $391 billion: $81.6 billion Q1 actual plus $91 billion Q2 guidance, $103.1 billion expected for Q3, and about $115.5 billion for Q4 by carrying roughly 12% sequential growth from Q3. This is below $400 billion and therefore rung 3. | Approximately $448B. Carrying FY2026 Data Center revenue of $193.7B forward at FY2027 Q1's 92% year-over-year growth gives about $372B; the Q2 guide and acceleration commentary, together with the cited H2 tracking, support an estimate above that baseline, but the quantified SpaceX and OpenAI capacity is largely outside FY2027.\\\\n2026-08-19 3862 3874 Approximately $406 billion: use $81.6 billion reported in Q1, BofA's $94–95 billion Q2 expectation and $107–108 billion potential Q3 guidance, then carry roughly 14% sequential growth into Q4 (about $122 billion). | About $448B: FY2026 Data Center revenue of $193.7B carried forward at Q1 FY2027’s 92% year-over-year growth implies about $372B, with the Q2 growth-acceleration outlook and SemiAnalysis’s H2 estimate supporting a higher full-year figure. The estimate remains just below $450B.\\\\n2026-08-21 3989 3993 Using BofA's $94–95 billion Q2 estimate and potential $107–108 billion Q3 guidance, their midpoints imply about 13.7% sequential growth; carrying that rate into Q4 gives roughly $122 billion. Adding reported Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion implies approximately $406 billion for FY2027. | About $448B: carry the $193.7B FY2026 Data Center base forward at the reported 92% year-over-year growth rate (about $372B), then incorporate the previously in-force H2 SemiAnalysis estimate of revenue 20% above analyst estimates, alongside the $75.25B Q1 result and Q2 guidance for approximately $91B total revenue with accelerating Data Center growth. This remains below $450B.\\\\n2026-08-22 4030 4029 About $405–406 billion: start with reported Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion, use an upside-tilted Q2 estimate of roughly $94–95 billion against the $91 billion company guide, then use BofA's $107–108 billion Q3 expectation and carry the Q2-to-Q3 sequential growth rate into Q4 (about $122 billion). | About $448B for FY2027: the FY2026 baseline carried forward with the reported growth trajectory, then supported by Q1 FY2027 Data Center revenue of $75.25B, management's accelerating-growth commentary and Q2 guide, and SemiAnalysis's H2 estimate. This is below $450B and above $400B.\\\\n2026-08-23 4090 4088 About $411 billion: $81.6 billion reported in Q1, approximately $95 billion in Q2, approximately $109 billion in Q3, and about $125 billion in Q4 by carrying roughly 15% sequential growth from Q2 to Q3 forward. The Q2/Q3 estimates are forecasts, not reported outcomes; the Q3 calculation discounts the more speculative $112 billion estimate against lower consensus and BofA estimates. | About $448B for FY2027. This carries forward the reported FY2026 base using the strong FY2027 Q1 growth rate, while incorporating Q1 Data Center revenue of $75.25B, management's approximately $91B total-revenue Q2 guide and accelerating Data Center growth commentary, plus SemiAnalysis's forecast for H2 Data Center revenue to exceed analyst estimates by 20%.\\\\n2026-08-25 4433 4437 Approximately $408 billion: $81.6 billion reported in Q1, about $94–95 billion for Q2, about $107–108 billion for Q3, and about $122–123 billion for Q4 by carrying forward roughly the Q2-to-Q3 sequential growth pace. | Approximately $417B: start with reported Q1 revenue of $75.25B and the $86.3B Q2 estimate, carry the approximately 14.7% sequential increase into Q3 and Q4, then apply SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 upside to the resulting H2 run-rate.\\\\n2026-08-27 5138 5139 Using reported Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion and Q2 revenue of $96.2 billion, plus Q3 guidance of $108 billion, carrying Q3's approximately 12.3% sequential growth over Q2 implies Q4 revenue of about $121 billion. The resulting FY2027 total is approximately $407 billion. | Approximately $417 billion: the $372 billion reference less Q1 actual revenue of $75.25 billion and the Q2 estimate of $85.8 billion implies about $211 billion of H2 estimates; applying SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 outperformance forecast gives about $253 billion for H2. Adding Q1 actual revenue and Q2 actual revenue of $89 billion yields about $417 billion. The $108 billion Q3 total-revenue guide, applied to the recent roughly 92.5% Data Center share, implies about $100 billion of Q3 Data Center revenue, leaving the forecast dependent on a strong Q4.\\\\n2026-08-28 5471 5473 About $407 billion: $81.6 billion Q1 + $96.2 billion Q2 + $108 billion Q3 guidance, plus an implied Q4 of about $121.3 billion by carrying forward the roughly 12.3% sequential growth from Q2 to guided Q3. | Approximately $419 billion for FY2027: $164.25 billion in the first half, about $100 billion in Q3 from the $108 billion total-revenue guide and recent segment mix, and roughly $112 billion in Q4 if Q3 sequential growth carries forward. Applying SemiAnalysis’s 20% second-half outperformance forecast to that roughly $212 billion baseline implies about $254 billion in the second half and about $418 billion for the year.\\\\n2026-08-29 5602 5598 About $407.1 billion: Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion plus Q2 revenue of $96.2 billion and Q3 guidance of $108 billion, with Q4 estimated at about $121.3 billion by carrying forward the roughly 12.3% sequential growth from Q2 to guided Q3. This is rung 2, at least $400 billion but less than $450 billion. | Approximately $422 billion: $164.25 billion in Q1–Q2, about $100 billion in Q3 using the $108 billion total-revenue guide and recent Data Center mix, and a roughly $115 billion Q4 estimate reflecting management's stated Q4 reacceleration. Applying SemiAnalysis's 20% second-half outperformance forecast to the roughly $215 billion baseline second half gives about $258 billion for H2 and about $422 billion for FY2027 overall.\\\\n2026-08-30 5736 5752 About $407.1 billion: Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion plus Q2 revenue of $96.2 billion, Q3 guidance of $108 billion, and an estimated Q4 of about $121.3 billion by carrying forward the roughly 12.3% sequential growth indicated for Q3. | Approximately $422 billion for FY2027: $164.25 billion actual in Q1–Q2, about $99.9 billion in Q3 from the $108 billion total-revenue guide at the recent 92.5% Data Center mix, and an estimated $115 billion in Q4; applying SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 outperformance forecast to the roughly $215 billion H2 baseline yields about $258 billion for H2.\\\\n2026-08-31 5965 5967 About $407.1 billion: $81.6 billion Q1 + $96.2 billion Q2 + $108 billion Q3 guidance, with Q4 estimated at about $121.3 billion by carrying forward the roughly 12.3% sequential growth implied by Q2 to Q3. | Approximately $422 billion: $164.25 billion in Q1–Q2 plus about $258 billion in H2, applying SemiAnalysis's 20% outperformance forecast to an approximately $215 billion H2 analyst baseline. The H2 baseline is consistent with about $99.9 billion in Q3 from the $108 billion total-revenue guide at a 92.5% Data Center mix and roughly $115 billion in Q4.\\\\n2026-09-01 6189 6195 Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion plus Q2 revenue of $96.2 billion plus Q3 guidance of $108.0 billion, with Q4 estimated by carrying forward Q3's approximately 12.3% sequential growth ($108.0 billion × $108.0 billion / $96.2 billion ≈ $121.3 billion), implies FY2027 revenue of about $407.1 billion. | Approximately $422 billion for FY2027: $164.25 billion from Q1–Q2 plus an implied roughly $99.9 billion in Q3 and the carried roughly $115 billion Q4 estimate gives an H2 baseline near $215 billion; applying SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 outperformance estimate yields about $422 billion for the year.\\\\n2026-09-02 6219 6218 FY2027 revenue of about $407.1 billion: $81.6 billion reported in Q1, $96.2 billion reported in Q2, $108.0 billion guided for Q3, and approximately $121.3 billion for Q4 if Q3's roughly 12.3% sequential growth carries forward. | About $422 billion for FY2027: $164.25 billion reported in Q1–Q2, about $99.9 billion implied for Q3 from the $108 billion total-revenue guide at the latest 92.5% Data Center mix, and the carried Q4 baseline of about $115 billion make an H2 analyst baseline near $215 billion. Applying SemiAnalysis's estimate that H2 Data Center revenue will exceed analyst estimates by 20% gives about $258 billion for H2 and roughly $422 billion for FY2027.\\\\n2026-09-03 6392 6405 Q1 $81.6 billion + Q2 $96.2 billion + Q3 guided midpoint $108.0 billion + implied Q4 about $121.3 billion = approximately $407.1 billion. Q4 is derived by carrying forward the Q2-to-Q3 sequential growth rate of about 12.3%. | About $422 billion: Q1 and Q2 total $164.25 billion; Q3 is estimated at about $99.9 billion by applying the reported 92.5% Q2 Data Center mix to the $108 billion total-revenue outlook; with the carried Q4 baseline of about $115 billion, H2 is about $215 billion. Applying SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 upside to estimates gives roughly $258 billion for H2 and $422 billion for FY2027.\\\\n2026-09-04 6590 6599 About $407.1 billion: $81.6 billion Q1 plus $96.2 billion Q2 plus $108 billion Q3 guidance, with Q4 estimated at about $121.3 billion by carrying forward the roughly 12.3% Q2-to-Q3 sequential growth rate. | About $422 billion for FY2027: $164.25 billion actual in Q1–Q2, about $99.9 billion implied for Q3 from the $108 billion total-revenue guide at a 92.5% Data Center mix, and a carried Q4 baseline of about $115 billion yield an H2 baseline near $215 billion. Applying SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 outperformance estimate gives roughly $258 billion for H2 and about $422 billion for the year.\\\\n2026-09-05 6715 6702 About $407.1 billion: reported Q1 and Q2 revenue total $177.8 billion; adding Q3 guidance of $108 billion and carrying the Q2-to-Q3 sequential growth rate (about 12.3%) into Q4 implies about $121.3 billion. The resulting FY2027 total is approximately $407.1 billion. | About $422 billion for FY2027: $164.25 billion of Q1–Q2 actuals, approximately $99.9 billion for Q3 from the $108 billion total-revenue guidance at a 92.5% Data Center mix, and a carried Q4 baseline of about $115 billion produce a roughly $215 billion H2 baseline; SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 upside forecast implies about $258 billion for H2.\\\\n2026-09-07 6966 6975 Approximately $407 billion: FY2027 Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion plus Q2's $96.2 billion plus Q3 guidance of $108.0 billion totals $285.8 billion; carrying Q3's roughly 12.3% sequential growth forward implies Q4 of about $121.3 billion. The total is about $407.1 billion, within rung 2. | About $414 billion: Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue total $164.25 billion; Q3 is estimated at about $100 billion by applying the latest reported 92.5% Data Center mix to the $108 billion total-revenue guide. The $372 billion reference implies about $208 billion in H2; SemiAnalysis's 20% H2 upside implies about $249 billion in H2 and approximately $414 billion for FY2027.\\\\n2026-09-08 7058 7072 About $407 billion: Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion plus Q2 revenue of $96.2 billion plus Q3 midpoint guidance of $108 billion, with Q4 estimated at about $121.3 billion by carrying forward Q3's 12.3% sequential growth once. This is an extrapolation rather than Q4 guidance, and it falls in rung 2. | About $414 billion: Q1 and Q2 actual Data Center revenue sum to $164.25 billion; the H2 analyst baseline of about $208 billion, derived from the carried FY2027 reference, rises to roughly $249 billion under SemiAnalysis’s 20% H2 upside forecast. The $108 billion Q3 total-revenue guide and latest Data Center mix imply roughly $100 billion for Q3, consistent with—not additional to—that H2 estimate.\\\\n2026-09-09 7169 7178 About $407 billion: $81.6 billion Q1 plus $96.2 billion Q2, plus the $108 billion Q3 midpoint, plus an estimated $121.3 billion Q4 by carrying forward the 12.3% sequential growth implied by Q3 guidance. | About $413–414 billion: Q1–Q2 total $164.25 billion; Q3 is roughly $100 billion from the $108 billion total-revenue guide at the latest 92.5% Data Center mix; the carried H2 baseline of about $208 billion, raised 20% by SemiAnalysis, is about $249–250 billion. The Q3 estimate is included within H2, not added again.\\\\n2026-09-10 7396 7400 About $407.1 billion: $81.6 billion in Q1 plus $96.2 billion in Q2 plus the $108 billion Q3 guide, then approximately $121.3 billion for Q4 by carrying forward the roughly 12.3% sequential growth implied by the Q3 midpoint. | About $413–414 billion: $164.25 billion of reported FY2027 H1 Data Center revenue plus approximately $249–250 billion implied for H2 by the prior roughly $208 billion baseline and SemiAnalysis's 20% upside estimate. The approximately $99.9 billion Q3 calculation is included within H2, not added separately.\\\\n2026-09-11 7568 7562 About $407.1 billion: $81.6 billion (Q1) + $96.2 billion (Q2) + $108 billion (Q3 guidance) + approximately $121.3 billion for Q4, carrying forward the roughly 12.3% sequential growth implied by Q2-to-Q3 guidance. | About $414 billion: $75.25 billion in Q1 plus $89.0 billion in Q2 equals $164.25 billion for H1; applying SemiAnalysis's 20% uplift to the carried-forward roughly $208 billion H2 baseline implies about $249.6 billion in H2, or about $413.9 billion for FY2027.\\\\n2026-09-12 7684 7670 About $407.1 billion: $81.6 billion Q1 + $96.2 billion Q2 + $108.0 billion Q3 guidance midpoint + approximately $121.3 billion for Q4, carrying forward the 12.3% sequential growth implied from Q2 to Q3. | Approximately $414 billion: Q1 plus Q2 Data Center revenue is $164.25 billion; Q3 is estimated at about $99.9 billion from the $108 billion company revenue guide and the latest 92.5% Data Center mix. The prior H2 baseline of about $208 billion, raised 20% in line with SemiAnalysis’s H2 estimate, implies about $249.6 billion for H2 and roughly $414 billion for the year.\\\\n2026-09-13 7776 7770 About $407.1 billion: $81.6 billion (Q1) + $96.2 billion (Q2) + $108 billion (Q3 guidance midpoint) + about $121.3 billion for Q4, carrying forward the 12.3% sequential growth implied by Q2-to-Q3 guidance. This is rung 2. | About $414 billion: $164.25 billion from Q1 and Q2 plus approximately $249.6 billion for H2, using the carried $208 billion H2 analyst baseline increased 20% by SemiAnalysis. The Q3 guide and current Data Center mix imply about $100 billion for Q3, which is part of H2, not an additional amount.\\\\n2026-09-14 7934 7939 About $407.1 billion: $81.6 billion in Q1, $96.2 billion in Q2, and $108 billion at the Q3 guidance midpoint, plus an estimated $121.3 billion in Q4 by extending the roughly 12.3% Q2-to-Q3 sequential growth rate. This is above $400 billion and below $450 billion. | Approximately $414 billion: FY2027 Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue total about $164.25 billion; the $108 billion Q3 total-revenue guide implies about $100 billion of Data Center revenue at the latest reported mix. Carrying forward the prior H2 baseline of about $208 billion and applying SemiAnalysis’s 20% above-estimates forecast gives about $249.6 billion for H2, including Q3, and about $414 billion for FY2027.\\\\n2026-09-17 8312 8319 Using Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion and Q2 revenue of $96.2 billion, estimate Q3 at about $113.6 billion by applying the reported 3.1% average beat to the $110.16 billion high end of the $108 billion guidance. Carrying forward the roughly 12.3% sequential growth implied by Q2-to-Q3 guidance gives Q4 of about $127.6 billion, or approximately $419 billion for FY2027. | About $382 billion: Q1 and Q2 total approximately $164.25 billion; applying the recent 92.5% Data Center mix to the $108 billion Q3 total-revenue guide implies about $99.9 billion for Q3; carrying that run rate forward with Q4 hyperscale reacceleration implies roughly $115–120 billion for Q4.\\\\n3 32 25\\\\n2026-08-19 4048 4033 Q1 actual revenue of $81.6 billion, Q2 guidance of $91 billion, the Q3 estimate of $103.1 billion, and about 12% sequential growth into Q4 imply a baseline around $391–$392 billion. Applying the carried estimate of 20% upside to second-half Data Center compute adds roughly $40 billion, implying total FY2027 revenue around $431–$433 billion. | $361 billion for FY2027: Morningstar explicitly estimates that figure, citing FY2026 data-center revenue of $194 billion and 86% annual growth. The estimate sits exactly at rung 2’s lower boundary and below rung 1’s $400 billion threshold.\\\\n2026-08-20 4101 4100 Roughly $434–$437 billion: carry forward the prior $391–$392 billion quarterly baseline plus about $40 billion from the estimated 20% second-half Data Center compute upside, then add about $3–$4 billion for BofA’s $94–$95 billion Q2 forecast versus the $91 billion guide midpoint. The higher Q3 expectation is not added separately because it overlaps the second-half tracking uplift. | Around $361 billion with an unquantified modest upward tilt: the China shipment reports add potential revenue, but give no sales value from which to calculate a larger increment. That remains below the $400 billion rung-1 threshold.\\\\n2026-08-21 4186 4180 Approximately $432–436 billion: applying the roughly $40 billion implied second-half Data Center compute upside from SemiAnalysis to the roughly $392 billion annual reference, with BofA's Q2 estimate adding about $3–4 billion versus guidance, while avoiding a separate overlapping Q3 addition. | Around the high-$300 billions, anchored on Morningstar’s $361 billion estimate with some upside from reported China shipments and demand evidence. The supplied evidence does not quantify an FY2027 increase of at least $39 billion, so the implied figure remains below $400 billion.\\\\n2026-08-22 4222 4216 About $432–436 billion: apply SemiAnalysis's 20% upside to second-half FY2027 Data Center compute, implying roughly $40 billion above the $392 billion consensus, then include about $3–4 billion for BofA's $94–95 billion Q2 forecast versus the roughly $91 billion guide/consensus. This is a forecast, not an established result, and sits just above the $431.2 billion rung-1 boundary. | About $372 billion: apply the reported 92% Q1 FY2027 year-over-year growth rate to the cited $194 billion FY2026 revenue base ($194B × 1.92).\\\\n2026-08-23 4298 4288 About $438–440 billion: start from the $392 billion FY2027 estimate, add roughly $40 billion implied by SemiAnalysis’s 20% second-half Data Center compute upside, and allow about $6–8 billion for BofA’s Q2 and following-quarter estimates above the respective consensus figures. | About $372 billion for FY2027: carry the reported 92% year-over-year Q1 FY2027 growth forward across the $194 billion FY2026 base ($194 billion × 1.92).\\\\n2026-08-24 4510 4507 Approximately $438–440 billion: the Q1 reported revenue of $81.6 billion and Q2 guide of $91 billion anchor the run-rate; above-consensus Q2/Q3 outlooks and the roughly $40 billion implied upside from SemiAnalysis’s 20%-above-consensus second-half Data Center compute projection lift the estimate above $431.2 billion. | Carrying the reported 92% Q1 FY2027 year-over-year growth forward from the cited $194 billion FY2026 data-center revenue implies approximately $372 billion for FY2027. The Q2 consensus of $85.14 billion, up about 107% year over year, is consistent with strong growth but does not establish an estimate above $400 billion.\\\\n2026-08-25 4665 4667 About $436 billion: start from the $396 billion FY2027 estimate and carry forward the existing roughly $40 billion uplift implied by SemiAnalysis's forecast that second-half FY2027 Data Center compute revenue will exceed consensus by 20% (e60, e1116). | Approximately $387 billion: applying an indicative 99.5% FY2027 growth rate—the midpoint of reported Q1 growth of 92% and the Q2 consensus growth estimate of 107%—to the cited $194 billion FY2026 base.\\\\n2026-09-01 6457 6454 First-half revenue was $177.837 billion; the $108 billion Q3 guide implies roughly 89% year-over-year growth. Carrying that growth into Q4, whose FY2026 comparison is about $68.1 billion ($215.9 billion FY2026 revenue less $90.805 billion first-half revenue and $57.01 billion FY2026 Q3 revenue), implies roughly $129 billion for Q4 and about $415 billion for FY2027. | About $374–379 billion: Q1 and Q2 sum to about $164.2 billion; Q3 is estimated at about $99.9 billion by applying Q2’s 92.5% Data Center mix to management’s $108 billion total-revenue guide; the carried Q4 estimate is about $110–115 billion with hyperscale growth reaccelerating.\\\\n2026-09-12 8046 8045 The first-half reported revenue of $177.837 billion, plus Q3 guidance of $108 billion and a 12% sequential carry into Q4, implies about $406.8 billion before the SemiAnalysis forecast of second-half data-center compute revenue 20% above consensus. Applying a discounted uplift only to that portion supports an approximate FY2027 outcome of $435 billion. | About $376 billion: Q1 and Q2 total about $164.2 billion; the roughly $108 billion Q3 total-revenue outlook at the 92.5% Data Center mix implies about $99.9 billion; carrying the guided 12.3% sequential growth forward implies roughly $112 billion in Q4.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r45.stream:89:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_46\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,json,pathlib,re,collections,decimal\\\\nD=decimal.Decimal\\\\ndef db(i,name='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''views'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):\\\\n c=sqlite3.connect((pathlib.Path(f'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-{i}/prod'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')/(name+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.sqlite'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')).resolve().as_uri()+'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''?mode=ro'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',uri=True)\\\\n c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\\\\n return c\\\\ndef req(a,j):\\\\n c=a.execute('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''select * from model_calls where call_id=?'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',(j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''call_id'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''],)).fetchone()\\\\n assert c and c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']==j['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''request_sha256'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] and c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''purpose'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']=='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''judge'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',dict(j)\\\\n d=json.loads(c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''request_json'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''])\\\\n return d,json.loads(c['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''answer_json'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''])\\\\nEVID=re.compile(r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\"'^- (e'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\[.*?(?=\\\\\\\"'^- e'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+ \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\[|\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Z)'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',re.M|re.S)\\\\ndef evidence(t):\\\\n b=t.split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''[Evidence in view under this thesis, '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[0]\\\\n m=dict((x.group(1),x.group(0).strip()) for x in EVID.finditer(b))\\\\n assert len(m)==int(b.split()[0]),(len(m),b[:20])\\\\n return m\\\\ndef user(d):\\\\n return next(m['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''content'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] for m in d['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''messages'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] if m['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''role'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']=='\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''user'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')\\\\nUNIT=r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''(?:trillion(?:s)?|billions?|millions?|bn|mm|[BTM]|%|percent(?:age points?)?)'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\nNUM=r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+(?:,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d{3})*(?:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\d+)?'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\nFIG=re.compile(rf'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''(?<\\\\\\\"'!['\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\w.])(?P<sign>[+−-])?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'$?'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*(?P<lo>{NUM})(?:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*[-–—]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'$?'\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*(?P<hi>{NUM}))?\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\s*(?P<unit>{UNIT})(?\\\\\\\"'![a-zA-Z0-9])'\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',re.I)\\\\nMULT={'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''trillion'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''trillions'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''t'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1000,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''billion'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''billions'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''bn'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''b'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':1,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''million'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''millions'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''mm'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''),'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''m'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'':D('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''.001'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')}\\\\ndef figures(t,unit):\\\\n out=[]\\\\n for m in FIG.finditer(t or '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):\\\\n  u=m['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''unit'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''].lower()\\\\n  if (u in MULT)\\\\\\\"'!=(unit=='\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):continue\\\\n  mult=MULT.get(u,1)\\\\n  if m['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''sign'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] in ('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''-'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''−'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):mult=-mult\\\\n  for g in ('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''lo'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''hi'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):\\\\n   if m[g]:out.append(D(m[g].replace('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''))*mult)\\\\n return out\\\\ndef snippets(ed):\\\\n return [re.split(r'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    (?:It replaces|Opinion, not verified:)'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',b,1)[0].split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[1] for b in ed.values()]\\\\ndef prior_text(t):\\\\n return t.split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''[Previous conclusion'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[1].split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nAnswer per'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[0].split('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''] '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',1)[1]\\\\ndef tag(x,pattern): return bool(re.search(pattern,x or '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',re.I))\\\\ndef record(i):\\\\n v=db(i);a=db(i,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''archive'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'')\\\\n return (v,a,v.execute(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"select j.*,k.unit from judgements j join view_keys k using(view_id) where k.unit in ('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''USD'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''percent'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'') order by judgement_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"))\\\\nv,a,_=record(2)\\\\nfor call,ids in [(8734,['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''e2620'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''e2889'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''e3474'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''e3934'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''e4648'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''e4729'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']),(8595,['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''e1786'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''e1926'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''e2535'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'']),(8730,['\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''e3108'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''e4900'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''])]:\\\\n j=v.execute('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''select * from judgements where call_id=?'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',(call,)).fetchone();d,raw=req(a,j);ed=evidence(user(d))\\\\n for id in ids:print(call,id,ed.get(id,'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''ABSENT'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''))\\\\nfor id in ('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''e3108'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''e2532'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'','\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''e2889'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''):\\\\n row=v.execute('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\''select * from evidence where evidence_id=?'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\'',(id,)).fetchone()\\\\n for c in a.execute(\\\\\\\