{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONPATH=src python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,glob\nfrom hivemind import service\nfor f,vid,jid in [('\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite'\\\\'','\\\\''v10'\\\\'',865),('\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-3/prod/views.sqlite'\\\\'','\\\\''v36'\\\\'',799)]:\n c=sqlite3.connect('\\\\''file:'\\\\''+f+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True);c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n j=c.execute('\\\\''select * from judgements where judgement_id=?'\\\\'',(jid,)).fetchone()\n print(f,vid,j['\\\\''publication_day'\\\\''],j['\\\\''why_changed'\\\\''],j['\\\\''theme_pushes_json'\\\\''])\n for i in ('\\\\''v6'\\\\'','\\\\''v7'\\\\''):\n  s=service.view(c,i,j['\\\\''publication_day'\\\\'']);print(i,s['\\\\''question'\\\\''],s['\\\\''state'\\\\'']['\\\\''position'\\\\''],s['\\\\''state'\\\\'']['\\\\''condition'\\\\''])\n print([x['\\\\''why_changed'\\\\''] for x in service.history(c,vid,j['\\\\''publication_day'\\\\''],j['\\\\''publication_day'\\\\''])['\\\\''judgements'\\\\'']])\n if vid=='\\\\''v10'\\\\'':\n  print('\\\\''v8 hist changes'\\\\'',len(service.history(c,'\\\\''v8'\\\\'')['\\\\''changes'\\\\'']),'\\\\''evidence'\\\\'',len(service.evidence(c,'\\\\''v8'\\\\'')))\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"PYTHONPATH=src python3 -B -c 'import sqlite3,glob\nfrom hivemind import service\nfor f,vid,jid in [('\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite'\\\\'','\\\\''v10'\\\\'',865),('\\\\''poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-3/prod/views.sqlite'\\\\'','\\\\''v36'\\\\'',799)]:\n c=sqlite3.connect('\\\\''file:'\\\\''+f+'\\\\''?mode=ro&immutable=1'\\\\'',uri=True);c.row_factory=sqlite3.Row\n j=c.execute('\\\\''select * from judgements where judgement_id=?'\\\\'',(jid,)).fetchone()\n print(f,vid,j['\\\\''publication_day'\\\\''],j['\\\\''why_changed'\\\\''],j['\\\\''theme_pushes_json'\\\\''])\n for i in ('\\\\''v6'\\\\'','\\\\''v7'\\\\''):\n  s=service.view(c,i,j['\\\\''publication_day'\\\\'']);print(i,s['\\\\''question'\\\\''],s['\\\\''state'\\\\'']['\\\\''position'\\\\''],s['\\\\''state'\\\\'']['\\\\''condition'\\\\''])\n print([x['\\\\''why_changed'\\\\''] for x in service.history(c,vid,j['\\\\''publication_day'\\\\''],j['\\\\''publication_day'\\\\''])['\\\\''judgements'\\\\'']])\n if vid=='\\\\''v10'\\\\'':\n  print('\\\\''v8 hist changes'\\\\'',len(service.history(c,'\\\\''v8'\\\\'')['\\\\''changes'\\\\'']),'\\\\''evidence'\\\\'',len(service.evidence(c,'\\\\''v8'\\\\'')))\n'\"","aggregated_output":"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod/views.sqlite v10 2026-08-28 The rung remains 1 and no new transaction terms are shown. The updated AI-capex themes now put 2026 hyperscaler data-center capex at rung 4 and 2027 capex at rung 4, strengthening the contextual support for Firmus financing and changing the supporting outlook, without changing the implied completion date. [{\"view_id\": \"v6\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"view_id\": \"v7\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}]\nv6 How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2026? 4 Combined spending is at least $700 billion and less than $800 billion.\nv7 How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data center capital expenditures in calendar 2027? 4 Combined spending is at least $1.1 trillion and less than $1.2 trillion.\n['The rung remains 1 and no new transaction terms are shown. The updated AI-capex themes now put 2026 hyperscaler data-center capex at rung 4 and 2027 capex at rung 4, strengthening the contextual support for Firmus financing and changing the supporting outlook, without changing the implied completion date.']\nv8 hist changes 9 evidence 1284\npoc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-3/prod/views.sqlite v36 2026-08-25 The rung remains Yes, and the shipment-testing evidence is unchanged. The updated 2027 AI-capex theme now points to spending around $1 trillion, refreshing and strengthening the demand support for the same forecast without supplying a shipment date. [{\"view_id\": \"v6\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}, {\"view_id\": \"v7\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}]\nv6 How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026? 4 Combined spending is at least $700 billion and below $800 billion.\nv7 How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027? 3 Combined spending is at least $900 billion and below $1.1 trillion.\n['The rung remains Yes, and the shipment-testing evidence is unchanged. The updated 2027 AI-capex theme now points to spending around $1 trillion, refreshing and strengthening the demand support for the same forecast without supplying a shipment date.']\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers | rg '72|FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE'; nl -ba poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js | tail -15; nl -ba poc/config/poc-v118-idea.json | tail -11; nl -ba src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '203,213p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/idea.py | sed -n '211,223p'; ls poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod | head -50; rg -n 'file_server|http.server|poc/mock/data|mock/index.html|/library' README.md poc/ui/README.md | head -40\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers | rg '72|FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE'; nl -ba poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js | tail -15; nl -ba poc/config/poc-v118-idea.json | tail -11; nl -ba src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '203,213p'; nl -ba src/hivemind/idea.py | sed -n '211,223p'; ls poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-1/prod | head -50; rg -n 'file_server|http.server|poc/mock/data|mock/index.html|/library' README.md poc/ui/README.md | head -40\"","aggregated_output":"docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72b.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72b.stream\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round72b-brief.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r72.stream\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round72-brief.md\n   280\t        composer.destroy();\n   281\t      },\n   282\t      { once: true },\n   283\t    );\n   284\t    showLibrary();\n   285\t    updateSendState();\n   286\t    loadLibrary();\n   287\t  } catch (error) {\n   288\t    const message = document.createElement('p');\n   289\t    message.className = 'ui-error';\n   290\t    message.setAttribute('role', 'alert');\n   291\t    message.textContent = `Cannot load the thesis data: ${error.message}`;\n   292\t    libraryRoot.append(message);\n   293\t  }\n   294\t}\n    88\t    \"prompt_version\": \"idea-v7\",\n    89\t    \"reasoning_effort\": \"none\",\n    90\t    \"max_output_tokens\": 4000\n    91\t  },\n    92\t  \"idea_summary\": {\n    93\t    \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    94\t    \"prompt_version\": \"idea-summary-v8\",\n    95\t    \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    96\t    \"max_output_tokens\": 4000\n    97\t  }\n    98\t}\n   203\t    if themes:\n   204\t        lines.append(f'\\n[Themes in force, {len(themes)}]')\n   205\t        for theme in themes:\n   206\t            tv, state = theme['view'], theme['state']\n   207\t            mark = f'; {UPDATED_MARK}' if theme['updated'] else ''\n   208\t            lines.append(f'- {theme[\"view_id\"]} ({tv[\"object_id\"]}, due {tv[\"due_day\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"]} {theme[\"rung_label\"]}; '\n   209\t                         f'judged {state[\"publication_day\"]}{mark}; reasons: {(state[\"reasons\"] or \"\")[:THEME_REASONS_CHARS]}')\n   210\t    if last:\n   211\t        lines.append(f'\\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung {last[\"rung\"]}; reasons: {last[\"reasons\"][:800]}')\n   212\t    else:\n   213\t        lines.append('\\n[Previous conclusion] none: this is the first judgement, so changed must be true.')\n   211\t        for r in (a, b):\n   212\t            if r is not None and r['view_id'] not in seen:\n   213\t                seen.add(r['view_id'])\n   214\t                out.append(r)\n   215\t    return out[:limit]\n   216\t\n   217\t\n   218\tdef read_idea(ledger, index, items, archive, cfg, text, as_of=None, k=10, aliases=None, semantic=True, transport=None, bundles=True, embed=search.openai_embeddings, on_progress=None):\n   219\t    \"\"\"The idea card: idea, what the idea's own search found, the reading (typed parts, the candidates each got, the\n   220\t    views each maps to, the summary, the claim), the related views from the dependency graph, the evaluation, every\n   221\t    view's bundle, the days, the trace of searches, and all call costs. No recorded view → no model call.\"\"\"\n   222\t    text = (text or '').strip()\n   223\t    if not text:\narchive.sqlite\nmanifests\nreplay.log\nviews.sqlite\nREADME.md:13:| Browse the included demo | [Thesis Library and Explore Ideas](poc/mock/index.html); serve it locally using the command below |\nREADME.md:29:python3 -m http.server 8000 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory \"$repo\"\nREADME.md:32:Open <http://127.0.0.1:8000/poc/mock/index.html> for the app, or <http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs/system-design.html> for the design. Stop the page server with Ctrl-C. The included standalone page can browse its embedded snapshot without the API; submitting an Idea needs the service below.\nREADME.md:107:| `scripts/mock_build.py` | `--ledger` and `--items` defaults, then `python3 scripts/mock_build.py` rebuilds `poc/mock/index.html` |\nREADME.md:133:The app calls `http://127.0.0.1:8788`; its host may override this with `<body data-api=\"…\">`. `/library` returns the dated snapshot. `--views` and `--items` select other source databases; `--index`, `--archive` and `--config` select derived storage and configuration. Stop only the API instance you started:\nREADME.md:188:Install pytest in your Python environment to run the Python tests. `mock_build.py` reads the local databases and embeds the dated market snapshot into `poc/mock/index.html`; it makes no model calls. `npm --prefix poc/ui run build` builds component assets only. The [frontend guide](poc/ui/README.md) covers the frontend in detail.\npoc/ui/README.md:11:Adapt existing bundles once with `fromBundles`. Cards do not rename fields or infer scores. `GET /library` or MCP `thesis_library` returns the full dated library. `createLibrary(root, {dataset})` renders it; its lifecycle supports `setDataset`, `getDay` and `destroy`. `coverage: selection` bundles include only loaded group members. Canonical v1 payloads remain readable through the compatibility boundary.\npoc/ui/README.md:75:`poc/mock/index.template.html` is the page shell. The generated `poc/mock/index.html` embeds CSS, JavaScript and validated data for standalone opening. The default build reads `served-2026-10-28-v34-nvda-3m-through-0828/views.sqlite` and `items-nvda-2026-07-01-10-27.sqlite` directly. `--ledger` and `--items` override them; `--data` selects an explicit legacy JSON export. Building does not modify source data or translation caches. esbuild, Ajv, ESLint and Prettier are build/development tools; the browser uses the generated standalone validator.\npoc/ui/README.md:81:`node poc/ui/verify-library.mjs` creates `poc/ui/dist/library-check.html` to verify invalid/empty snapshots, a narrower date span, teardown and unique DOM IDs in a real browser.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
