{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"agent_message","text":"1. **Revision 2 leaves a confirmed forecast leak through Yes/No answers.** In `old-3`, the August 25 explanation for a shipment question (`v36`, judgement 799) says that the 2027 spending forecast is “around $1 trillion.” In `old-1`, the August 28 explanation for the Firmus investment (`v10`, judgement 865) gives the selected band for **both** the 2026 and 2027 spending questions. I read both explanations through `service.history()`. The judge receives related questions’ selected bands and reasons, and history returns the resulting text. Revision 2 promises to return Yes/No records exactly as they are today. Those requirements conflict on stored data. Preserve the Yes/No outcome, and specify how release readers handle explanations that disclose another question’s forecast. Use these two records as acceptance cases. [Design:95](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:95) · [judging.py:208](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:208) · [service.py:263](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:263) · [bundle.py:120](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/bundle.py:120)\n\n2. **Identity works on the four stores if the Yes/No test uses the stored vocabulary.** I checked every question. The three comparison stores split into **19 number / 28 event**, **17 / 26**, and **18 / 31**. All 85 event questions have an `event` or `policy_event` measure. In the sealed ledger, 43 of 94 questions parse as money, 21 further number questions are safely withheld by the fallback, and 30 are Yes/No. All 30 use `是` and `否`. A literal English test would withhold all 30 incorrectly. Specify exactly two labels, canonicalized with the existing vocabulary, in either order. With that reading I found no wrong show-or-withhold result in the four stores. I also verified both round-72 counterexamples directly. Sealed revenue `v3` parses from its conditions. Xbox `v37` has the `growth_rate` measure and bounds around zero, but its two answers are explicitly Yes and No. [Design:30](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:30) · [identity.py:10](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/identity.py:10) · [vocabulary.py:24](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/vocabulary.py:24) · [test_service.py:90](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_service.py:90) · [test_service.py:119](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_service.py:119) · [Xbox store manifest:20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-10-25-english/data-manifest.md:20)\n\n3. **The ambiguity rule still has a gap for a record with a key.** Section 2 limits its fallback to records with *no key*. The opening check accepts a ladder with every bound null. I cleared only the bounds on an in-memory copy of `old-1/v8` and ran its five original English conditions through the service parser. All five were refused. The `segment_revenue` key still exists, so this supported shape reaches no stated outcome. Withhold and list every unresolved record, whether or not it has a key. That closes the gap without extending the money parser to every language and unit. [Design:34](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:34) · [extraction.py:493](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:493) · [service.py:422](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:422) · [service.py:499](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:499)\n\n4. **The idea card has a second path that restores hidden bands.** Revision 2 covers candidate summaries, related questions, evaluation, and `/ideas` with either bundle setting. But the configured idea-summary version reads the ladder directly from storage when building its answer format, and the summary call adds it to the input again. I passed `v8` through that helper with its judgement removed. It added back “at least $400 billion” and “less than $250 billion.” Exclude withheld ladders from both reads and inspect the actual summary request in the test. A clean `judged` field alone does not establish that the idea prose is clean. [Design:69](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:69) · [poc-v118-idea.json:94](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/config/poc-v118-idea.json:94) · [idea.py:350](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:350) · [idea_composite.py:255](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea_composite.py:255) · [idea_composite.py:281](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea_composite.py:281)\n\n5. **The approved screen, `claim_position`, search ranking, processing dates, closing text, and fixed setting are addressed in the design.** The question page keeps the question, its sources and “Forecast unavailable,” including amounts a source actually quoted. Evaluation returns only the marker. Assessment counts and dates are omitted, and a closing record can say “closed” without its final band. Search ranks possible outcomes without reading the selected one. The design also identifies the browser’s separate assessment-date sort and fixes the release setting at `withheld`. These provisions match Alex’s decision and the cited readers. [D756:11833](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11833) · [Design:46](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:46) · [Design:65](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:65) · [Design:81](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:81) · [search.py:275](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/search.py:275) · [library.js:32](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/model/library.js:32) · [service.py:553](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:553)\n\n6. **The main exports are named, but a clean HTML file can reload unrestricted data.** The page opens its embedded snapshot, then automatically fetches `/library` from an API that defaults to `127.0.0.1:8788`. It replaces the snapshot after checking only that the response is a complete library. The idea page fetches its bundles from the same address. Since revision 2 explicitly leaves the existing POC setting open, a release HTML file opened beside that POC can show its forecasts. Bind the release page to the release service or have it refuse unrestricted responses. Apply the same content check to prepared JSON before embedding it. The static builder also embeds `--composite-trials` separately from the main dataset, and the translated `data.en.json` export retains judgement prose. Keep those inputs outside the release package unless checked. [Design:72](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:72) · [bootstrap.js:20](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:20) · [bootstrap.js:193](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:193) · [bootstrap.js:254](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:254) · [mock_build.py:61](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_build.py:61) · [mock_translate.py:114](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/mock_translate.py:114)\n\n7. **The acceptance check selects the right question, but cannot prove the closing case as written.** `old-1/v8` has 75 judgements, 69 rows marked changed, and 9 actual moves between bands. Its only stored switch is `open=1, reason=created`. Round 72 generated the closing sentence by calling the formatter. There is no closing sentence on this question for the release page to hide. Keep `v8` for the page and same-sources check. Exercise closure on a temporary copy with a real stored closing switch, and first verify that the unrestricted response exposes its final band. For the $0 idea check, use a recorded or test transport and inspect the composed request as well as the delivered card. [Design:109](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/FORECAST-UNAVAILABLE-DESIGN.md:109) · [pull.py:11](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/pull.py:11) · [service.py:280](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:280) · [service.py:356](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/service.py:356) · [idea.py:218](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/idea.py:218)\n\n**Verdict — not ready.** An unchanged Yes/No explanation already discloses a number forecast in the stored data. Revision 2 needs to resolve that conflict and close the idea, identity, and export gaps before Alex opens release work. This review was read-only and cost $0."}}
